garding issue of Greater Mumbai pertaining to \nCRZ Notification 2011 (MCGM), preparation of new development plan for Mumbai \nincluding redevelopment of dilapidated, cessed and unsafe buildings;  \n(b) if so, the details in this regard;  \n(c) the present status of the said proposals; and  \n(d) the time by which the said proposals are likely to be finalised along with the reasons for \ndelay in this regard? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  FOR ENVIRONMENT, FOREST \nAND CLIMATE CHANGE \n  \n(SHRI ANIL MADHAV DAVE) \n \n \n(a) No proposal has been received in  the Ministry  from Government of Maharashtra seeking \nenvironmental clearance under Coastal Regulation Zone (CRZ) Notification, 2011 for new \ndevelopment plan of Mumbai including redevelopment of dilapidated, cessed  and unsafe \nbuildings in CRZ areas of Mumbai.   \n \n (b) to (d) : Does not arise in view of answer at (a) above.  \n \n*** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |460", "t": "Smuggling/Trade of Animals", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OE ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 460 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.07.2016 \n \nSmuggling/Trade of Animals \n \n460. SHRI R. GOPALAKRISHNAN:  \n \nWill the Minster of ENVIRONMENT, FORESTS AND  CLIMATE CHANGE be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a) whether it is a fact that there are hundreds of websites involved in trade of rare animals \nand their body parts; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether the Government is contemplating to bring out guidelines/legislation specifica lly \nto curb smuggling and online trading of animals and their body parts; and \n(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor and the other steps taken/proposed \nto be taken to prevent such illegal acts in the country? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  FOR ENVIRONMENT, FOREST \nAND CLIMATE CHANGE \n  \n(SHRI ANIL MADHAV DAVE) \n \n(a)  & (b)  Several websites are seen advertising sale of rare animals and their parts. \nThe details of various websites advertising rare animals and their parts \ncollated by Wildlife Crime Control Bureau are at Annexure A. \n( c )& (d)  Illegal online smuggling of rare animals and their parts are being \nmonitored under relevant laws existing under Department of Information \nTechnology at both State and Central Government as a part of combating \ncybercrime. \nFollowing steps are being taken by this Ministry through Wildlife Crime \nControl Bureau with limited resources available with it, to prevent such \nillegal acts: \n1. Services of Cyber Crime Specialist on Contractual b asis is being \nutilized to carry out regular cyber patrolling to detect any posts and \noffers over such trade portals on the World Wide Web: \n2. On detection of such offers, details are retrieved of the suspect and the \n\ninformation is passed on to relevant enforc ement agencies for legal \naction: \n3. A meeting of representatives from online trade portals was convened \non 19th May 2016  to discuss issues pertaining to online wildlife trade \nand sensitize them on illegal wildlife trade and to discuss modalities to \nassist Wildlife Crime Control Bureau in case of such detection. \n4. During training and sensitization programme conducted by the \nBureau, the issue of illegal online wildlife trade is being highlighted so \nthat the officials involved in enforcement are abreast of such tr ends \nand taken necessary action. \n**** \n  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure-A \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) AND (b) OF THE LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO . 460 REGARDING “SMUGGLING/TRADE OF \nANIMALS”  BY SHRI R. GOPALAKRISHNAN  FOR REPLY ON 19.07.2016 \n \nLIST OF WEBSITES INVOLVED IN TRADE OF RARE ANIMALS AND THEIR BODY \nPARTS , AS HAS BEEN NOTICED TILL DATE BY WILDLIFE CRIME CONTROL \nBUREAU \n1. Quikr.com  21. Aliexpress.com \n2. Gumtree.com  22. ocala4sale.com \n3. ClickIndia.in  2