e \n12 Bolivia 62 Monaco 112 Venezuela \n13 Brazil 63 Mongolia 113 Vietnam \n14 Cambodia 64 Montenegro 114 Albania \n15 Canada 65 Montserrat 115 Austria \n16 Cayman Island 66 Mozambique 116 Bosnia & Herzegovina \n17 Chile 67 Myanmar 117 Botswana \n18 China 68 Nauru 118 Brunei \n19 China-SAR Hong Kong 69 Netherlands 119 Bulgaria \n20 China- SAR Macau 70 New Zealand 120 Cape Verde \n21 Colombia 71 Nicaragua 121 Comoros \n22 Cook Islands 72 Niue Island 122 Cote d’Ivoire \n23 Costa Rica 73 Norway 123 Croatia \n24  Cuba 74 Oman 124 Czech Republic \n25 Djibouti 75 Palau 125 Denmark \n26 Dominica 76 Palestine 126 Eritrea \n27 Dominican Republic 77 Panama 127 Gabon \n28 East Timor 78 Papua New Guinea 128 Gambia \n29 Ecuador 79 Paraguay 129 G"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |468", "t": "Satellite for Regional Grouping", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n DEPARTMENT OF SPACE \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 468 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON WEDNESDAY, JULY 20, 2016 \n \nSATELLITE FOR REGIONAL GROUPING \n468.  SHRI C.S. PUTTA RAJU: \n Will the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n(a)  whether a meeting of  experts from South Asian Association \nfor Regional Cooperation (SAARC) countries was held last \nyear to finalise modalities for developing a satellite \nexclusively for regional grouping and if so, the details \nthereof; and \n(b)  the time by which the satellite  is likely to be launched and \nthe areas in which it would give information? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF PERSONNEL, PG & \nPENSIONS AND IN THE PRIME MINISTER’S OFFICE \n(DR. JITENDRA SINGH): \n(a) No Madam. The conference on “Satellite for the SAA RC \nregion and Space Technology Applications” held on June \n22, 2015 at New Delhi was intended to familiari se the \nrepresentatives from all member countries of SAARC Region \nabout the satellite configuration and its potential utili sation \nfor the benefit of SAA RC Region. Indian Space Research \nOrganisation (ISRO) is developing a communication satellite \nfor use by South Asian countries. The satellite is now \nnamed as Satellite for South Asia. \n \n\n(b) The proposed satellite is planned to be ready for use by \nSouth Asian countries by first half of 2017. The satellite will \nhave capability to provide services in the areas of \nbroadcast and telecommunication including Disaster \nmanagement, Tele -education & Tele-health, T elevision and \nVery Small Aperture Terminals. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |469", "t": "NSDF", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.469 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20-07-2016 \nNSDF \n†469.  SHRI BHAIRON PRASAD MISHRA: \nWill the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether his Ministry has sent any  letter to corporate houses to provide \nfunds for National Sports Development Fund  (NSDF) from their Corporate \nSocial Responsibility (CSR) fund or through other sources; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and  \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nFOR YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS \n(SHRI VIJAY GOEL) \n(a) & (b)  Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports has been  regularly \ninteracting with the corporate entities both in public sector and private \nsector for making contributions to the National Sports Development Fund \n(NSDF).  They are also encouraged to contri bute to the NSDF under CSR \n(Corporate Social Responsibility).  \n Further, the apex industry bodies  namely, Federation of Indian \nChamber of Commerce and Industries (FICCI), Confederation of Indian \nIndustries (CII) and Associated Chamber of Commerce (ASSOCHAM) are \nrepresented in the council of NSDF. \n Meetings of Parliamentary Standing Committee on Human Resource \nDevelopment on Promotion of Sports have been held at Mumbai, Bangaluru, \nDelhi, Koltaka and other places . Chairmen and Managing Directors (CMDs) \nfrom various Public Sector Undertakings (PSUs) attended the meetings and \nthey were impressed upon to contribute to NSDF.  \n The Ministry has written letters to  Chairmen and Managing Directors \n(CMDs) of Public Sector Banks (PSBs) such as State Bank of Mysore, \nCanara Bank, Vijya Bank, Syndicate Bank, State Bank of India, Bank of \nIndia Dena Bank, Allahabad Bank etc. and Public Sector Undertakings \n(PSUs) such as Indian Oil Corporation, Oil & Natrual Gas commission, Air \nIndia, Coal India Ltd, Bharat Electronics Ltd, Hindustan Aeronoutics Ltd \netc., for making contribution to NSDF. \n(c): Question does not arise. \n**** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |470", "t": "Sports Infrastructure in Schools", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 470 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nSports Infrastructure in Schools \n \n470. SHRIMATI P.K. SREEMATHI TEACHER: \n  \n Will the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to \nstate:  \n(a) whether the Government has got any scheme for providing financial \nassistance for development of sports infrastructure in schools and \ncolleges; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \nFOR YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS  \n(SHRI VIJAY GOEL) \n \n(a) & (b) The Government is implementing the “Khelo India – National \nProgramme for development of Sports” Scheme from the current financial \nyear 2016-17. The Scheme inter-alia provides for creation of the following \nsports infrastructure : \nS. \nNo. Particulars  At District/State level \n1. Synthetic Athletic Track  Rs. 7.00 crore \n2. Synthetic Hockey field  Rs. 5.50 crore \n3. Synthetic turf football \nground \nRs. 5.00 crore \n\n4. Multipurpose Hall of size \n60M x 40M x 12.5M \nRs. 8.00 crore \n5. Swimming Pool Rs.5.00 crore \n6. Construction of Stadia \ncomplex at District Hqs. \nRs.50.00 crore  \n \n Among others, Schools, colleges and Universities under Central \nand State Governments are eligible to receive funds under this Scheme \nfor the purpose. \n(c) Does not arise.  \n****** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |471", "t": "Progress of UD Schemes", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.471 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON JULY 20, 2016 \n \nPROGRESS OF UD SCHEMES  \n \nNo. 471  SHRI C. MAHENDRAN:  \n \nWill the Minister of URBAN DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Urban Development (U D) schemes / projects of the \nGovernment are progressing sluggi shly and if so, the details \nthereof along with the reasons therefor; \n(b) whether the State Government s are not cooperating well to \nexpedite the projects and if so, the details thereof; \n(c) the steps taken / bei ng taken by the Government to tackle the \ncrisis; \n(d) whether any committee / speci al task force has been \nconstituted in this regard; and  \n(e) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n \n(a)&(b): Urban Development is a Stat e subject.  The State Government \nis responsible for implementing urban infrastructure schemes / \nprojects.  Ministry of Urban Development supports these efforts \nthrough its schemes and progra mmes. The status and other \ndetails of progress of projects under schemes (i) 10% Lumpsum \nscheme for NER (ii) Urban Infrastructure development in \nsatellite towns around seven mega cities, (iii) NERUDP (iv) \nUrban Transport and (v) MRTS are given at Annexure I, II, III, IV  \nCont.. \n \n\n-2- \nand V respectively.  The project s are implemented by the state \ngovernments and their agencies. \n \n(c):  There is no crisis regarding implementation.  Ministry holds \nregular meetings and in teractions with the representatives of \nall State / UT Governments to review the progress of these \nschemes / projects.  The Stat e Government also submits \nQuarterly Progress Report, utiliz ation certificate etc. States \nare being sensitised to complete  the on-going projects through \nseminars, symposiums, conferences and various other \nmechanisms.   \n \n(d) to(e): For effective monitoring of  the projects, Ministry of Urban \nDevelopment has issued the guideli nes to all the States / UTs \nfor setting up of a District Level Advisory and Monitoring \nCommittee (DLAMC) for Urban Development under the \nchairpersonship of an elected re presentative.  The Committee \nwill review and monitor the following programs:- \n(i) Swachh Bharat Mission (Urban) \n(ii) Atal Mission for Rejuvena tion and Urban Transformation \n(AMRUT) \n(iii) Heritage City Development and Augmentation Yojana \n(HRIDAY) \n(iv) Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (PMAY) – Housing for All \n(Urban) \n(v) Deendayal Antyodaya Yojana – National Urban Livelihood \nMission (NULM)  \n \n******* \n\nAnnexure - I \n \nAnnexure-I referred to in reply to part (a) to (c) of the Lok Sabha \nUnstarred Question No.471 for 20.07.2016. \n \n10% LUMPSUM PROVISION SCHEME FOR BENEFIT OF NORTH EASTERN STATES \nINCLUDING SIKKIM \n \nThe scheme started in the financial year 2001-02 to provide fin ancial assistance to North \nEastern States for Development of Urban Infrastructure. Scheme covers NE States Arunachal \nPradesh, Assam, Manipur, Meghalaya, Mizoram, Nagaland, Tripura and Sikkim.  In the last 12 \nyears, 313 projects worth Rs.3012.32 crore has been sanctioned for the 8 States. Out of 313 \nProjects, 181 Projects (57%) have been completed so far.   State of Assam having a slow progress.  \nThe status of each state under the scheme is as under: - \n \nS. \nNo \nState Number \nof \nProject \nProject \nCompleted\nTotal \nestimated cost \n(Rs. in  crore) \nCentral \nAssistance  \n(Rs. in crore) \nReleased upto \n11/07/16  \n(Rs. in crore)  \n1 Arunachal Pradesh 78 54 542.31 495.84 412.34\n2 Assam 47 9 418.89 384.31 245.75\n3 Manipur 23 19 213.65 197.56 150.03\n4 Meghalaya 22 11 192.30 186.40 126.20\n5 Mizoram 24 15 409.42 402.21 326.27\n6 Nagaland 63 39 491.80 444.79 282.68\n7 Sikkim 34 21 381.58 365.88 282.19\n8 Tripura 22 13 362.33 361.40 285.50\n Total 313 181 3012.28 2838.39 2110.98\n \nReasons for slow progress : NE States are located in a climately disadvantage area.  The working \nseason generally remain short due to prolonged rains and snowfa ll in higher reaches.  Many of the \nprojects are located in remote region with poor assess hampering project execution.   Further, States \nis also not contributing their state share on timely basis resulting in delay of project execution.   \n \n\nAnnexure - II \n \nAnnexure-II referred to in reply to part (a) to (c) of the Lok Sabha \nUnstarred Question No.471 for 20.07.2016. \n \nURBAN INFRASTRUCTURE DEVELOPMENT IN SATELLITE TOWNS AROUND SEVEN \nMEGACITIES (UIDSST) \n \nThe pilot scheme of UIDSST was approved midway during the 11 th Plan in July, 2009 with a total outlay of \nRs.500 crore. The scheme aimed at providing basic urban infrast ructure in selected satellite towns around \nseven mega cities with the overa ll objective of ameliorating pr essure on mega cities by improving \ninfrastructure and reforms in the selected towns. Scheme covers  seven satellite towns viz. Vikarabad \n(Telangana), Sanand (Gujarat), Sonepat (Haryana), Hoskote (Karn ataka), Vasai-Virar"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |472", "t": "Encroachment on Forest Land", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \n \n UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 472 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON JULY 20, 2016  \n \nENCROACHMENT ON FOREST LAND \n \nNo. 472        SHRI HUKUM SINGH: \n \nWill the Minister OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) the details of Government, Delhi Development Authority (DDA) and DDA \nreserved forest land under encroachment and illegal construction in \nDelhi along with the value thereof, location and zone-wise;  \n(b) the measures taken by the Government to release the land from \nencroachment and illegal construction along with the action taken \nagainst the officials found guilty;  \n(c) the total land along with value t hereof that got recovered from the \nencroachment/illegal construction in different parts of Delhi, \nparticularly from the clutches of builders and land mafia during the last \none year and till date, location and zone-wise; and \n(d) the stringent measures taken by the Government to make Delhi free \nfrom encroachment and illegal constructions? \n                                \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \n( RAO INDERJIT SINGH ) \n \n(a): Delhi Development Authority (D DA) has informed that there is no \nencroachment on reserved forest land under DDA except some very old \nreligious structures such as: \n1. Peer and Ravidas temple at J.P. City forest. \n2. Nazir Peer, Id Gaha, Kali Mata ka Mandir, Madarsha, Guru Gorakh Nath \nMandir, and Gorakh Nath Madi at Sanjay Van Reserved forest.  \n3. Gurudwara and temple at Seed Bed, R-Block, Rajender Nagar and \nDusghara Village, respectively. \n \n(b) & (c): DDA has informed that the cases  in respect of very old structures \nof Peer and Ravi Das Temple at J.P. City forest are pending in the court.  The \nother structures mentioned in reply to part (a) of the question are very old and \nhave been in existence for a very long time.  \n \n(d): DDA deploys Security Guards and Officials of Horticulture and Land \nManagement Wing to keep a strict vigil and as and when any encroachment \nis noticed, prompt action is taken to remove the same.  \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |473", "t": "GDP Calculation", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF STATISTICS AND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 473 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON WEDNESDAY, THE 20th JULY, 2016 \n \nGDP CALCULATION \n \n473. SHRI RAMESH BIDHURI:  \n  \n Will the Minister of STATISTICS AND PROGRAMME \nIMPLEMENTATION be pleased to state: \n \n(a) Whether the Government has  made any new changes in GDP \nmeasurement standards; \n(b)  If so, the details of changes made previously by the Government in \nlast year’s GDP statistics; \n(c) Whether the Government is working on  new poverty estimates in \nthe country; and \n(d) If so, the details thereof along with previous poverty estim ate \ndetails done by expert committees, committee-wise and if not, the \nreasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATISTICS & PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION (SHRI D. \nV. SADANANDA GOWDA) \n \n \n(a):  Yes, Madam. \n \n(b):  Changes have been made in Gross Domestic Product (GDP) \nmeasurement standards to make them better compliant with the latest \nUnited Nation’s guidelines in System of National Accounts, 2008. They \ninclude: \n \n(i) revising base year of national accounts from 2004 -05 to 2011-\n12 to take into account the changing structure of the economy; \n \n(ii)  using corporate sector data of the Ministry of Corporate \nAffairs as a new source of data for corporate entities in  mining, \nmanufacturing and services sectors; \n \n\n(iii) using latest available data of the National Sample Survey  \nOffice including data of  Unincorporated Enterprise Survey (2010-\n11) and Employment -Unemployment Survey (2011 -12) and data \non sales and service taxes; and \n \n(iv) improving coverage of activities in respect of local bodies \nand autonomous institutions. \n \n(c) & (d): As per the report received from NITI Aayog, the official \npoverty estimates are based on the data of large sample \nsurveys on household consumer exp enditure conducted by \nNational Sample Survey Office, the latest being the survey \non household consumer expenditure conducted in 2011 -12.  \nAt present, t he official poverty line remains the Tendulkar \nline at which the existing estimates relating to 2011 -12 \nhave been computed and released through a Press Note \nissued on 22 nd July 2013.  Since n o further survey on \nhousehold consumer expenditure was carried out \nsubsequently, no new poverty estimates are possible \nunless there is a change in the official poverty line. \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |474", "t": "AC Coaches in Satyagrah Express", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.474 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \n            AC COACHES IN SATYAGRAH EXPRESS \n \n†474. SHRI RAJESH VERMA:  \n \n  Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to attach air conditioned 2 -tier \ncoaches in train number 15273-15274 up-down (Satyagrah Express); \n \n(b) if so, the time by which the said air conditioned 2 -tier coaches will \nbe attached and the train will be operational with these coaches; and  \n \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n                  MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \n                  OF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) to (c) One First cum Second Air conditioned coach is already \nattached in 15273/15274 Raxaul-Delhi Satyagrah Express. \n              However, attachment of additional 2nd Air conditioned coach \nis not feasible at present as the train is running with maximum \npermissible load of 24 coaches.  \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |475", "t": "Complaints/Petitions in Indian Missions", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS  \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.475 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nCOMPLAINTS / PETITIONS IN INDIAN MISSIONS \n \n475.  SHRI JANARDAN SINGH SIGRIWAL: \n \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Indian Missions abroad have received complaints/ petitions/ \nrepresentations from Indian citizens/ people of Indian origin about the \nproblems/hardships being faced in the countries of their residence; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof alon g with the number of such complaints/ petitions/ \nrepresentations reported during each of the last three years and the current year; \nand  \n \n(c)  the details of the steps taken by the Government to address their problems?  \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n[GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD)] \n \n(a) to (c)  As part of good governance efforts, the Ministry of External Affairs \nlaunched an online Consular Grievances Management System named MADAD, on 21st \nFebruary 2015, to extend a helping h and to Indians abroad requiring consular assistance \nand to redress their grievances.  The MADAD online portal represents a qualitative \nimprovement over existing procedures for handling of consular grievances, through \nonline forwarding, filing, tracking and escalation until their eventual resolution.  In \naddition to the Ministry, all our Missions and Posts abroad and the MEA’s Branch \nSecretariats in Chennai, Guwahati, Hyderabad and Kolkata, have been linked to this \nportal.  \n \n  A Call Centre has also been launc hed, in Hindi and English languages, to assist \nconsular grievants by advising them about how to register their grievances on the Madad \nPortal and if necessary register their grievances on their behalf.  \n \nAn Overseas Workers Resource Centre (OWRC)  with a multi -lingual 24x7 helpline \nhas been operational since 2008 and provides information to intending migrants and \noverseas workers on all aspects of overseas employment including requirements to \nobtain a legitimate work permit/visa for employment abroa d. Five Migrant Resource \nCentres (MRCs) have been set up in Kochi, Hyderabad, Gurgaon, Chennai and Lucknow \nto provide information and counselling for intending migrants about the procedure for \nlegal migration and precautions to be taken while migrating . An Indian Workers \nResource Center (IWRC) has been operational in Dubai, UAE since 2010.  \n \n  So far Madad portal has registered over 11,300 grievances, out of which over \n7,360 have been resolved. A table indicating the country -wise status of grievances is \nattached at Annexure.   \n***** \n  \n\n2 \n \nAnnexure \n \n \nMission Location \nGrievances \nReceived \nGrievances \nResolved \nGrievances \nReopened \nTotal Pending \nDeffered More \nInformation \nRequired \nOthers Total \nAfghanistan-Herat 30 13 0 0 0 3 3 \nAfghanistan-Jalalabad 8 7 0 0 0 1 1 \nAfghanistan- Kabul 6 4 0 0 1 1 2 \nAfghanistan - Kandahar 1 0 0 0 1 0 1 \nAfghanistan - Mazar-e-\nSharif \n2 2 0 0 0 0 0 \nAlgeria-Algiers 6 3 0 0 2 1 3 \nAngola- Luanda 22 9 3 2 3 11 16 \nArgentina - Buenos Aires 1 1 0 0 0 0 0 \nArmenia - Yerevan 1 1 0 0 0 0 0 \nAustralia - Canberra 5 0 0 0 0 5 5 \nAustralia - Melbourne 23 12 1 1 0 11 12 \nAustralia - Pert 7 8 1 0 0 0 0 \nAustralia - Sydney 23 21 0 0 0 2 2 \nAustria - Vienna 4 3 0 0 0 1 1 \nAzerbaijan - Baku 3 1 0 0 0 2 2 \nBahrain - Manama 103 78 7 2 1 29 32 \nBangladesh - Chittagong 1 1 0 0 0 0 0 \nBangladesh - Dhaka 30 11 0 0 0 19 19 \nBangladesh - Rajshahi 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 \nBelarus - Minsk 2 2 0 0 0 0 0 \nBelgium - Brussels 2 1 0 0 0 1 1 \nBhutan - Phuentsholing 1 0 0 0 0 1 1 \nBhutan - Thimphu 2 1 0 1 0 0 1 \nBotswana - Gaborone 4 3 0 0 0 1 1 \nBrazil - Brasilia 1 0 0 0 0 1 1 \nBrazil - Sao Paulo 3 1 0 0 0 2 2 \nBrunei Darussalam - \nBander Seri Begawa \n4 2 0 0 0 2 2 \nBulgaria - Sofia 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 \nCambodia - Phnom Penh 2 0 0 0 0 0 0 \nCanada - Ottawa 10 11 1 0 0 0 0 \nCanada - Toronto 30 24 0 1 0 5 6 \nCanada - Vancouver 19 9 1 0 0 11 11 \nChile - Santiago 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 \nChina - Beijing 13 9 1 0 0 5 5 \nChina - Guangzhou 8 5 0 0 0 3 3 \nChina - Hong Kong 10 7 0 1 1 1 3 \nChina - Shanghai 15 8 0 0 0 7 7 \nColombia - Bogota 2 0 0 0 2 0 2 \nCote Divoire - Abidjan 8 2 1 0 1 6 7 \n\n3 \n \nCroatia - Zagreb 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 \nCuba - Havana 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 \nCyprus - Nicosia 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 \nCzech Republic - Prague 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 \nDPR Korea - Pyongyang 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 \nDemocratic Republic Of \nCongo - Kinshasa \n8 2 0 0 0 6 6 \nDenmark - Copenhagen 5 3 1 1 0 2 3 \nEgypt - Cairo 6 1 0 0 0 5 5 \nEthiopia - Addis Ababa 5 2 0 0 0 3 3 \nFiji - Suva 2 0 0 1 0 1 2 \nFinland - Heisinki 1 0 0 0 0 1 1 \nFrance - Paris 17 11 2 1 1 6 8 \nFrance - Saint Denis 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 \nGermany - Berlin 12 11 0 1 0 0 1 \nGermany - Frankfurt 8 5 0 0 0 3 3 \nGermany - Hamburg 2 1 0 0 0 1 1 \nGermany - Munich 4 4 0 0 0 0 0 \nGhana - Accra 14 6 0 1 0 7 8 \nGreece - Athens 13 7 3 0 0 9 9 \nGuatemala - Guatemala \nCity \n0 0 0 0 0 0 0 \nGuyana - Georgetown 2 2 0 0 0 0 0 \nHungary - Budapest 1 0 0 0 0 0 0 \nIceland - Reykjavik 0 "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |476", "t": "Cloud Computing Technology", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY  OF ELECTRONICS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 476 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON: 20.07.2016 \n \nCLOUD COMPUTING TECHNOLOGY \n \n476  SHRI  DUSHYANT SINGH: \n                    \nWill the Minister of Electronics and  Information Technology be pleased to state: - \n(a) whether the Government is promoting research and development in the Cloud Comput ing Technology in \nvarious educational institutes, startups and established companies via financial assistance, knowledge sharing: \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether the Government is also adopting cloud computing methods in function and promotion of PSUs which \nare operating in the IT sector; \n(d) if so, the details thereof and  \n(e) the steps taken by the Government to tackle the security challenges associated with this technology?  \n ANSWER \n \nMINISTER  OF STATE FOR MINISTRY OF ELECTRONICS AND  \nINFORMATION TECHNOLOGY (SHRI P.P. CHAUDHARY) \n \n (a) and (b):  Yes, Sir. The Government is promoting Research & Development in Cloud Computing Technology as \nper the details below:- \n  \n(i)       Grant in-aid support to institutions i.e. IITs, IISC Bangalore, CDAC etc. in Cloud Computing \n(ii)       CDAC has developed Meghdoot, a comprehensive  free and open source Cloud suite useful for setting up a \nCloud Computing environment, Sumegha, a packaged software kit for setting up cloud labs for academic \ninstitutes and research and Megh-Shikshak which is a cloud-based learning management system. \n(iii)     Under the IMPRINT initiative of the Ministry of HRD, designed to promote research in the premier \ninstitutions, one exclusive domain has been created for research on Information and Communica tion \ntechnology including Cloud. \n(iv)     Department of Science & Technology (DST) is also promoting Research and Development activities through \ngrand-aid support to academicians, scientists, technologists and other practicing researchers in the areas of \nCloud and Grid Computing. \n(v) National Institute of Electronics and Information Technology (NIELIT), a capacity building arm of \nDepartment of Electronics and Information technology (DeitY) is also providing training in the field of \nInternet of Things (IoT) and Cloud Computing. \n(c) and (d):  Yes, Sir. NIC has setup the National Cloud for providing services to Government \nMinistries/Departments and other PSUs/organizations. Some of the PSUs/Organizations using NIC National Cloud \nfor hosting of websites and other applications are listed as below:- \n     i.             Satluj Jal Vidyut Nigam Limited  \n                             ii.            Gas Authority of India Limited  \n                            iii.            Balmer Lawrie and Company Limited \n                            iv.            Hindustan Shipyard Limited  \n                             v.            Minerals and Metals Trading Corporation Limited  \n                            vi.            National Thermal Power Corporation  \n                           vii.            Bharat Broadband Network Limited  \n                          viii.            Food Corporation of India  \n                            ix.            Delhi Metro Rail Corporation  \n\n                             x.            National Minorities Development & Finance Corporation  \n                            xi.            Engineering Projects India Limited  \n                           xii.            Garden Reach Shipbuilders Engineers Limited  \n(e):    Government has established a cloud facility which is operated by NIC. It is a cloud deployment model which is \nowned by Government and used by Government departments. All the applications and data hosted in this cloud are \nadhering to the IT Act 2000 and following the security guidelines issued by Comp uter Emergency Response Team \nIndia (CERT-IN) to avoid any security breaches. \n******* \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |477", "t": "Investment by e-Commerce Companies", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ELECTRONICS  AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 477 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20-07-2016 \n \n \nINVESTMENT BY E-COMMERCE  COMPANIES \n \n477    SHRIMATI  VANAROJA  R:  \n                    \nWill the Minister of Electronics and Information Technology be pleased to state: - \n(a) whether the Government has been holding discussio ns with e-commerce giants for the \ninvestment in digital India and startup programmes; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c) the response received by the Government in this regard? \n  \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER  OF STATE FOR MINISTRY OF ELECTRONICS AND  \nINFORMATION TECHNOLOGY (SHRI P.P. CHAUDHARY) \n \n \n(a) and (b):  E-commerce is a rising sector in the country and many leading players are \ninvolved in this enterprise. The Government’s policy framework enunciated in its guidelines \non e-commerce have created an enabling atmosphe re for 100% FDI in Business to Business \ne-commerce and 100% FDI in market place model of e-commerce through automatic route. \n \n(c):    Does not arise. \n \n \n******* \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |478", "t": "Battery Operated Vehicles for Disabled", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.478 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nBATTERY OPERATED VEHICLES FOR DISABLED \n \n478. SHRI ASHWINI KUMAR CHOUBEY: \n \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether there is any provision for free of cost battery operated \n vehicles for disabled and old age passengers at railway stations; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof along with the number of such vehicles at \n major railway stations; \n \n(c) whether the Government has r eceived any complaints that the \n drivers have charged money for use of such vehicles; \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof and the details of action taken against the \n drivers in such cases; and \n \n(e) the number of battery operated vehicles that are proposed to be \n provided per station for convenience of handicapped people? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a): Yes, Madam. \n(b): Zonal Railways have be en authorized to introduce Battery Operated \nVehicles (BOVs) at major railway stations for disabled, old age and sick \npassengers on first come first served basis through sponsorship from \nindividuals, NGOs, Trusts, Charitable institutions, Corporates and \nPSUs/Corporate Houses under their Corporate Social Responsibility with \nno charge to passenger or to the Railway. 5 9 BOVs have been provided \nat 40 major railway stations. \n\n(c): No, Madam. \n(d): Does not arise. \n(e): Battery Operated Vehicle s at major stations are  provided depending \nupon the passenger traffic and availability of sponsors. \n*** \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |479", "t": "Rural Sports Stadiums", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 479 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nRural Sports Stadiums \n \n479.  SHRI RABINDRA KUMAR JENA: \n SHRI DEVJI M. PATEL: \n  \n Will the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to \nstate:  \n(a) the number of rural sports stadium constructed by the Government \nduring the last three years, State-wise; \n \n(b) whether there is a proposal to build such stadiums in the current \nfiscal; \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof, State-wise; and \n \n(d) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \nFOR YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS  \n(SHRI VIJAY GOEL) \n \n(a) to (d) Sports is a State subject and, therefore, it is primarily the \nresponsibility of the State Government to create adequate sports \ninfrastructure including rural sports stadium . The Central Government \ncomplements/supplements the efforts of the State Governments  in this \nregard. \n The Government is implementing the “Khelo India – National \nProgramme for development of Sports” Scheme from the current financial \nyear 2016 -17. The Scheme inter -alia provides for Construction of Stadia \n\ncomplex at District Headquarters wit h a cost ceiling of Rs.50 crores. \nStadia Complex will be funded subject to availability of adequate funds  \nand after taking into account the various facilities available in a State.  \n******* \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |480", "t": "Adequate Staff in ICCR", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.480 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nADEQUATE STAFF IN ICCR \n  \n480.   SHRI P.R. SUNDARAM: \n \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has appointed adequate research \nofficers, directors in Indian Council for Cultural Relations and \nits offices across the world; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the vacancy position as on date; \n \n(c) whether the Government has taken up new r esearch projects \nto highlight cultural relations between India and different \ncountries all over the world and if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(d) the funds allocated, disbursed and utilized in the last three \nyears, year-wise? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n[GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD)] \n \n(a) & (b) Indian Council for Cultural Relations (ICCR)’s structure \ndoes not include posts sanctioned for Research Officers, therefore, \nit does not appoint Research Officers at its Headquarters, Regional \nOffices and Indian Cultural Centres abroad.  The Council, howev er, \nhas established Chairs of Indian Studies (Indian Languages, history, \nYoga etc.) in various foreign universities/institutes. It has a panel of \nProfessors/ Teachers from which Professors/ Teachers are deputed \nto these Chairs. The Council has 35 Cultural Centres and one Sub- \nCentre to which Directors are appointed from ICCR Cadre, MEA \nCadre and from other organizations/Institutions.  \n \n(c) Question does not pertain to ICCR. However, ICCR has not \nundertaken any research project yet in the field mentioned abo ve in \nthe question.  \n\n(d) The Indian Council for Cultural Relations receives funds/grant \nfrom its Administrative Ministry, Ministry of External Affairs. Details \nof allocation, disbursal and utilization of grant for the last three \nyears are as follows: \n \n Year Grant allocated \n(in crores of \nRupees) \nGrant disbursed \n(in crores of \nRupees) \nGrant  utilized \n(in crores of \nRupees) \n2013-14 160.00 160.00 165.45 \n2014-15 167.20 157.62 160.29 \n2015-16 192.00 192.00 161.57* \n   \n*Subject to reconciliation of accounts and statutory audit. \n \n***** \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |481", "t": "Water through Taps/Handpumps at Stations", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS  \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 481 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nWATER THROUGH TAPS/HANDPUMPS AT STATIONS  \n \n†481. SHRI SATYAPAL SINGH:  \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government  has chalked out any special plan to provide \nwater through taps/handpumps at railway stations during summer and if \nso, the details thereof; and \n \n(b) whether there is any proposal to install water coollers at every station \nduring summer and if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS  \n \n (SHRI MANOJ SINHA)  \n \n(a): It is Railways’ endeavour to provide potable drinking water at all \nstations through taps/hand-pumps as per norms. During summer season, \nwhen there is a water scarcity and existing sources are found \ninadequate to meet the water requirements at the stations, water \nsupply is made through tankers. \n(b): No, Madam. However, as per extant policy g uidelines of Railway \nBoard, water coolers are to be provided on those stations which deal \nwith 1000 passengers or more (inward and outward) per day, on the \naverage, and water coolers are accordingly provided. \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |482", "t": "Umang App", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ELECTRONICS  AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 482 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20-07-2016 \n \nUMANG APP \n \n482    SHRI  CHANDU  LAL  SAHU: \n  SHRI  OM BIRLA: \n                    \nWill the Minister of Electronics and Information Technology be pleased to state: - \n(a) whether the Government has proposed to launch new UMANG App to converge existing \ngovernance service under one center; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the other key features of this App; \n \n(c) The time by which the Government proposes to launch the application ; and \n \n(d) The total cost involved in the development of this application? \n \n  \n ANSWER \n \nMINISTER  OF STATE FOR MINISTRY OF ELECTRONICS AND  \nINFORMATION TECHNOLOGY (SHRI P.P. CHAUDHARY) \n \n \n(a) and (b):   Yes, Sir. Unified Mobile Application for New -age Governance (UMANG) will \nprovide for a single unified platform to major Government departments for mobile \nenablement of their services. The primary features are: \n \ni. To provide eGovernance services of Central, State Government departments, \nlocal bodies and/or their agencies through a centralized platform on the mobile \ndevices  \nii. In addition to public services, UMANG shall provide some Citizen Centric \nservices offered from authorized private businesses \niii. Citizens will get a single mobile app for all the services through UMANG  \niv. UMANG App will be multi-lingual, with support covering 12 Indian languages, \nin addition to English \n \n(c):    The UMANG App is likely to be launched by Mar 2017. \n(d):   The total cost involved in development of project including promotion and awareness is \nestimated to be Rs. 52.04 Crores.  \n******* \n\n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |483", "t": "New Passport Seva Kendras", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.483 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nNEW PASSPORT SEVA KENDRAS \n \n†483.     SHRI ARJUN LAL MEENA: \n \n         Will the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has granted approval to open new          \nPassport Seva Kendras in the country;   \n \n(b) if so, the State-wise/Union Territory-wise details thereof; \n \n(c) the details of total amount allocated for opening new Passport \nSeva Kendra in Udaipur dur ing the year 2014 -15 and 2015 -16; \nand \n \n(d) the time by which the new Passport Seva Kendra in Udaipur is \nlikely to be made functional by the Government? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n[GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD)] \n \n(a) & (b) Yes. T he Government has granted approval to open 7 \nnew Passport Seva Kendras (PSK) in addition to the 89 PSKs that \nare working across the country.  These are at Indore (Madhya \nPradesh), Udaipur (Rajasthan), Solapur (Mah arashtra), Siliguri, \nKharagpur, Branch  Secretariat Kolkata  (West Bengal) and Leh \n(Jammu & Kashmir).    \n \n(c)   No expenditure was incurred during 2014 -15 and 2015 -16 for \nthe opening of PSK, Udaipur. The Ministry is working on \nrefurbishment, civil/electrical works, air conditioning and \nprocurement of IT equipments/network installations etc. to set up \nthe PSK.  The anticipated expenditure to set up the PSK Udaipur \nwould work out to be approximately 2.86 Crores. \n     \n(d)  After completion of relevant works, it is expected that PSK, \nUdaipur would be made functional by the end of November, 2016. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |484", "t": "Tilting of Indian Land", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EARTH SCIENCES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 484 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON WEDNESDAY, JULY 20, 2016 \n \nTILTING OF INDIAN LAND \n \n484.   SHRI NANA PATOLE: \n \n          Will the Minister of EARTH SCIENCES be pleased to state: \n \n(a)     whether the Government has studied the data regarding tilting of Indian land \nmass towards north and underground disturbances in the rocky plates and if \nso, the details thereof;  \n(b)    whether this underground disturbance has posed the threat of earthquake  in \nthe country and if so, the details thereof; and \n(c)     the steps taken/being taken by the Government in this regard? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR MINISTRY OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY AND \nMINISTRY OF EARTH SCIENCES \n(SHRI Y. S. CHOWDARY) \n \n(a) Yes Madam. Indian plate is moving towards northeast at a rate of about 5 \ncm/year. This natural process of the Indian Plate movement has been studied \nusing GPS (Global Positioning System) measurements.  \n(b) Yes Madam. In the north, Indian plate collides with the Eurasian plate. The \nrelative convergence between the two causes eart hquakes in the Himalayan \nregion.  \n(c) Bureau of Indian Standards (BIS) has published several guidelines and \nbuilding codes for construction of earthquake resistant structures and for \nretrofitting of ex isting buildings. These guidelines are in wide circulation \namongst the public and the administrative authorities responsible for the \ndesign and construction of earthquake resistant structures in earthquake \nprone areas.  \n \nNational Disaster Management Authority (NDMA), Ministry of Home Affairs \n(MHA), Ministry of Earth Sciences and other state Disaster Management \nAuthorities, have also taken up various initiatives to educate and enhance \nawareness amongst general public and sc hool children on the general \naspects of earthquakes, their impacts and measures to mitigate losses \ncaused by them. A National Disaster Response Force (NDRF) is also functional \nunder the general superintendence, direction and control of the NDMA for the \npurpose of specialized response to natural and man-made disasters.  \n \nMarkets, schools, hospitals and Railway and Bus stations, airports etc. are \nregularly sensitized by organizing mock drills and information dissemination \nrelating to evacuation and steps to b e taken during  emerging response,  \nrescue and relief operations. \n \n*****  "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |485", "t": "Regularization of Unauthorised Colonies", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n \nMINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 485 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON JULY 20, 2016 \n \nREGULARIZATION OF UNAUTHORISED COLONIES \n \nNo. 485 SHRI ASHOK MAHADEORAO NETE: \n \nWill the Minister of URBAN DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the current status of the procedure related to \nregularization of unauthorised colonies in Delhi; \n \n(b) the details of the proposed re vision of the regulations \nwith regard to regularization of unauthorised colonies; \n \n(c) the number of unauthorised colonies for which \nregularization process has been completed as on date \nand the time by which remaining colonies are proposed \nto be regularised; and  \n \n(d) the reasons for delay in this regard? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE  \nIN THE MINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \n  \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n(a): Regularization of Unaut horised Colonies (UCs) in \nDelhi is done by the Govern ment of National Capital \nTerritory of Delhi (GNC TD) in accordance with the \nprocedure laid down in the Regulations dated \n24.03.2008 read alongwith amendments dated \n16.06.2008, 06.06.2012 and 01.01.2015.  \n \n(b): Revision of regulations for regularization of UCs is \nunder consideration. \n \n(c)&(d): GNCTD has informed th at no unauthorised colony \nhas been regularized since 1990. They have received \n1639 applications for regul arization of unauthorised \ncolonies in the year 200 7-08 and 244 in the year \n2013-14. The regularizat ion process involves \nconsultation with various stakeholders and is time \nconsuming. \n \n \n******** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |486", "t": "Passport Melas", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.486 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nPASSPORT MELAS \n \n†486.   KUNWAR SARVESH KUMAR: \n               SHRI RAOSAHEB DANVE PATIL: \n \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has taken note of  the difficulties being  \nfaced by the applicants due to delay in issuing of passport as \ntimely appointment is not given by Passport Seva Kendras and if \nso, the details thereof; \n \n(b) whether passport melas have been organized by various passport \noffices in the recent past; \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof and the details of number of applications  \ndisposed of in  passport melas separately; \n \n(d) whether there is any proposal to organise such passport melas in \nvarious parts of the country particularly in Moradabad in near \nfuture; and  \n \n(e)  if so, the details thereof and if not,  the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n[GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD)] \n \n(a)    The Ministry has been working continuously to improve \navailability of appointment by taking various steps including organizing \nPassport Melas and Passport Seva Camps at week -ends; allowing  \n‘Walk-in’  facility  for certain categories of services such as  Tatkaal  \npassports,  Police Clearance Certificates  and   other miscellaneous \nservices and to Senior citizens (above 60 years) and  differently -abled \n\npersons for all services;  and introduction of online advance payment \nfor seeking appointment to minimize ‘no -shows’. These measures have \nresulted in substantial improvement in availability of appointments.  \n \nAs on 30th June 2016 , out of 8 9 Passport Seva Kendras ( PSKs), \nappointments were available in 53 PSKs within 1 calendar day, 22 \nPSKs within 2 to 7 days, 10 PSKs within 8 to 14 days, 2 PSKs within 15 \nto 21 days and 2 PSKs from 22 to 30 days.   \n \nComparatively, as on 1st September, 2014, out of 77 PSKs \noperational at that time, appointments were av ailable in 29 PSKs \nwithin 7 days, in 11 PSKs within 8 to 14 days, in 11 PSKs within 15 to \n21 days, in 10 PSKs between 22 to 30 days and in 16 PSKs beyond 30 \ndays.  \n \n(b) & (c) Yes. Passport Melas have been organized by various \nPassport Offices in the recent  past.  During January - June 2016,   98  \nPassport Melas have been organized on weekends by various Passport \nOffices where 59,749 passports applications have been processed. The \npassport Office–wise details are annexed.   \n \n(d) & (e) The Passport Melas would  continue to be organized by the \nconcerned Passport Offices on need basis  in their respective PSKs  \nacross the country .  Since Passport Melas are held at the PSKs, it \ncannot be held at Moradabad as there is no PSK there.  However, \nPassport Seva Camps can be  organized if there are adequate passport \napplications from Moradabad necessitating organization of such \ncamps.  One such camp was held at Moradabad on 29 -30 November, \n2014 wherein 166 applications were processed. \n  \n***** \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure \n \nNumber of Passport Melas conducted by Passport Offices, applications received and \nPassports issued during January – June, 2016. \n \n \n \nNumber of \nMela \nApplications \nReceived \nPassports \nIssued \nAhmedabad 14 7,560 7,443 \nAmritsar 3 1,762 1,370 \nBareilly 1 309 304 \nBengaluru 19 20,556 18,097 \nBhopal 5 4,848 3,851 \nBhubaneswar 3 1,151 811 \nChennai 6 3,529 3,209 \nCochin 1 723 716 \nCoimbatore 3 1,553 1,498 \nDelhi 3 1,359 468 \nGoa 1 42 39 \nHyderabad 2 313 292 \nJaipur 7 3,011 2,708 \nJalandhar 13 6,265 5,476 \nJammu 5 1,391 998 \nLucknow 2 1,144 1,131 \nNagpur 2 1,164 983 \nPune 1 1,195 1,131 \nRaipur 1 218 38 \nShimla 3 400 385 \nSrinagar 2 432 330 \nThane 1 824 770 \nTotal 98 59,749 52,048 \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |487", "t": "Slums Near Government Colonies", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \n \n UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 487 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON JULY 20, 2016  \n \nSLUMS NEAR GOVERNMENT COLONIES \n \nNo. 487        SH RI KAUSHAL KISHORE: \n \nWill the Minister OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) Whether a large number of slums have come up around/nearby the \nGovernment colonies in Delhi;   \n \n(b) if so, the details of such colonies;  \n \n(c) whether any efforts were made to  remove these slums and if so, \nthe expenses incurred; \n \n(d) the reasons for the existence of such slums despite efforts made \nto remove them; and \n \n(e) the further steps taken/being tak en by the Government in this \nregard? \n                               \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n \n(a) to (e): Yes, Madam.  The details provided by the Central Public \nWorks Department (CPWD) are A nnexed. CPWD has informed that \ncontinuous efforts are made to remove these slums for their relocation \nand rehabilitation with the help of Delhi Urban Shelter Improvement \nBoard (DUSIB), a body under the Government of National Capital \nTerritory of Delhi (GNCTD).   CPWD has informed that these slums have \ncome up over a long period of time, as the appurtenant land was lying \nunprotected.  \n \nFurther, the National Capital Territory of Delhi Laws (Special Provisions) \nSecond (Amendment) Act,  2014, provides protection from punitive \naction till 31 December 2017, inter-alia, with respect to (i) \nEncroachment or unauthorized development as on 1\nst January 2006; and \n(ii) Unauthorized colonies, village abadi area (incl uding urban villages) \nand their extensions, which existed on 31 st March, 2002 and where \nconstruction took place even beyond that date and upto 1st  June, 2014.\n            \n******* \n \n\n  ANNEX \n \nAnnexure to the reply given to Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No. 487 for \nanswer on 20.07.2016 regarding Slum near Government colonies raised  \nby Sh. Kaushal Kishore. \n \nSl. \nNo. \nColony-wise detail Action taken/effort made/Expenses \nincurred \nArea Under New Delhi Zone-III \n1.  Qtr. No 373, 365, 357 to \n364,833,897,148, D-II-A, 93, kanak \nDurge Colony, Sector-12, R.K.Puram. \nJoint survey was made by Municipal \nCorporation Delhi (MCD), CPWD in year \n1998. A sum of ₹2.34 Crore was \ndeposited by CPWD with MCD for \nrelocation of 605 eligible slum dwellers \nfamilies.  However, action is yet to be \ncompleted.   \n2.  Sankar Camp near ‘J’ & ‘K’ Block M.S. \nFlat, Sector-13, R.K. Puram, New Delhi. \n \nFully encroached land was handed over \nby Land & Development Office (L&DO). \nPayment of compensation for ₹1,89,900/- \nhas been made by CPWD to JJ Cluster \nDeptt., MCD on 03.05.2003 for removing \nthe jhuggies.  However, action is yet to be \ncompleted. \n3.  Anant Ram Dairy, near ‘N’ Block M.S. \nFlat, Sector-13, R.K. Puram, New Delhi. \n \nFully encroached land with permanent \nstructure/semi-permanent structure was \nhanded over by L&DO to the CPWD on \n14.05.1998, on as and where basis. Only \n4 Nos. small plots are vacant for which \ncourt cases are pending in various \ncourts. \n4.  Near ‘E’ Block, M.S. Flats Sector-13, \nR.K. Puram, New Delhi (Taxi stand) \n \nTaxi stand was removed after decision of \nHon’ble Court in favour of CPWD.  The \nappeal  filed in the case is pending in \nSaket  Court.\n \n5.  i. Sector-5, R.K. Puram, New Delhi \nii. Sector-7, R.K. Puram, New Delhi \niii. Sector-8, R.K. Puram, New Delhi \niv. Sector-9, R.K. Puram, New Delhi \nv. Ambedkar Basti near West Block, \nR.K. Puram, New Delhi. \nThe relocation/rehabilitation of Jhuggis is \nunder jurisdiction of  DUSIB. Continuous \nefforts are being made for \nrelocation/rehabilitation by approaching \nDUSIB. \n6. i. Under Service center No. 317, N.W. \nMoti Bagh, New Delhi. \nii. Under Service Center No. 319, Moti \nBagh-1, New Delhi. \niii. Under Service Center No. 321, Type-\nII, Nanakpura, New Delhi \niv. Under Service Center No. 322, Type-\nIV, Nanakpura, New Delhi \nNotices have been issued. \n7.  i. Sector-1, R.K . Puram, New Delhi. \nii. Sector-2, R.K. P uram, New Delhi. \niii. Sector-3, R.K. Puram, New Delhi. \niv. Sector-4, R.K. P uram, New Delhi. \nThe information is based upon the basis \nof joint survey wit h MCD, CPWD, L&DO \nand Delhi Development Authority (DDA), \netc. in 2001-2002. Further, action for the \nrelocation is to be initiated by local body. \nA letter dated 16-04-2012 was written to \nDUSIB in this regard.  \n\n8. i. Lodhi colony, New Delhi Lodhi  Colony, New Delhi is having  87 \nNos. slums clusters. \nCourt case No. WP(C) No. 441/2009 is \npending in Delhi High court. The next \nstep shall be taken up after decision of \nDelhi high court.  \nArea Under New Delhi Zone-II \n1. Timarpur – Sanjay Basti Around 124 No. \nold Type-I Qtrs. \n( Approx. No. of Jhuggy – 1500  \n   Approx. area (Sqm.) -  25485 ) \nThe survey of Slums / Juggies has been \ncarried out jointly by CPWD and DUSIB. \n \nThe initial amount of ₹2,02,50,000/-  has \nbeen deposited with DUSIB for taking \naction for remova"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |488", "t": "Sports Promotion Schemes", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS \n (DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.488 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nSports Promotion Schemes \n \n†488.  SHRIMATI REKHA VERMA: \n  \n Will the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS  AND SPORTS be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a)  the details of schemes being  implemented by Sports Authority of \nIndia (SAI) for encouraging sports and selection  of sports talent and \ntraining; \n \n(b)  the details of amount spent to  encourage sports during the last \nthree years, State and year-wise; and \n \n(c)  the details of achievements at the  international sports events \nduring the last three years? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) FOR YOUTH AFFAIRS \nAND SPORTS \n(SHRI VIJAY GOEL) \n \n(a) S ports is a state subject. H owever, Ministry of Youth Affairs and \nSports (MYAS) through Sports Authority of India (SAI) is implementing \nthe following sports promotional schemes to identify talented sports \npersons in the age group of 8 -25 years and nurture them to excel at \nnational and international levels: \n National Sports Talent Contest Scheme (NSTC) \n Army Boys Sports Company (ABSC) \n SAI Training Centre (STC) \n Special Area Games (SAG) \n Extension Centre of STC/SAG \n Centre of Excellence (CoE) \n National Sports Academies (NSA) \n\n \n SAI has established 10  Regional Centres and 02 educational \ninstitutions to implement the above sports promotional schemes in the \ncountry through 251 SAI sports centres.  Presently, 11773 talented \nsports persons (6626 boys and 5147girls) are being trained in 27 sports \ndisciplines on the residential and non-residential basis.   \n \nThe selected trainees are provided with facilities in the form of expert \ncoaches, sports equipment, boarding and lodging, sports kit, \ncompetition exposure, educational expenses, medic al insurance and \nstipend as per the approved scheme norms. \n \n(b) The scheme-wise expenditure incurred to encourage sports in the \nlast three years is provided at Annexure – I. \n(c) The list of medals won by SAI trainees in International sports events \nduring the last three years is provided at Annexure - II. \n***** \n \n  \n\n \nANNEXURE - I  \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (b) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 488 TO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07. 2016 REGARDING ‘SPORTS \nPROMOTION SCHEMES’ ASKED BY SHRIMATI REKHA VERMA, MP. \nA. \nStatement showing expenditure under Plan (OTHER THAN NER) \n    (Rs. in crore)   \nName of the Scheme 2013-14 2014-15 \n2015-\n16 \n \n  Exp. Exp. Exp. \n \n      Prov. \n \nNational Sports Talent Contest 0.35 0.41 0.90 \n \nArmy Boys Sports Companies 5.37 10.75 6.50 \n \nSpecial Area Games 4.61 4.58 6.63 \n \nSAI Training Centres 26.38 28.3 36.31 \n \nCentres of Excellence 2.16 2.24 0.71 \n \nTotal 38.87 46.28 51.05 \n \nCoaches salaries & other misc exp. 93.42 97.38 96.08 \n \nSalaries & other misc. expenses of establishment & field staff 54.00 36.72 39.66 \n \nSports Sciences & Medical Centre 0.74 0.79 0.85 \n \nEquipment Support -4.63* 1.89 10.17 \n \nOperation & Maint. of staff houses 0.00 0.00 0.00 \n \nOperation & Maintenance of stadia (Delhi) 50.62 59.93   \n \nOperation & Maintenance of stadia (Units/Centers) 15.42 17.03 86.68 \n \nAcademic Programme 1.16 1.83   \n \nComputerized Sports Data Bank 0.00 0.00  0.00 \n \nCapital Projects/Construction Works 18.70 34.44   \n \nCapital Expenditure 10.55   47.92 \n \nGrand Total  278.85 296.29 355.55 \n \n* This expenditure pertains to LC Margin Money incurred during previous year \nand the same has been adjusted during current year \n\n \n \nB. \nStatement showing grants released(allocated) and expenditure under Plan(FOR \nNER) \n    \n \n(Rs. in crore) \nName of the Scheme 2013-14 2014-15 2015-16 \n  Exp. Exp. Exp. \n      Prov. \nNational Sports Talent Contest 0.14 0.10 0.08 \nArmy Boys Sports Companies 0.00 0.00 0.00 \nSpecial Area Games 6.95 6.81 8.21 \nSAI Training Centres 4.05 4.07 4.8 \nCentres of Excellence 0.41 0.38 0.44 \nTotal 11.55 11.36 13.53 \nCoaches salaries & other misc exp. 8.00 10.07 11.32 \nSalaries & other misc. expenses of \nestablishment & field staff 5.97 5.04 5.53 \nSports Sciences & Medical Centre 0.07 0.03 0.03 \nEquipment Support 0.00 0.01 0.00 \nOperation & Maint. of staff houses 0.00 0.00 0.00 \nOperation & Maintenance of stadia 0.54 1.04 0.58 \nAcademic Programme 0.00 0.00 0.07 \nComputerized Sports Data Bank 0.00 0.00 0.00 \nCapital Projects/Construction Works 7.00 7.74 26.70 \nGrand Total  33.13 35.29 57.76 \n  \n \n\nANNEXURE - II \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO  PART (c) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 488 TO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07. 2016 REGARDING ‘SPORTS \nPROMOTION SCHEMES’ ASKED BY SHRIMATI REKHA VERMA, MP \n Details of achievements of SAI Trainees in International Sports events during the year 2012-\n13, 2013-14 & 2014-15 \n            \n \n            \n SN Scheme name 2012-2013 2013-2014 2014-2015 \n     \n G \n S \n B \n G \n S \n B \n G \n S \n B \n 1 NSTC Schools 2 0 4 1 2 3 1 0 0 \n 2 Army Boys Sports \nCompanies (ABSC) 0 2 8 11 8 9 6 8 9 \n 3 SAI Training Centre (STC) 20 12"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |489", "t": "Rationalisation of Freight", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.489 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nRATIONALISATION OF FREIGHT  \n \n489.   SHRIMATI JAYSHREEBEN PATEL: \n   \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Railways intends to rationalise the freight for long \ndistance transportation of coal for Power Generation;  \n  \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) to (c) Rationalisation of freight structure is an on -going \nprocess. The distance slabs beyond 1500 kilometers have been \nrevised from 250 kilometer slab to 125 kilomet er from 01.04.2015. \nFurther, classification of Coal has also been reduced from Class -\n150 to Class-145. \n**** \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |490", "t": "Trains on Metre Gauge and Broad Gauge", "head": " \n \n \n     GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.490 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nTRAINS ON METER GAUGE AND BROAD GAUGE \n \n †490. SHRI HARIOM SINGH RATHORE: \n  \n    Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state  the details of \nnumber of trains being run on meter gauge and broad gauge in different \nStates and Union Territories in the country which are incurring financial \nloss? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTER OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n( SHRI MANOJ SINHA ) \n \n \n \n****** \n \n \n  Train-wise and States/Union Territories wise figures of profitability, \nearnings and expenditure are not maintained. However, on overall \nbasis, Railways are making losses on passenger operations. The loss \nincurred  on  account  of  passenger  services  during  2014-15  was   \n32458.41 crore. \n  \n  \n"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |491", "t": "Modernisation of Stadiums", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 491 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nModernisation of Stadiums \n \n491. SHRI K. ASHOK KUMAR: \n  \n Will the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to \nstate:  \n(a) whether many stadiums are unfit for sports in the country; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) whether the Government has any plan to modernise  some of the \nstadiums in the country to bring them at par with international standards; \nand \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \nFOR YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS  \n(SHRI VIJAY GOEL) \n \n(a) & (b) Sports is a State subj ect and, therefore, it is primarily the \nresponsibility of the State Government to create adequate sports \ninfrastructure in the country . The Central Government \ncomplements/supplements the efforts of the State Governments.  \nTherefore, the Ministry does not ma intain any record of Stadia under the \nState Governments which are unfit for sports in the country. However, the \nfive Stadia , viz., Dr. Karni  Singh Shooting Range,   Dr. Shyama Prasad \nMukherjee Swimming Pool Complex , Indira Gandhi Stadium Complex, \nJawaharlal Nehru Stadium and Major Dhyan Chand National Stadium \n\nmanaged by the Sports Authority of India (SAI), an autonomous body \nunder the aegis of the Ministry of Youth Affairs & Sports , are all being \nused for sports activities. \n(c) & (d) Under the Special Package approved by the Government for \nstrengthening of Sports facilities in Jammu & Kashmir, renovation/ \nmordernisation of existing Bakshi Stadium at Sri nagar and MA Stadium at \nJammu to international standard is being undertaken at total estimated \ncost of Rs.84 crore. \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |492", "t": "Laundries for Washing Bedrolls", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 492 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nLAUNDRIES FOR WASHING BEDROLLS \n \n492.  DR. P. VENUGOPAL: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether it is true that the Railways has taken steps to set up state -of-the-art \nmechanised laundries at many stations to cater to the increased requirement \nof daily washing of bedrolls; \n \n(b)   if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) whether it is also true that the existing laundries of the Railways are flooded \nwith bedrolls, etc. for washing due to lack of manpower and infrastructure to \nmeet the demand; and \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDPENDENT CHARGE)  \nOF THE MINSITRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) & (b):   Indian Railways always endeavor to provide properly washed and cleaned \nlinen to its passengers. With a view to further improve upon the standards of \ncleanliness and hygiene in the linen supplied to passengers in trains, mechanized \nlaundries at 44 l ocations have been set up. These laundries also take care of the \nincreasing requirements of daily washing of bed rolls to the extent of available \ncapacity. \n(c) & (d): No, Madam.  The bedroll washing is done as per the capacity of \nrespective laundries. To meet the additional requirement of washing of bedrolls \nbeyond the capacity of the laundry, the same is outsourced to private laundries. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |493", "t": "Relationship with Nepal", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.493 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nRELATIONSHIP WITH NEPAL \n  \n493.   SHRI BADRUDDIN AJMAL: \n \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether India is losing  out on its good relationship with \nneighbouring country Nepal; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the steps taken by the Government to \nsmoothen out the relationship; \n \n(c) whether any committee/group has been formed to strive for revival \nof the good relationship; \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof along with the current status; and  \n \n(e) if not, the reasons therefor?  \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n[GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD)] \n \n(a) & (b) No.  India’s age–old ties with Nepal are unique and special, \ncharacterized by an open border based on shared history, geography, \nculture, close people–to–people ties, mutual security and close economic \nlinkages. Two–thirds of Nepal’s global trade is with Indi a and over 90% of \nNepal’s third country import –export transit is through India. India is \ncommitted to further strengthen and expand India –Nepal cooperation \nthrough regular bilateral exchanges and development assistance.  India \nwill continue to extend all a ssistance in accordance with the aspirations \nof the people of Nepal, for peace, stability and socio –economic \ndevelopment of the country.  \n \n(c) & (d) There are several bilateral mechanisms in place covering the \nareas of defence and security, trade, power, w ater resources and \nboundary demarcation, besides the India –Nepal Joint Commission which \ncomprehensively reviews the entire gamut of bilateral relations.  An \nEminent Persons Group for India –Nepal relations was also constituted \nafter the visit of Nepalese Prime Minister, Mr. K.P. Sharma Oli, to India, in \nFebruary 2016.  The Group held its first meeting in Kathmandu on 4 –5 \nJuly 2016. \n \n(e)  Does not arise. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |494", "t": "Status of Fruit Preservation Unit at Vatakara", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION  NO. 494 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nSTATUS OF FRUIT PRESERVATION UNIT AT VATAKARA \n \n494. SHRI MULLAPPALLY RAMACHANDRAN: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state the present \nstatus of the vegetable/ fruit preservation unit proposed to be set up \nat Vatakara Railway station?  \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n (SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n Central Railside Warehouse Corporation (CRWC) has carried \nout preliminary surveys for construction of temperature -controlled \nstorages at 10 locations including Badagara (also known as \nVatakara). The survey does not indicate feasibility due to \ninadequate availability of traffic at Vatakara. As such, there is no \nproposal for setting up of temperature controlled cold storage at \nVatakara. \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |495", "t": "Railway Line to Andhra Pradesh Capital", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 495 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nRAILWAY LINE TO ANDHRA PRADESH CAPITAL \n \n495.   SHRI Y.S.AVINASH REDDY: \n \n          Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Railways has considered the request of the \nGovernment of Andhra Pradesh to lay a new railway line to \nconnect its new Capital Amaravati and if so, the details thereof; \nand  \n \n(b)  the quantum of funds earmarked and the status of the \nwork execution done so far?    \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n \n(a) & (b):   Yes, Madam. On request of Government of Andhra Pradesh, \na Reconnaissance Engineering Cum Traffic Survey (RETS) for new \nline between Vijayawada and Guntur via Amravati (67 km) has been \nincluded in Budget of Railway   for the year 2016 -17.  This surv ey is \nbeing carried out by M/s Rail Vikas Nigam Limited. Budget outlay for \nthe survey for the year 2016 -17 is `. 7.00 lakhs.  Execution of this \nwork has not been taken up as the project is yet to be sanctioned.    \n**** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |496", "t": "Express Train from Gorakhpur", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 496 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nEXPRESS TRAIN FROM GORAKHPUR \n †496. SHRI PANKAJ CHAUDHARY: \n     Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether  the Government has announced to run an express train from \nGorakhpur to Lucknow via Anandnagar Badhni and Gonda; and  \n(b) if so, the time by which it is likely to be operational? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a)  & (b) No, Madam. At present, there is no such proposal. However, \nintroduction of train services is an ongoing process on Indian Railways \nkeeping in view traffic demand, operational feasibility, availability of \nresources etc. \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |497", "t": "Maintenance of Display System", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.  497 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON JULY 20, 2016 \nMAINTENANCE OF DISPLAY SYSTEM \nNO.  497            SHRI C.R. PATIL: \n \nWill the Minister of URBAN DEVELOPMENT be please to state: \n(a) Whether display systems on the pl atforms of Metro Stations \nare not working properly in many stations; \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor; \n(c) the number of complaints receive d during last si x months and \ncorrective steps taken in this regard along with details of \ninbuilt mechanism to be adopted to detect such lapses before \ncomplaints are received from users; \n(d) whether the Government proposes  to upgrade the system to \ninform the users of the timing an d destination of the next train \nas well as quick information abo ut disruptions and alternate \nroutes to avoid inconvenience to  passengers as being done in \nsome foreign countries particularly London Tubes; and  \n(e) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF URBAN \nDEVELOPMENT \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n(a) & (b): Delhi Metro Rail Corporation (DMRC) has informed \nthat as on date, out of 636 disp lay panels, only 33  panels are not \nworking due to electronics hardwar e component failure.  The other \nmetro corporations which are being implemented on 50:50 Joint \nCont.. \n\n-2- \n  \nventure of Government of India and respective State/UT Government \nhave informed that the display systems on the platforms are \nworking properly. \n \n(c) : During the last six mont hs, DMRC had received 103 \ncomplaints and all the complaints have been addressed except for \nthe electronics hardware compone nt. Chennai Metro has informed \nthat only 3 complaints were received and attended to.  \n \nDMRC has further informed that, in case of hardware / \nsoftware failure, the repair activitie s are done either in in-house lab \nor through external agencies. Regular preventive maintenance and \nlog monitoring is done to detect  and correct such failures.  \nHowever, it is ensured that at leas t one display is working in every \nplatform. \n \n(d) : No Madam. \n \n(e) : Does not arise. \n \n \n**** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |498", "t": "Catering to Private Contractors", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 498 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nCATERING TO PRIVATE CONTRACTORS \n \n 498. SHRI NABA KUMAR SARANIA: \n \n          Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n                    \n(a) whether IRCTC has given catering services to private contractors; \n(b) if so, the details thereof;  \n(c) the details of the eligibility criteria for getting contracts from IRCTC; \nand  \n(d) the  details of some of the approved actual prices of foods served in \ntrains? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) & (b):  Catering services are provided by Indian Railway Catering and \nTourism Corporation (IRCTC)  to passengers departmentally or by private \nlicencees through both static and mobile units in accordance with the \nprovisions of Catering Policy 2010 and other instruc tions issued from time \nto time.  As on 31.03.2016, 72 mobile units and 344 static catering units \nare being managed by IRCTC.  \n \n(c):  An Expression of Interest (EOI) has been floated by IRCTC in April, 16 \nfor  empanelment  of  service  providers  for  provision of onboard catering  \nContd..2/- \n \n \n\n..2.. \n \nservices in trains for shorter duration. The detailed eligibility criteria has \nbeen defined in the EOI document which inter-alia, includes legal status of \nthe bidder, minimum annual turnover, experience of catering business, \nexperience of kitchen etc. Existing mobile catering licensees of Zonal \nRailways selected through the process of Standard Bid Document (SBD) \nare eligible for empanelment by IRCTC.  \n \n(d):  The approved prices of standard meals, breakfast a nd beverages for \nMail/Express trains are  appended. Sale of A -la-carte items circulated to \nzonal railways has also been permitted in Mail/Express trains. \n**** \n  \n\nAPPENDIX REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (d) OF UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 498  BY SHRI NABA KUMAR SARANIA TO BE ANSWERED \nIN LOK SABHA ON 20.07.2016 REGARDING CATERING TO PRIVATE \nCONTRACTORS. \n(d): The approved price of standard meals, breakfast and beverages for \nMail/Express trains are as under:- \n \n**** \nS. No. Item Existing \nTariff  \nMobile  \n1 Standard tea (150 ml) in disposable cups of 170 ml \ncapacity \n5.00 \n2 Tea (with tea bag)  (150 ml) in disposable cups of \n170 ml capacity \n7.00 \n3 Coffee using instant coffee powder (150 ml) in \ndisposable cups of 170 ml capacity. \n7.00 \n4 Tea in pots  (285 ml) + 2 tea bags + 2 sugar \npouches \n \n10.00 \n5 Coffee in pots (285 ml) + 2 instant Coffee sachets \n+ 2 sugar pouches \n15.00 \n6 Rail Neer/ Packaged drinking water (chilled) \n \n1 litre bottle /1000 ml \n500 ml. bottle                                 \n \n \n15.00 \n10.00 \n7 Janta Meal  or Economy meal or Janta Khana 20.00 \n8  Standard Breakfast  \n8 (i) Vegetarian Breakfast  \na) Bread Butter & cutlet \nb) Idli & Vada \nc) Upma & Vada \nd) Pongal & Vada \n30.00 \n8 (ii) Non-Vegetarian Breakfast \nBread, Butter and omelet \n35.00 \n9 Standard Casserole meals  \n9 (i) Vegetarian 50.00 \n9 (ii) Non- Vegetarian 55.00 "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |499", "t": "Disqualification of Candiates", "head": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF PERSONNEL, PUBLIC GRIEVANCES AND PENSIONS \n(DEPARTMENT OF PERSONNEL & TRAINING) \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 499 \n(TO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016) \n \nDISQUALIFICATION OF CANDIATES \n \n499. SHRIMATI KOTHAPALLI GEETHA: \n \nWill the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether a large number of candidates declared successful by the Union Public Service \nCommission (UPSC) in the civil services examination, 2015 are set to be disqualified \nas reported in the media; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor; and \n \n(c)  whether the Department of Personnel and Training (DoPT) is planning to conduct a \nreview of all those wards of Public Sector Undertaking (PSU) employees who joined \nservice from 1993 and if so, the details thereof and the reasons  therefor?  \n \nANSWER \n \nMinister of State in the Ministry of Personnel, Public Grievances and Pensions and Minister \nof State in the Prime Minister’s Office. (DR. JITENDRA SINGH) \n(a) & (b):    I n case of recommendation of name of a candidate by UPSC for  service \nallocation, the candidate is considered for  allocation to one of those services by the \nGovernment for  which he has indicated his preference subject to fulfillment of  other \nconditions like Medical fitness, eligibility for availing reservation etc . as per Civil Services \nExamination Rules and extant instruction on the subject. \n(c):    No Madam. \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |501", "t": "Special Trains", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.501 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nSPECIAL TRAINS \n \n 501.    SHRI NAGAR RODMAL: \n \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) the details of special trains running in the country, State-wise;  \n(b) whether there is lack of basic amenities in these trains; \n(c) if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor; and \n(d) the steps being taken by the Governmen t for providing basic \namenities in these trains? \n        ANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE ( INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n        (SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n (a) Special trains are being run  during peak seasons, festivals, special \nevents for clearance of extra rush of passengers traffic keeping in view \nthe pattern of traffic, commercial justification, operational feasibility \nand availability of resources. Run ning of special trains on various \nsectors is a continuous process and continue s to vary on day to day \nbasis.  However, a  compendium of special trains on State -wise basis is \nnot maintained.   \n(b) No, Madam. \n(c) Does not arise. \n(d) Regular maintenance, cleaning and upkeep of all passenger amenity \nfittings and fixtures provided in coaches is carried out during laid down \nmaintenance schedules as per prescribed norms.  \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |502", "t": "Shortage of Drinking Water", "head": " \nO.I.H.   \n  GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 502 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON JULY 20, 2016 \nSHORTAGE OF DRINKING WATER \n \nNo. 502  SHRI KIRTI AZAD: \n \n \nWill the Minister of URBA N DEVELOPMENT be pleased to \nstate:\n \n \n(a) whether various cities are facing shortage of \ndrinking water and if so, the details thereof, city-wise;  \n \n(b) the details of water supply schemes in urban \nareas/cities in the country;  \n \n(c) the funds sanctioned an d work undertaken under \nthese schemes during the last three years and the current \nyear so far, State and city-wise; and  \n \n(d) the other remedial measures 