  1176 235.2 0 \n14  Tamil Nadu  3834.49  1582.8 316.56 0 \n15  West Bengal  1393.69  642 128.4 0 \n16  Punjab  857.02  400.8 80.16 0 \n17  Tripura  49.33  44.4 8.88 0 \n18  Manipur  60  54 10.8 0 \n19  Mizoram  46.67  42 8.4 0 \n20  Lakshdweep  1.2  1.2 0.24 0 \n   Total   19212.68  8654.48 1730.9 942.26 \n \n\nANNEXURE II \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (b to d) OF THE LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 502 FOR 20.07.2016 REGARDING “SHORTAGE OF \nDRINKING WATER”. \n \n \n10% Lumpsum scheme for North East States \n(Fund rele"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |503", "t": "Repatriation Treaties", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS  \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.503 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nREPATRIATION TREATIES \n \n†503.      DR. SWAMI SAKSHIJI MAHARAJ: \n     \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether repatriation treaty exists between India and our \nneighbouring countries; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c)  if not, the reasons therefor; \n \n(d)  whether the matter has been discussed with the neighbouring \ncountries; \n \n(e) if so, the details ther eof and the reaction of the neighbouring \ncountries thereto; and \n \n(f)  the time by which these treaties are likely to come into force? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n[GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD)] \n \n(a) to (c) No repatriation or readmission agreement exists at \npresent between India and any of our neighbouring countries. \n \n(d) to (f) Cases relating to illegal entry and stay of foreigners, \nincluding nationals of neighbouring  countries, are dealt with under \nthe provisions of the Foreigners Act, 1946. Following the conclusion \nof legal proceedings under this Act against persons whose stay in \nIndia is illegal, they are deported to their countries of origin.  The \nMinistry of External Affairs and the Ministry of Home Affairs engage \nwith the Embassies of these countries for issue of travel documents \nto enable the repatriation of such persons to their countries.  \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |504", "t": "Monetizing Data Information", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 504 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nMONETIZING DATA INFORMATON \n \n504. SHRI K. C. VENUGOPAL:  \n \n          Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has proposed to monetise data \ninformation like passenger preferences, ticketing patterns and \ncommodity flows by providing it to interested players; \n \n (b) if so, the details of the proposed scheme; \n \n(c) whether the Government has constituted any committee for \nthis purpose and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(d) whether the Government has made any consultation with \nvarious stakeholders in this regard; and \n \n (e) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) & (b) Monetization of data, software, IRCTC website and some of the \nfree services provided by Railways such as PNR enquiry is  one of the \ncomponents of non fare revenue envisaged in the Minister of Railways ’ \nBudget Speech 2016-17. \n\n-2- \n(c) Yes, Madam. A Committee has been formed comprising officers of \nRailways and Centre for Railway Information Systems  (CRIS), on \n10/06/2016. \n \n(d) & (e) Consultation with stakeholders is an integral part of the work of \nthe Committee. \n***** \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |505", "t": "State Employment Scheme", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 505 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nSTATE EMPLOYMENT SCHEME \n \nQUESTION \n \n†505. SHRI R. DHRUVA NARAYANA: \n \nWill the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRE NEURSHIP be \npleased to state: \n \n(a) the number of total States' employment scheme l aunched so far under skill \ndevelopment scheme started by Central Government;  \n \n(b)  whether the Central Government has conducted a  survey of those organisations \nwho have participated in the skill development scheme;  \n \n(c) if so, whether State-wise details of these have  been obtained; and  \n \n(d)  if so, the amount distributed among the organi sations under skill development \nscheme so far, State-wise?    \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) IN THE MINISTRY OF  \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n(SHRI RAJIV PRATAP RUDY) \n \n \n(a) to (d) The Government has set up National Skill  Development Corporation (NSDC) as \na Public private Partnership entity to promote priv ate training providers across the Country. \nThe NSDC conducts short term skill training courses through its approved training partners. As \non date, it has 267 approved training partners (TPs ) with 5093 operational training centres, \nincluding 602 mobile centres with coverage across 29 states and 6  Union Territories. All these \ntraining partners are approved by the NSDC after fo llowing due process. Various kinds of \ntraining, including Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yo jana (PMKVY) are imparted by these TPs \nbased on the Qualifications Packs (QPs) and Nationa l Occupation Standards (NOSs) \ndeveloped by the respective Sector Skill Councils. Field inspections including affiliation & \naccreditation of these training partners are done b y the NDSC. So far, an amount of Rs. 2366 \ncrore has been spent by the NSDC for various training programmes. \n \n Long term vocational training is imparted through Industrial Training Institutes (ITIs). \nThere are a total 13,105 ITIs (Government – 2293 an d private - 10812) across India with 18.7 \nlakh seats in 126 trades. There is no central finan cial support for these long term courses. The \nsurvey of these institutions is done at the time of affiliation through the Quality Council of India. \n \n Further, under Skill Development Initiative (SDI) Scheme, vocational training was \nprovided to people to develop skilled manpower for the industry through a network of 13184 \nVocational Training Providers (VTPs). These VTPs ar e registered through States/UTs and at \nthe end of training, candidates are assessed by the  Assessing Bodies empanelled by the \nDirectorate General of Training. Regional Directora tes of Apprenticeship Training (RDATs) \nconduct inspection of these VTPs. There is no fee f or training and assessment. Successful \ncandidates are awarded National Council of Vocation al Training (NCVT) certificate. The funds \nfor these training courses are released to State/UT  Governments for payment towards all \nreimbursement claims of VTP. A Statement showing the State-wise release of funds under SDI \ntill 2015-16 is annexed (Annexure I). \n \n \n\n  \nAnnexure I  \nFund released to States under SDI Scheme  \n(Amount in Rs. Lakhs)  \nS.NO. STATE/UT                          \nFund \nreleased  in \n2013-14 \nFund \nreleased  \nin 2014-15 \nFunds released \nin 2015-16  \nVTP Registered under SDI \nScheme  \n1 \nAndaman & Nicobar \nIslands \n       762.00                 -                  -                      20  \n2 Andhra Pradesh                -                  -          177.90                  687  \n3 Bihar                -                  -                  -                   532  \n4 Chandigarh          36.00           38.00                 -                      18  \n5 Chhattisgarh                -       3,175.30           70.27                  966  \n6 Dadra & Nagar Haveli                -                  -                  -                        1  \n7 Daman & Diu          11.00                 -                  -                        1  \n8 Delhi     1,008.00      1,500.00         372.00                  218  \n9 Goa                -                  -                  -                      11  \n10  Gujarat                 -          600.00         166.28                  925  \n11  Haryana                 -                  -          143.79                  235  \n12 Himachal Pradesh        166.00         180.10           18.88                  121  \n13 Jammu And Kashmir     1,100.00      1,629.00         260.50                  269  \n14 Jharkhand                -                  -                  -                   174  \n15 karnataka     1,854.00                 -       1,013.20               1,163  \n16 Kerala                -                  -            91.90                  351  \n17 Lakshdweep                -                  -                  -                        6  \n18 Madhya Pradesh     3,651.00      5,943.00         377.81           "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |506", "t": "International Cricket Stadiums", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. †506 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nInternational Cricket Stadiums \n \n†506. SHRI ALOK SANJAR: \n  \n Will the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to \nstate:  \n(a) the details of International cricket stadiums in the country, State -\nwise; \n \n(b) the total number of proposals received from the States for \nconstruction of stadiums including Madhya Prad esh and the action taken \nin this regard, State-wise; and  \n \n(c) the names of places where construction of stadiums are pending due \nto non -allotment of land and the corrective measures taken by the \nGovernment in this regard? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \nFOR YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS  \n(SHRI VIJAY GOEL) \n \n(a) to (c) Sports is a State subject and, therefore, it is primarily the \nresponsibility of the State Government to create adequate sports \ninfrastructure including international cricket stadium . The Central \nGovernment complements/supplements the efforts of the State \nGovernments. Therefore, the Ministry does not maintain any record of \nInternational Cricket Stadiums in the country. \n The Government is implementing the “ Khelo India – National \nProgramme for development of Sports” Scheme from the current financial \nyear 2016 -17. The Scheme inter -alia provides for Construction of Stadia \n\ncomplex at District Headquarters with a cost ceiling of Rs.50 crores. \nStadia Complex will be funded subject to availability of adequate funds  \nand after taking into account the various facilities available in a State.  \n So far, no project for construction of Stadium has been sanctioned \nby this Ministry under the “Khelo India” Scheme. \n******* \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |508", "t": "Employment to BPL Youth", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n \n \nLOK SABHA \n \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 508 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \n \nEMPLOYMENT TO BPL YOUTH \n \n†508. SHRI SUNIL KUMAR SINGH: \n \n \n \n Will the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPR ENEURSHIP \nbe pleased to state: \n(a)  whether the Government has prepared any action -plan for making the youth \nliving below poverty line skilled and preparing the m in accordance with the demand \nof the labour market; \n \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof, scheme-wise and th e total number of youth in the \ncountry living below poverty line who are unemployed, State-wise; \n \n \n(c)  whether the Government has conducted any surve y in this regard and if so, \nthe details thereof; and \n \n \n(d)  the number of institutions providing training in skill development functioning in \nvarious States including Jharkhand and the fields i n which the said institute are \nproviding training, State-wise details thereof? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) IN THE MINISTRY OF \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n(SHRI RAJIV PRATAP RUDY) \n(a) to (d)  The Government of India has over 40 ski ll development \nSchemes/programmes being implemented by various Min istries/Department. These \nSchemes have provisions to promote participation in  skill development by all socio-\neconomic group particularly economically weaker sec tions including those living \nbelow poverty line. The Ministry of Rural Developme nt has been implementing two \nschemes viz; (i) Rural Self Employment and Training  Institutes (RSETI), which \nprovides entrepreneurship development and enables t he trainee to take bank credit \nand start his/her own Micro-enterprise for training  rural poor youth under National \nRural Livelihoods Mission (NRLM) and (ii) Deen Daya l Upadhyaya Grameen \nKaushalya Yojana (DDU-GKY) which is a placement lin ked skill development \nprogram. Details about RSETIs established State/UT- wise is given at Annexure-I \nwhile those pertaining to DDU-GKY ongoing projects along with their sectors is given \nin Annexure II .  Information pertaining to unemployed BPL youth i s not available. \nHowever, the National Sample Survey Office (NSSO) h as been conducting \nquinquennial employment-unemployment surveys to mea sure employment-\nunemployment related indicators. Based on these sur veys, NSSO inter-alia \nestimates number of unemployed persons. Last survey  on employment-\nunemployment was conducted during NSS 68th round (J uly, 2011 – June, 2012). A \nstatement as per this Survey showing State-wise num ber of unemployed persons \naccording to usual status is given at Annexure-III . \n  \n\n \nAnnexure-I \n \nNumber of RSETIs set up in various states \n \nS.N. STATE / UNION TERRITORY No. OF RSETIs ESTABLIS HED \n1 Andhra Pradesh  15  \n2 Arunachal Pradesh  1 \n3 Assam  22  \n4 Bihar  39  \n5 Chhattisgarh  18 \n6 Goa  1 \n7 Gujarat  28  \n8 Haryana  21  \n9 Himachal Pradesh  10 \n10  Jammu and Kashmir  21  \n11  Jharkhand  25  \n12 Karnataka  33 \n13  Kerala  14  \n14  Madhya Pradesh  51  \n15 Maharashtra  35 \n16  Manipur  1 \n17  Meghalaya  4 \n18 Mizoram  1 \n19  Nagaland  1 \n20  Odisha  30  \n21 Punjab  19 \n22  Rajasthan  34  \n23 Sikkim  1 \n24 Tamil Nadu  32 \n25  Telangana  10  \n26  Tripura  5 \n27 Andaman and Nicobar Islands  1 \n28 Dadra & Nagar Haveli  1 \n29 Lakshadweep  1 \n30 Puducherry 1 \n31  Uttar Pradesh  75  \n32 Uttarakhand  13 \n33 West Bengal  19 \n Total 583 \n  \n\n \nAnnexure-II \nNumber of ongoing DDU-GKY projects in States with their sectors \n \nSl \nNo.  \nState Name  No. of \nProjects  \nSector in which training provided  \n1 ANDHRA \nPRADESH \n4 Apparel, Banking, Financial services and Insuranc e (BFSI), \nConstruction, IT-ITES, Production And Manufacturing , \nRetail, Tourism & Hospitality \n2 ASSAM 21 Apparel, Automotive, Banking, Financial services and \nInsurance (BFSI), Beauty & Wellness, Business & \nCommerce, Capital Goods, Construction, Electrical, \nElectronics, Healthcare, IT-ITES, Logistics & Suppl y \nChange Management, Production And Manufacturing, \nRetail, Security, Telecom, Textiles, Tourism & Hospitality \n3 BIHAR 34 Agriculture, Apparel, Automotive, Bankin g, Financial \nservices and Insurance (BFSI), Beauty & Wellness, \nBusiness & Commerce, Construction, Electrical, \nElectronics, Healthcare, IT-ITES, Logistics & Suppl y \nChange Management, Media & Entertainment, Power & \nEnergy, Retail, Security, Telecom, Textiles, Touris m & \nHospitality \n4 GUJARAT 18 Apparel, Automotive, Banking, Financia l services and \nInsurance (BFSI), Beauty & Wellness, Capital Goods,  \nChemical, Construction, Electrical, Electronics, He althcare, \nIT-ITES, Production And Manufacturing, Retail, Secu rity, \nTelecom, Tourism & Hospitality \n5 HARYANA 11 Apparel, Automotive, Banking, Financia l services and \nInsurance (BFSI), Business & Commerce, Construction , \nElectrical, Electronics, Healthcare, IT-ITES, Retai l, Security, \nTelecom, Tourism & Hospitality \n6 JAMMU AND \nKASHMIR \n15 Apparel, Beauty & Wellness, Construct"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |509", "t": "Impact of Brexit on Indian Community in U.K.", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.509 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nIMPACT OF BREXIT ON INDIAN COMMUNITY IN U.K. \n \n509.  SHRI M.B. RAJESH: \n \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS  be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) whether the Government of India has assessed the impact of \nBrexit on Indian community in UK; \n \n(b) the possible impact of Brexit on our country; and \n \n(c) the measures taken by the Government to protect Indian \ncommunity in UK from adverse impact of Brexit, if any? \n  \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n[GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD)] \n \n(a) to (c) For the United Kingdom to leave the European Union, it \nhas to invoke Article 50 of the Lisbon Treaty . It is up to the \nGovernment of United Kingdom to decide when to invoke this \nArticle. Such an invocation will then set in motion , the process for \nthe United Kingdom to withdraw from the European Union. The \nrelationship between the United Kingdom and the European Union is \ntherefore yet to evolve and until such time, it is hard to as sess the \nimpact of Brexit on India and the Indian community in the United \nKingdom. High Commission of India in London is in touch with the \nIndian community, various organisations and business associations \nto understan d the eventual implications of B rexit on the Indian \ncommunity.  \n***** \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |510", "t": "Sanitation Facilities", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 510 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON JULY 20, 2016 \nSANITATION FACILITIES \n \n \nNo. 510  SHRI GODSE HEMANT TUKARAM:  \n \nWill the Minister of URBAN DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has reviewed the sanitation \nfacilities in different parts of t he country, particularly in metros and \nother major cities;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c ) whether the Union Government  provides funds to the various \nState Governments, Non-Govern mental Organisations (NGOs), \nCharitable Trusts/Institutions fo r the construction of community \ntoilets and sanitation facilities in  various States , including semi-\nurban areas of the country; and \n \n(d)       if so, the details thereof?  \n \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF URBAN \nDEVELOPMENT \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n \n \n(a & b): Yes,  Madam. \n             Swachh Bharat Mission (SBM) has been framed based on the \nsanitation facility available in the urban areas of the Country as per \nCensus 2011. The SBM is under  implementation by all the \nStates/UTs for providing sanitati on facilities, particularly in the \nmetros and other major cities. Mini stry of Urban Development is \nregularly reviewing the progress of  SBM at Central level through in-\nperson interactions, video  conferences, regular visits etc. to speed \nup the implementation of the Mission.  \nP…2/- \n\n-2- \n(c &  d):  Yes,  Madam. \n  Government of India has s anctioned Rs. 1520.43 Crore for the \nconstruction of individual household toilets, Rs. 208.57 Crore for the \nconstruction of community toilets & Rs. 890.84 Crore for solid \nwaste management to the States/UTs  under SBM, so far, including \nsemi-urban areas of the Country. Further, there is no provision in the \nguidelines of SBM to provide dir ect funds/assistance to NGOs or \nCharitable Trusts/Institutions for the construction of toilets and \nother sanitation facilities from Centre.  \n**** \n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |511", "t": "Increase in Lower Berth for Senior Citizen Quota", "head": "   \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 511 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nINCREASE IN LOWER BERTH FOR SENIOR CITIZEN QUOTA \n  \n511.   SHRI G. HARI: \n \n          Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Railways has increased lower berth quota for senior \ncitizens in trains; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) whether the Railways is considering to clear the waiting list \ntickets of the senior citizens on priority basis; and \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) & (b): Yes Madam.  The combined quota earmarked  for Senior \nCitizens; Female passenger 45 years of age and above and Pregnant \nwomen  in Sleeper, AC -3 tier and 2A classes has been enhanced by \n50% and now this quota is six lower berths per coach in Sleeper class \nand three lower berths per coach in AC 3 tier and AC 2 tier classes . In \ncase of Rajdhani, Duronto and fully Air Conditioned/Express trains, the \nnumber of lower berths to be earmarked under this quota in 3 AC class \nare four per coach as against 3 in normal Mail/Express trains. \n(c) No, Madam. \n(d) Does not arise. \n******  "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |512", "t": "Environment Friendly Construction", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 512 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON JULY 20, 2016 \n  \nENVIRONMENT FRIENDLY CONSTRUCTION \n \nNo. 512       \n ADV. M. UDHAYAKUMAR: \n \nWill the Minister of URBAN DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to streamline new construction \nwith solar energy and environment friendly modules and if so, the \ndetails thereof;  \n(b) whether the Government also pr oposes to give more thrust on \nrainwater harvesting for various types of buildings; \n(c) if so, whether the rainwater harvesting norms is likely to be \nmonitored by a special cell in each civic body; and  \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF URBAN \nDEVELOPMENT \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n \n(a): Yes, Madam. This Ministry has  released the Model Building Bye \nLaws (MBBL), 2016 in March, 2016 which is an advisory document for \nthe State Governments to revise their respective Building Bye Laws. \nThe MBBL, 2016 have incorporated the norms for green buildings and \nsustainability which includes norm s for installing roof top solar \nphotovoltaic cells for residential and non-residential buildings. \n(b): Yes, Madam. Rainwater harvesting norms have been incorporated \nin Model Building Bye Laws (MBBL), 2016. \n(c) & (d): Yes, Madam. The Model  Building Bye Laws (MBBL), 2016 \nrecommend establishing the Rainwater Harvesting Cell in the Urban \nLocal Bodies. As Urban Development is a State subject, it is up to the \nState Governments to revise their respective Building Bye Laws by \ntaking into considerati on the advisory issued in the form of Model \nBuilding Bye Laws, 2016. Therefore, it is upto the State Governments \nto set up a special cell to moni tor rainwater harvesting norms in \nbuilding plan. \n******* "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |513", "t": "Adarsh Station Yojana", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS  \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 513 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nADARSH STATION YOJANA  \n \n513. SHRI RAM MOHAN NAIDU KINJARAPU:  \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the amount of fund allotted and  released for Adarsh Station Yojana \nduring the last three years and the current year; \n \n(b) whether the Railways has fixed any timeframe for implementation of \nthis scheme and if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c) the stage at which the work has been complete d in the stations \nselected under the scheme? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE  (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS  \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA)  \n(a) to (c): The expenditure on development of stations under  ‘Adarsh’ \nStation Scheme is generally funded under Plan Head –‘Passenger \nAmenities’. Fund allocation under this Plan Head, during 2013 -14, \n2014-15, 2015 -16 and 2016 -17 is ` 914.40 crores,  ` 1047.90 crores,   \n` 1211.81 crores and ` 838.27 crores (Budget Es timate) respectively.  \n Development of identified stations under ‘Adarsh’ station \nscheme is a continuous process. 1252 stations have been identified \nfor development under this scheme, out of which 986 stations have \nbeen developed. The remaining stations hav e been planned for \ndevelopment by the end of the year 2017 -18. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |514", "t": "Railway Reservation Counter at Kochi Airport", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.514 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \n \nRAILWAY RESERVATION COUNTER AT KOCHI AIRPORT \n \n \n514. SHRI ANTO ANTONY :  \n \n       \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has received any proposal for setting \nup of railway reservation counter at Kochi International Airport ; \nand \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the response of the Government \nthereto? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n \n(a) No, Madam. \n \n(b)   Does not arise. \n**** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |515", "t": "Mechanism to Deal with Complaints of Passengers", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 515 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nMECHANISAM TO DEAL WITH COMPLAINTS OF PASSENGERS \n \n \n†515. SHRIMATI RANJANBEN BHATT: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is paying serious attention towards \nredressal of complaints of railway passengers; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof alongwith the details of steps taken \nin this regard; and  \n \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND  \n MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n \n(a) to (c): Yes, Madam. Government has set up different \nchannels of registering passengers complaints/grieva nces \nnamely, Complaints Books at the Stations and in trains, May I \nhelp you booth/Counters at Stations, All India Help line No. -138, \nCPGRAMS, COMS, Social Media etc. Large numbers of \ncomplaints are received through these channels which are sent \nto concerned authorities for prompt and satisfactory redressal. \n \n****** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |516", "t": "Swachh Yug Campaign", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF YOUTH AFFAIRS) \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. +516 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \nSwachh Yug Campaign \n+516. SHRI KUNWAR PUSHPENDRA SINGH CHANDEL \n Will the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to \nstate: \n(a) whether the Government has initiated 'Swachh Yug' campaign; \n(b) if so, the salient features of the same; \n(c) whether the Government proposes to ensure more social \nparticipation of youth through this campaign and if so, the details \nthereof; and \n(d) the manner in which youths are likely to be benefitted under \nthis campaign? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) FOR  \nYOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(SHRI VIJAY GOEL) \n \n(a) to (d) :  Yes, Madam. The Ministry of Drinking Water and \nSanitation, in partnership with Ministry of Youth Affairs and \nSports and Ministry of Water Resources, River Development \nand Ganga Rejuvenation, has launched ‘Swachh Yug’ campaign, \nwhich involves  intensifying s upport to the five States of \n\nUttarakhand, Uttar Pradesh, Bihar, Jharkhand and West Bengal \nto make all villages along the banks of the Ganga, Open \nDefecation Free (ODF). There are 4257 villages on the banks of \nGanga under 1651 Gram Panchayats, 52 districts and 5 States. \n1020 villages (23.96%) have been declared ODF as on 19 -07-\n2016 in this effort. The Swachh Yug campaign is a \ncollaborative effort between the Swachh Bharat Mission, local \nyouth leaders and Namami Gange Project.  \n \nThe Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports is enlisting the support \nof Nehru Yuva Kendra Sangathan (NYKS) a nd other youth \norganisations. These organizations are called upon to mobilise \nlocal youth volunteers to support behavior change campaign in \nthe targeted villages. 5 days Virtual Classrooms trainings have \nbeen organized for this purpose.  \n \nNYKS has formed 2,218 new youth clubs in targeted villages to \nensure sustained participation of local youth in the campaign. \n6,666 youth have been selected from youth clubs to ta ke lead \nand actively participate in the campaign. This is also benefiting \nthe youth participating in campaign by way of developing \ncommunity leadership qualities in them. \n \n    **** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |517", "t": "Aadhaar Card to NRIs", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY  OF ELECTRONICS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 517 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON: 20.07.2016 \n \nAADHAAR CARD  TO NRIs \n \n517       SHRIMATI  RAKSHATAI  KHADSE: \n                    \nWill the Minister of Electronics and Information Technology be pleased to state: - \n(a) whether the Government proposes to issue Aadhaar Cards to the Non - Resident Indians \n(NRIs) making them active in participation of various flagship programmes of  Government \nincluding Skill India, Digital India and Clean Ganga Initiatives; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the steps the Government is planning to adopt in this  regard; \n \n(c) whether the Government is also planning to issue Aadhaar Cards for the Overseas Citizen \nof India card holders on the same ground as in case of NRIs; and \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER  OF STATE FOR MINISTRY OF ELECTRONICS AND  \nINFORMATION TECHNOLOGY (SHRI P.P. CHAUDHARY) \n  \n   \n(a) to (d):  The Aadhaar (Targeted Delivery of Financial and other Subsides,  Benefits and \nServices) Act, 2016 has been notified in the Gazette of India on 26 th March 2016. According \nto Section 3(1), every resident shall be entitled to obtain an Aadhaar number by submitting \nhis demographic information and biometric information by u ndergoing the process of \nenrolment. It also provides that Central Government may from time to time notify such other \ncategory of individuals who may be entitled to obtain an Aadhaar number.  \n \nAt present, only residents of the country are being enrolled for Aadhaar. \n \n******** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |518", "t": "Telecom and Internet in Lakshadweep", "head": " \n  \n \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS \nDEPARTMENT OF TELECOMMUNICATIONS  \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.518  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20 TH  JULY, 2016 \n \nTELECOM AND INTERNET IN LAKSHADWEEP \n \n518. MOHAMMED FAIZAL: \n \n \nWill the Minister of COMMUNICATIONS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has any plan to improve Telecommunications and \nBroadband Internet facilities in Lakshadweep; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c)  the action taken and the result achieved as a result thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (IC) OF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS & \n MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) Yes, Madam. \n \n(b) & (c) \n \n (i)  The Department proposes to enhance the existing satellite bandwidth capacity \nlinking mainland and Lakshadweep islands from 102 Mbps to 318 Mbps, which will \nrequire capital investment of Rs. 46.53 Crore. The work has been awarded to Bharat \nSanchar Nigam Limited (BSNL). The project is likely to be completed by December \n2016. \n \n(ii)  Work of setting up 10 mobile towers in Lakshadweep Islands has also been \ngiven to BSNL. BSNL has prepared the Detailed Project Report (DPR) and cost \nestimates. \n \n(iii)  As a long term measure to improve connectivity in Lakshadweep islands, the \nDepartment is studying the feasibility of laying submarine Optical Fibre Cable (OFC) \nbetween Kochi and Lakshadweep islands. Telecommunications Consultants India \nLimited (TCIL) has been entrusted to carry out the study.  \n \n \n************** \n  \n \n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |519", "t": "Building Bylaws", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \n  \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN POVERTY ALLEVIATION \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 519 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON JULY 20, 2016 \n \nBUILDING BYLAWS \n \nNo. 519 SHRI ASADUDDIN OWAISI: \n \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AN D URBAN POVERTY ALLEVIATION \nbe pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government has released model building bylaws \nto give boost to the real esta te sector and for fast processing \nand approval of projects; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) the minimum time fixed for approval of project; \n \n(d) whether any penalty clause has been imposed for delayed \napproval of project; and  \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof? \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOUSING & URBAN \nPOVERTY ALLEVIATION \n \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n \n(a)&(b):   Yes, Madam, the Model  Building Bye Laws (MBBL), 2016 \nwere released in March, 2016. The Bye Laws have a \nchapter on Streamlining t he Building Plan approvals \nwhich  \n..2/- \n\n \n-2- \n \n \nprescribe various initiati ves for fast processing and \napproval of projects, like single window online \napplication, e-payments, common application form, etc.  \n \n(c): There is no minimum time  fixed. However, the Model \nBuilding Bye Laws, 2016 prescrib e that all building plans \nshould be approved within 30 days.  \n \n(d): No, Madam. \n \n(e): Question does not arise. \n  \n********** \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |520", "t": "Telecom Towers at Residential Colonies", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 520 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON JULY 20, 2016 \n  \nTELECOM TOWERS AT RESIDENTIAL COLONIES \n \nNo. 520       \n SHRI SANGANNA AMARAPPA:              \n \nWill the Minister of URBAN DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has allowed telecom companies to \ninstall telecom towers on the top of the residential houses/societies;  \n(b) if so, the details of norms that  are to be followed and fees to be \ncharged from the telecom companies for the same; and \n(c) the types of residential houses/ societies on which such telecom \ntowers are likely to be installed? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF URBAN \nDEVELOPMENT \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n(a) to (c): Regulating telecom companies regarding setting up norms \nand fees etc. to install telecom towers on various buildings including \nresidential houses/societies falls under the purview of State \nGovernments. This Ministry has  released the Model Building Bye \nLaws (MBBL), 2016 in March, 2016 which is an advisory document for \nthe State Governments to revise their respective Building Bye Laws. \nThe advisory norms for installing the mobile towers have been \nprescribed in the MBBL, 2016. \n Similarly, Delhi De velopment Authority (DDA), with the approval \nof Ministry of Urban Development, has notified Unified Building Bye \nLaws for Delhi in March, 2016. \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |521", "t": "Pending Proposals for Promotion of Sports", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. †521 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nPending Proposals for Promotion of Sports \n \n†521. PROF. RAVINDRA VISHWANATH GAIKWAD: \n  \n Will the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to \nstate:  \n(a) the proposal received by Union Government from State Government of \nMaharashtra for promoting sports in the State, district -wise during the \nlast two years; \n \n(b) the number of proposals cleared out of them and the amount released, \nthe details thereof; \n \n(c) the number of proposals lying pending; and \n \n(d) the time by which the pending proposals are likely to be cleared by the \nGovernment? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \nFOR YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS  \n(SHRI VIJAY GOEL) \n \n(a) to (d) Sports is a State subject and, therefore, promotion of sports in \nthe States is primarily the responsibility of the State Government . The \nCentral Government has been complementing/supplementing the efforts \nof the State Governments  for creation of sports infrastructure and \nconduct of competitions through schemes, namely, Rajiv Gandhi Khel \nAbhiyan (RGKA) and Urban Sports Infrastructure Scheme (USIS) during \nthe last two years. Release of grants under RGKA and USIS are demand -\ndriven and made against  proposals received from States /UTs and other \n\neligible entities, and which are complete in all respects as per provisions \nof the respective Scheme and subject to  furnishing of Utilisation \nCertificate against grants released  earlier by this Ministry.  Details of \nfunds released under RGKA and USIS during the last two years to the \nState of Maharashtra are given in Annexure -I. A new Central Sector \nScheme called “Khelo India – National Programme  for Development of \nSports” has been launched in place of erstwhile RGKA and USIS, for \nimplementation during 2016 -17. All the States and other eligible entities \nhave been asked to furnish project proposals in accordance with the \nguidelines of the new Scheme.  \n****** \n  \n\nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF THE LOK \nSABHA UN STARRED QUESTION NO. †521 FOR 20.07.2016 ASKED BY \nPROF. RAVINDRA VISHWANATH GAIKWAD , MP REGARDING PENDING \nPROPOSALS FOR PROMOTION OF SPORTS \n \nAnnexure- I  \n \nDetails of funds released to the State of Maharashtra during 2014-15 and 2015-16 under RGKA Scheme  \n                                                                                                          \n  (Rs. in crore) \n \nDetails of funds released to the State of Maharashtra during 2014-15 and 2015-16 under USIS \n2014-15         (Rs. in crore) \nS. No. State Project \nGrant \napproved \n(Date) \nGrant released \n(Date) \n1.  Maharashtra \nLaying of synthetic athletic track at \nArmed Forces Medical College \n(AFMC), Pune \n5.00 \n(23.07.2014) \n3.00 \n(23.07.2014) \n2. Maharashtra \nConstruction of Multi -purpose indoor \nhall at University of Mumbai. 6.00 \n(19.12.2014) \n \n1.00 \n(19.12.2014) \n \n2015-16          (Rs. in crore) \nS. No. State Project Grant approved \n(Date) \nGrant \nreleased \n(Date) \n1. Maharashtra \nConstruction of a Multi -purpose \nIndoor Hall at Nashik Municipal \nCorporation. \n6.00 \n(18.01.2016) \n0.695 \n(18.01.2016) \n2. Maharashtra \nConstruction of multi -purpose indoor \nhall at Rashtrasant Tukdoji Maharaj \n(RTM) Nagpur University, \nMaharashtra \n6.00 \n(01.03.2016) \n1.80 \n(01.03.2016) \n \n****** \nName of the State/ UT \n2014-15 2015-16 \nInfrastructure Competition Infrastructure Competition \nMaharashtra - 5.18  -  - \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |522", "t": "Chengalpet-Arakkonam Railway Line", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 522 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nCHENGALPET-ARAKKONAM  RAILWAY LINE \n \n522. SHRI B. SENGUTTUVAN: \n  \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS  be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Chengalpet-Arakkonam railway line has been \nremaining incomplete for well over two years and if so, the reasons \nfor the long pendency of this project; \n \n(b)  whether objection was received from the navy that electrification \nof railway line from Thakkolam to Arakkonam on Chengalpet -\nArakkonam line, since it lies adjacent to the Rajali Naval Base, \nwould pose security -related issues to the naval station, and if so, \nthe details thereof; \n \n(c)  whether alternate route avoiding Thakkolam has been finalized by \nthe southern railway in view of the objections raised by the navy \nand if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(d)  whether any compensation amount was agreed to be given by the \nMinistry of Defence to the Railways for the said deviation and if so, \nthe details thereof; and \n \n(e)  the timeframe by which the project would be completed entirely \nand the suburban train services would commence operation?  \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n  \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n(a) to (e): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.   \n***** \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 522 BY SHRI B. SENGUTTUVAN TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 20.07.2016 REGARDING \nCHENGALPET-ARAKKONAM RAILWAY LINE. \n \n(a) to (c) : Gauge conversion between  Chengalpattu -Arakkonam \nhas been completed and commissioned. Electrification of one block \nsection between Thakkolam -Arakkonam  portion  could not be \nexecuted due to objections from the Naval Authorities as \nelectrification of the line near Rajali Naval Base could not be taken \nup on account of security issues. Therefore,  it has been decided to \ntake up  construction of Thakkolam -Arakkonam i n diverted \nalignment with its electrification. \n(d): The work of diversion of broad gauge line was agreed by Naval \nAuthorities on deposit terms at an initial cost of ` 25.73 crore and   \n` 23.75 crore had been deposited by Naval Authorities.  However, \ndue to delay in land acquisition by State Government, the cost has \nescalated and Revised Estimate was prepared at a cost of ` 54.57 \ncrore and accepted and sanctioned by Naval Authorities.  Thus, \nNaval Authorities have to deposit balance amount of ` 30.82 crore \nwith the Railways.   \n(e): No time frame for completion of the work has been fixed.   \n****** \n \n \n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |523", "t": "Monorail Projects", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 523 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON JULY 20, 2016 \nMONORAIL PROJECTS \n \nNO. 523      SHRI  M. CHANDRAKASHI: \n \nWill the Minister of URBAN DEVELOPMENT be please to state: \n(a) Whether the Government has re cently received proposal for \nmonorail project from the Govern ment of Jharkhand and if so, \nthe details thereof; \n(b) The time by which the project  is likely to be approved and \nimplemented;  \n(c) Whether the same criteria/modalities as in the case of metro \nrail is likely to be followed fo r implementation of monorail \nprojects; and \n(d) If so, the details thereof?  \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n \n(a) :                No, Madam. \n \n(b)  to (d):      Does not arise. \n \n*** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |524", "t": "Land to NGOs", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 524 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON JULY 20, 2016 \n \nLAND TO NGOs \n \nNO. 524 SHRI RAM CHARITRA NISHAD:   \n \nWill the minister of urban development be pleased to state: \n \n(a) : Whether the Government allocat es land to Non-Governmental \nOrganizations (NGOs) on concessional rates and if so, the details \nalongwith the specific norms in this regard; and \n(b) The names of the NGOs allocated land on concessional rates so \nfar? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF URBAN \nDEVELOPMENT \n \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n \n(a) : The land was allotted to Non-Government Organizations (NGOs) \nby Land & Development Office (L&DO) on institutional rates prior \nto 7.11.2006. However, in view of scarcity of land in Delhi it has \nbeen decided on 7.11.2006 t hat L&DO lands in Delhi will not be \nallotted to NGOs. DDA allots l and to various NGOs at their \ninstitutional rates. The price fixation norms that are followed for \nallocation of land to NGOs are as per rates issued by the Ministry \nfrom time to time (copies of letters fixing such rates is placed at \nAnnexure-I). \n \n(b): The list of NGOs to which land has been allotted by L&DO and \nDDA are at Annexures-II & III respectively. \n                                              ********* \n\nANNEXURE‐II \nS.No.   Name of Institution  \n1.   All India Fine Arts Crafts Society  \n2.   Yogoda Satsanga Society of India  \n3.   Bhartiya Kala Kendra Trust  \n4.   Yuva Bharti Trust  \n5.   Pearey Lal Bhawan Association  \n6.   Delhi Symphony Society  \n7.   Chinmaya Mission  \n8.   Ganga Ram Hospital  \n9.   Children Book Trust  \n10.   Chittaranjan Park Bangiya Samaj  \n11.   Shanti Avedna Ashram  \n12.   Purboshree Mahila Samiti   \n13.   Indian Mountaineering Foundation  \n14.   Vedic Cultural Centre  \n15.   Alliance Franchise‐de‐Delhi  \n16.   Indian Social Institute  \n17.   National Academy of Medical Sciences  \n18.   Deshbandhu Chittaranjan Memorial Trust  \n19.   Sri Kanchi Kamakoti  \n20.   Bengal Association  \n21.   Bipin Chandra Pal Memorial Trust  \n22.   Natya Ballet Centre  \n23.   Moolchand Hospital  \n24.   Asian News International  \n25.   Public Opinion Trends Analysis & News Service  \n26.   Maratha Mitra Mandal  \n27.   Indo German Social Service Society  \n28.   Dr. Hardikar Foundation Trust  \n29.   National Youth Hostel Trust  \n30.   Lok Kalyan Samiti  \n31.   All India Sikh Federation  \n32.   Maulana Azad Medical College  \n33.   Bharat Sevak  Samaj Delhi Pradesh  \n34.   Bharti Sangam Trust  \n35.   Antar Rashtiya Sahayog Parishad  \n36.   India Institute of Architects  \n37.   Chronicle Society of India  \n38.   Indian Building Congress  \n39.   Natya Tarangini  \n40.   Caritas India  \n