, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |614", "t": "Gauge Conversion and Doubling of Railway Lines", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.614 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nGAUGE CONVERSION AND DOUBLING OF RAILWAY LINES \n \n†614.  SHRI DHARMENDRA YADAV: \nSHRI KODIKUNNIL SURESH: \nSHRI BHAIRON PRASAD MISHRA: \nSHRI VINAYAK BHAURAO RAUT: \nSHRI ARJUN LAL MEENA: \n \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether there has been slow progress of gauge conversion and \ndoubling of railway lines; \n \n(b)  if so, whether any study has been conducted for ascertaining the \nreasons behind slow progress of these works; \n \n(c)  if so, the details thereof; \n \n(d)  the present status of gauge conversion and doubling of railway lines \nprojects including gauge conversion pro ject of Kollam -Chenkotta \nduring the last three years; \n \n(e)  whether any monthly targets have been set for all the 17 railway \nzones under corrective measures and if so, the details thereof along \nwith the achievements reflected as a result thereof; and \n \n(f)  the manner and the extent to which these measures are likely to \nspeed up the works in Railways? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \n OF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \n MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) to (f):   A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n****** \n  \n\n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO ( f) OF UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 614 BY SHRI DHARMENDRA YADAV, SHRI KODIKUNNIL \nSURESH, SHRI BHAIRON PRASAD MISHRA, SHRI VINAYAK BHAURAO RAUT \nAND SHRI ARJUN LAL MEENA TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 20.07.2016 \nREGARDING GAUGE CONVERSION AND DOUBLING OF RAILWAY LINES \n \n(a) to (c):   The progress of commissioning of Gauge Conversion and \nDoubling Projects in last three years over Indian Railways is as given below:- \n \nYear Gauge Conversion (Km) Doubling (Km) \n2013-14 404 708 \n2014-15 527 705 \n2015-16 1042 972 \n \nFunds to the  ongoing Gauge Conversion and Doubling projects are \nallocated project-wise and zone -wise on year to year basis and allocation are \npresented alongwith cumulative expenditure in the form of Pink Book \nsubmitted to the Parliament along with the Budget Papers.  Project -wise \nbudget allotment is made as per availability of resources and progress of \nworks.  As the overall allocation was less in the past, all the projects could not \nbe allotted adequate funds, thereby affecting the progress adversely of  many \nprojects.  No special study has been carried out regarding progress of projects \nof Indian Railways. \n \n(d):   The status of gauge conversion and doubling projects  included in Works \nProgramme during the last three years i.e. 2013 -14, 2014-15 and 2015-16 is as \ngiven below:- \n \nPlah Head No. of Project (included in \nBudget in last three years) \nLength \n(in Km) \nLatest Cost \n(in Rs. Crores) \nGauge Conversion 2 176 821 \nDoubling 89 10,391 99,032 \n \n \n…2/- \n \n\n \n-2- \n \nThe present status of Kollam (Quilon)-Sengottai (Chenkotta) (95 Km) Gauge \nConversion project is as under:- \n \n(i)  Quilon -Punalur (45 Km) section is already commissioned.  Work has been \ntaken up on balance length Punalur-Kollam to Sengottai. \n \n(e) & (f):   Targets for Gauge Conversion and Doubling are fixed on yearly basis . \nOutlay for Gauge Conversion and Doubling Projects has been increased \nsubstantially in the last three years. However, to ensure steady progress \nthroughout the year and to address impediments, if any, faced by Zonal \nRailways, monthly monitoring is done for which such targets have also been \ncirculated.  \n \n******* "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |615", "t": "Bharat Net", "head": " \n  \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS \nDEPARTMENT OF TELECOMMUNICATIONS  \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.615  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20 TH  JULY, 2016 \n \nBHARAT NET \n \n615.  SHRI RAJESH RANJAN: \nSHRI KALIKESH N. SINGH DEO: \nSHRIMATI POONAMBEN MAADAM: \nSHRI RAM MOHAN NAIDU KINJARAPU: \nSHRI A.T. NANA PATIL: \nSHRI C.R. PATIL: \n \nWill the Minister of COMMUNICATIONS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the status of progress made under Bahrat Net P hase against the set target along with \nthe details of Gram Panchayats connected so far; \n \n(b)  whether the Government is considering the init iating of Phase II of the Bharat Net; \n \n(c)  whether any special feature is included for Ph ase II implementation in terms of \nstrengthening of Special Purpose Vehicle (SPV) as w ell as the monitoring mechanism and if \nso, the details thereof; \n \n(d)  whether the Government intends to engage any o ther agency/private sector in the \nprocess for efficient functioning and effective pro ject management and if so, the details \nthereof; and \n \n(e)  whether the Government has evaluated the perfo rmance of the three PSUs involved \nin the National Optical Fibre Network till date as compared to targets set, Statemwise and if so, \nthe details thereof, Statemwise and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (IC) OF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS & \n MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) BharatNet project is planned to be implemented in phases. Under PhasemI of the \nproject, 1 lakh Gram Panchayats (GPs) are to be con nected by laying underground OFC by \nMarch 2017. The status of progress made under  BharatNet PhasemI , as on 09.07.2016, is \ngiven below:m \n \nItems  Planned  Achieved  \nPipe laid (km) 2,30,000 1,50,540 \nOFC pulled (km) 2,30,000 1,25,642 \nPipe laid (Gram Panchayats) 1,00,000 64,875 \nOptical Fibre Network (OFC) pulled (Gram \nPanchayats) \n1,00,000 54,023 \nConnectivity provided (Gram Panchayats) 1,00,000 7,312 \n  \n(b) to (d) Under PhasemII of BharatNet project, it is planned to provide connectivity to \nremaining 1.5 lakh GPs in the country using an opti mal mix of underground fibre, fibre over \npower lines, radio and satellite media, by December, 2018. The salient features of BharatNet \nPhasemII in terms of strengthening of Special Purpo se Vehicle (SPV) i.e. BBNL and \nmonitoring mechanism are at Annexure-I. \n \n(e) The performance of all the three CPSUs is being  monitored regularly at various levels. \nStatemwise performance of CPSUs in implementation of BharatNet is at Annexure-II.  \n \n \nContdcelipsis2/m \n \n \n\n \n  \n \n \n \nm2m \n \n \n \nAnnexure-I\n \n \nSalient features of  BharatNet  Phase-II in terms of strengthening of Special Purpose  \nVehicle (SPV) i.e. BBNL and monitoring mechanism  \n \n(i) Indian Institute of Technology (IIT), Bombay ha s been engaged as consultant to \nprovide media plan for radio and satellite broadban d connectivity to GPs for Phase II \nand other technology issues. \n(ii) Indian Institute of Management (IIM), Ahmedaba d is being engaged to provide \nroadmap for reorganization of BBNL for efficient fu nctioning and effective project \nmanagement. \n(iii) World Bank is being engaged to provide projec t management framework, recommend \nstandards and good practices for BharatNet management and rural broadband \ndemand assessment study and development of marketing strategies \n(iv) Fresh recruitment of manpower for field operat ions and management \n(v) Monitoring Mechanism of BBNL has been strengthe ned in April, 2016 with the setting \nup monitoring and issues resolution by three committees:  \n \n1. Empowered Committee to review progress and resol ution of policy level \nimplementation issues &  to meet once in a month. \n2. Steering Committee for resolution of intermagency implementation matters, to meet \nevery fortnight.  \n3. Technical Standing Committee for deciding the te chnology related issues \npertaining to BharatNet implementation. \n \n(vi) Mobile application based GIS monitoring system  is being developed for  capturing \nmonitoring data at field level with mobile devices to be displayed on GIS maps in \nrealtime.   \n \n \n \n \n \nCondtcelipsis.3/m \n \n  \n\n \n  \n \n \n \n \nm3m \n \nAnnexure-II \n \n \nStatewise status of BharatNet as on  09.07.2016 \n \n \nS.No.  States/ UTs  Executing \nCPSU \nNo. of Gram \nPanchayats \n(GPs)- Phase I \nPipe \nlaid \n(kms.) \nOptical \nFibre Cable \n(OFC) laid \n(in kms)  \nNo. of \nGPs \nwhere \nOFC laid  \nNo. of \nGPs lit \n1 Andaman & Nicobar BSNL 69 0 0 0 0 \n2 Andhra Pradesh PGCIL 0 1913 19 0 0 \n3 Arunachal Pradesh RailTel 256 594 100 22 0 \n4 Assam BSNL 1013 1986 1887 707 156 \n5 Bihar  BSNL  5202  7928  6915  2597  215  \n6 Chandigarh BSNL 12 18 19 12 12 \n7 Chhattisgarh BSNL 2110 5207 4982 1684 602 \n8 Goa*  m m m m m \n9 Gujarat RailTel 5735 7005 5395 2479 139 \n10  Haryana  BSNL  6090  5633  5481  3399  168  \n11 Himachal Pradesh PGCIL 283 232 128 44 0 \n12 Jammu & Kashmir BSNL 624 253 240 103 0 \n13 Jharkhand PGCIL 1388 2895 2685 1062 156 \n14 Karna"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |616", "t": "RPF Strength", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 616 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nRPF STRENGTH \n \n†616.  SHRI SADASHIV LOKHANDE: \n        SHRI DUSHYANT CHAUTALA:  \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the present strength of personnel posted in the Railway \nProtection Force (RPF) is not adequate and a large number of \nrailway stations do not have women police personnel; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof ; \n \n(c) whether the Government had previously planned to place \nadequate number of women police in all railway station s across \nthe country;  \n \n(d) if so, the present status of the said proposal and the number of \npersonnel including women police posted in railway stations \nacross the country during the last three years; and \n \n(e) the details of the broad guidelines issued to RPF for the safety and \nsecurity of railway passengers and their luggage? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n (a) to ( d) : The present sanctioned strength of 75,879 of RPF staff is \nadequate as per present requirement, since the security in the \n\nRailways is looked after by Railway Protection Force (RPF), Govt. \nRailway Police (GRP) and local police.  \n With a view to increase the strength of women personnel in RPF, a \nprovision has been made to reserve 10% of the vacancies for women in \nall initial recruitments. 1014 women personnel have been recruited in \nlast 03 years and total strength of women personnel  has now been \nincreased from 1327 to 2341 at present.  \n  On an average approx 38798 Males and 1834 Females are deployed \non the Railway Stations across the country. \n  \n(e) Instructions for safety and security of Railway passengers and their \nluggage have been issued by Railway Board. In addition steps have also \nbeen taken by the Railways for the safety and security of Railway \npassengers. The guidelines cover the followings:-  \n1. Deployment of escort party of RPF in important trains for safety \nand security of passengers and their luggage. \n2. Deployment of special squad consisting of RPF personnel including \nwomen for women security.  \n3.  Help Line number 182 has been operationalised for providing \nsecurity related assistance round the clock to passengers. \n4. To coordinate wit h the GRP/Police authorities at all levels to \nensure proper registration and investigation of the case of crime. \n5. To launch regular drives under the provisions of the Railways Act, \n1989 to preven t unauthorized entry in trains and  in railway \npremises.  \n 6. Surveillance by CCTV at selected Railway stations to prevent    \ncrime.   \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |617", "t": "Inhuman Behaviour with Indians Abroad", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.617    \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nINHUMAN BEHAVIOUR WITH INDIANS ABROAD \n \n617.   SHRI RAHUL SHEWALE:  \nSHRI RAMDAS C. TADAS:  \nSHRI SANJAY DHOTRE:  \nSHRI BHARTRUHARI MAHTAB: \n \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether there has been an increase/ decrease in the cases of \nexploitation/torture of Indian workers working in other \ncountries; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof along with the number of such cases \nreported upon across the world during each of the last three \nyears and the current year, country-wise; \n \n(c) whether the Government has also received complaints about \nphysical and sexual abuse of domestic workers working in \nother countries during the said period;  \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof, country-wise; \n \n(e) whether the Government has taken up the issue with the \nforeign countries concerned; and  \n \n(f) if so, the details and the outcome thereof? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n[GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD)] \n \n(a) & (b) Information regarding Indian workers holding ECR \nPassports, going for overseas employment to 18 notified Emigration \nCheck Required (ECR) countries (Afghanistan, Bahrain, Indonesia, \nIraq, Jordan, Kuwait, Lebanon, Libya, Mal aysia, Oman, Qatar, North \nSudan, South Sudan, Syria, Thailand, the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, \n\nUnited Arab Emirates and Yemen), is maintained by this Ministry. As \nper information available with the Indian Missions/Posts in ECR \ncountries, there is no general pattern to indicate an increase in \ncases of exploitation/ torture of Indian workers. Details of \ncomplaints received during the last three years and current year are \nat Annexure. \n \n(c) & (d)   Most of the complaints received from Indian workers,  \nincluding  domestic workers, from time to time, are generally in the \nnature of non -payment/ delayed payment or underpayment of \nsalaries, long working hours, inadequate living conditions, physical \nharassment, non-renewal of visa and labour card on time, refusal to \npay for the medical treatment, denial of leave and air -ticket to the \nhometown on completion of contract period, forcible custody of \nPassport and Visa, refusal of leave or ‘exit/re -entry permits’/‘final \nexit visa’ etc. No specific complaint of sexual abuse has  been \nreported by the Missions.   \n \nSuch complaints are addressed by the Indian Missions by \ntaking them up with the concerned foreign authorities , Foreign \nEmployers or the officials of the Labour Ministry of that country.   \n \n(e) & (f)   Whenever the Indian Missions are approached by any \nIndian national in distress, the same is followed up, at various \nlevels, with the authorities concerned in the Governments of the \nrespective country.  In addition, Government of India has signed \nMoUs with 6 Gulf countries, na mely UAE, Qatar, Kuwait, Oman, \nBahrain, Kingdom of Saudi Arabia and Malaysia. As per these MoUs, \nthe host country will take measures for protection and welfare of \nthe workers in organized sector. The recruitment and terms of \nemployment will be in conformit y with the laws of both the \ncountries. \n  \nThese MOUs are renewed / signed afresh, from time to time, \nduring which process any modifications are duly considered for \ninclusion. \n \n The Government of India has set up Indian Community Welfare \nFund (ICWF) in all t he Indian Missions/consulates abroad to meet \ncontingency expenditure incurred by them for carrying out various \nwelfare activities for overseas Indian citizens who are in distress. \nThe objectives of the ICWF include:- \n  \n\n(i) Boarding and lodging for distressed O verseas Indians in \nneed; \n \n(ii) Extending emergency medical care to the Overseas Indians \nin need; \n \n(iii) Providing air passage to stranded Overseas Indians in need; \n \n(iv) Providing initial legal assistance to the Overseas Indians in \ndeserving cases; \n \n(v) Expenditure on incidentals and for airlifting the mortal \nremains to India or local cremation/burial of the deceased \nOverseas Indians in such cases where the sponsor is unable \nor unwilling to do so as per the contract and the family is \nunable to meet the cost; \n \n(vi) Providing the payment of penalties in respect of Indian \nnationals for illegal stay in the host country where prima \nfacie the worker is not at fault; \n \n(vii) Providing the payment of small fines/penalties for the release \nof Indian nationals in jail/detention centre; \n \n The Ministry has set up a 24X7 Helpline ‘Overseas Workers \nResource Centre (OWRC)’ based in Gurgaon, Haryana which provides \ninformation and guidance on all matters and problems pertaining to \noverseas employment of Indian nationals.  Indian Workers Resource \nCentre (IWRC) set up in Dubai by Embassy of India, in UAE, provides \nguidance and counseling on all matters pertaining to overseas \nIndian workers in UAE. Shelter homes for distressed Indian \nnationals, have been set up in"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |618", "t": "Attack on Indians", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.618 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nATTACK ON INDIANS \n \n618.     KUMARI SUSHMITA DEV:  \nSHRI JYOTIRADITYA M. SCINDIA: \n \n Will the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is aware that the recent spate of attacks \nagainst the African community in India and reprisal attacks against \nIndians in Africa has invited Global attention; \n \n(b)    if so, the details thereof and whether the Union Govern ment has \nfailed in preventing such attacks on Africans;  \n \n(c) If so, the reasons therefor; and  \n \n(d) the steps taken by the Government to ensure safety of students \nfrom Africa in various parts of the country? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n(SHRI M.J. AKBAR) \n \n(a) to (c) The recent incidents relating to the members of African \ncommunity in India were not premeditated acts against a particular \ncommunity. These were spontaneous attacks perpetrated by anti -social \nand criminal e lements.  Two of the three perpetrators of the killing of \nCongolese national were swiftly apprehended. Government of Democratic \nRepublic of Congo also acted swiftly to control reprisal attacks against \nIndians in Kinshasa. India’s historical relations with Africa rest on the \nfoundation of brotherhood and solidarity  and such incidents cannot be \nallowed to deflect from India’s historical friendship and close \ndevelopment partnership with Africa.  \n \n(d)  Ministry of External Affairs proactively reached out to the  African \ndiplomatic and student community. It was requested that police \npatrolling be increased in areas where sizeable African community  \nresides. It has also been decided to hold regular meetings with the \nAfrican community in all major metropolitan cities . The State \ngovernments, having large numbers of African nationals,  have also been \nrequested to take steps to ensure their safety and security. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |619", "t": "Welfare Schemes for Minorities", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.619 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nWelfare Schemes for Minorities \n \n \n 619.  SHRI DHARAMBIR: \nSHRI GEORGE BAKER: \nDR. MANOJ RAJORIA: \nSHRI P.K. BIJU: \n \n \n Will the Minister of MINORITY AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of various schemes under implementation for the welfare of minorities; \n \n(b) the funds allocated/released/spent for implementation of these schemes during each of the last \nthree years and the current year, scheme-wise, State/UT-wise; \n \n(c)  the targets fixed/achieved and the number of persons benefitted under these schemes during \nthe above period, State/UT-wise, scheme-wise; and \n \n(d) the steps taken by the Government for speedy implementation and to achieve the targets  under \nthe said schemes and to create awareness about such schemes? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE MINISTRY OF \nMINORITY AFFAIRS \n(SHRI MUKHTAR ABBAS NAQVI) \n \n(a) to (c) This Ministry implements the following schemes for the welfare of minorities:  \n(i) The Multi-sectoral Development Programme (MsDP)  aims at improving the socio -\neconomic condition and providing basic amenities for improving the quality of life of minorities. \nThe State/UT wise details of fund released during the last three years and current year is at \nAnnexure -I. \n  \nNo physical targets are fixed by this  Ministry under MsDP. Projects are approved on the basis of \nthe project proposals received from the States/UTs as per their requirement s. Under MsDP, assets \nare created for the welfare of the community as a whole and not for individuals. \n \n(ii) Pre-matric Scholarship Scheme - The scholarship is provided to  minority students \nstudying in C lass I to X in recognized Government/Private schools. Minimum 30% \nscholarships are earmarked for girls.  \n\n(iii) Post-matric Scholarship Scheme - The scholarship is provided to  minority students \nstudying in C lass XI to Ph.D level in recognized Government/Private \nschools/Colleges/Institutes. Minimum 30% scholarships are earmarked for girls.  \n The State/UT -wise details of funds released and Scholarships granted under the Pre-matric \nScholarship Scheme and Post -matric Scholarship Scheme may please be seen at Annexure \n–II.  \n(iv) Merit-cum-Means based Scholarship Scheme - The merit -cum-means scholarship \nscheme is awarded for pursuing professional and technical courses, at under -graduate and \npost-graduate levels, in institutions recognized by the appropriate authority. Under the \nscheme, 30% of these scholarships are earmarked for girl students. 85 institutes for \nprofessional and technical courses have been listed in the scheme.  \nThe State/UT -wise details of funds released and Scholarships granted under the Scheme \nmay please be seen at Annexure – III.  \n \n(v)    Maulana Azad National Fellowship - The objective of th e Fellowship is to provide \nintegrated five year fellowships in the form of financial assistance to students from \nminority communities to pursue higher studies such as M.Phil and Ph.D. It is implemented \nthrough University Grant s Commission (UGC). Fellowship s are awarded  to research \nstudents pursuing regular and full time M.Phil and Ph.D. courses.  \nThe State/UT -wise details of funds released and Scholarships granted under the Scheme \nmay please be seen at Annexure – IV.  \n \n(vi)  Free Coaching & Allied Scheme - The objectives of the scheme are to assist students \nbelonging to the minority communities by way of special coaching for (a) qualifying \nexaminations for admission in technical/ professional courses such as engineering, law, \nmedical, management, informatio n technology etc. (b) Competitive examinations for \nrecruitment to Group „A‟ , „B‟ and „C‟ services and other equivalent posts under the \nCentral and State governments including public sector undertakings, banks, insurance \ncompanies as well as autonomous bodies.  \nThe State/UT -wise details of funds released and Scholarships granted under the Scheme \nmay please be seen at Annexure – V.  \n \n(vii) Support to minority candidates clearing Prelims conducted by UPSC/SSC, State \nPublic Service Commission (PSC) etc. - The objective of the Scheme is to provide \nfinancial support to the minority candidates clearing prelims conducted by Union Public \nService Commission, Staff Selection Commission and State Public Service Commissions \nto adequately equip them to compete for appoi ntment to Civil Services in the Union and \nthe State Governments and to increase th e representation of the minorities  in the Civil \nServices by giving direct financial support to candidates clearing Preliminary Examination  \nof Group A and B (Gazetted and no n-Gazetted posts of Union Public Service Commission \n(UPSC); State Public Service Commissions (SPSCs) and Staff Selection Commission \n(SSC) etc.  \n\n(viii) Padho Pardesh - Interest Subsidy on Educational Loans for overseas studies - The \nobjective of the scheme i s to a"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |620", "t": "Railway University", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 620 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nRAILWAY UNIVERSITY \n \n620.    SHRI RAOSAHEB DANVE PATIL : \n  SHRI GEORGE BAKER : \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the present status of the  railway university proposed to be set \nup in the country; \n \n(b) the details of the funds earmarked for the purpose; \n \n(c) the details of the expenditure likely to be incurred thereon along \nwith the resources from where it is proposed to be raised; \n \n(d) whether some foreign countries have offered assistance for this \npurpose; \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof and the steps taken by the Railways in \nthis regard; and \n \n(f) the time-frame fixed, if any, for setting up the university? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) Ministry of Railways have decided to establish one Railway \nUniversity by   upgrading   National   Academy  of   Indian  Railways  at  \nContd…2/- \n\n-2- \n \nVadodara and by incorporating the existing Centralised Training \nInstitutes of Indian Railways as Constituent Schools of Study. \n \n(b) A token outlay of ₹ 10 lakhs has been provided in the Railway \nBudget 2016-17 for this purpose. \n \n(c) A capital cost of ₹ 861 crores is envisaged for the University. \nHowever, details of expenditure likely to be incurred and resources for \nthe proposed University have not been worked out at this stage. \n \n(d) No, Madam.  \n \n(e) Does not arise. \n \n(f) No time frame has been fixed. \n \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |621", "t": "Rail Victim Compensation Fund", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 621 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \n        RAIL VICTIM COMPENSATION FUND \n \n621.     SHRI GUTHA SUKENDER REDDY: \n   SHRI SANGANNA AMARAPPA: \n    SHRI ABHISHEK SINGH: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state : \n \n(a) whether the Government has received any proposal of creating \nRail Victim Compensation Fund to provide compensation to the \npersons suffered under rail accidents; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) the further action taken by the Government in this regard; \n \n(d)  the details of guidelines regarding payment of compensation to \nthe rail accident victims; and \n \n(e)    the details of accidents that took place during the last two years \nand the current year due to poor maintenance of ra ilway lines and the \naction taken by the Railways in this regard? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n ( SHRI MANOJ SINHA ) \n \n(a) to (e) : A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n**** \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 621 BY SHRI GUTHA SUKENDER REDDY, \nSHRI SANGANNA AMARAPPA AND SHRI ABHISHEK SINGH TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 20.07. 2016 REGARDING RAIL VICTIM \nCOMPENSATION FUND \n \n(a) to (c) : Yes Madam. A representation has recently been received \nfrom an Hon’ble Member of Parliament proposing creation of Rail \nVictim Compensation Fund to provide adequate compensation to \nvictims of rail a ccidents by levy of an additional charge on passenger \nfare. The proposal contained in the representation is under \nexamination in this Ministry. \n \n(d) : In terms of Section 125 of the Railways Act, 1989, and Section 16 \nof the Railway Claims Tribunal Act, 198 7, the claimant of the \ncompensation for death/injury in Train Accident / Untoward Incident \nhas to move an application for compensation in the Railway Claims \nTribunal.  The compensation is paid by the Railways after a decree is \nawarded by the Tribunal in fa vour of the claimant subject to \nsatisfaction of Railway. \n      Time limit for filing claims for train accident is one year from the \ndate of occurrence which can be condoned by the Railway Claim \nTribunal, if sufficient reason is shown. \n \n                ...2/- \n\n \n-2- \n(e) : Number of consequential train accidents on Engineering account \nthat took place during the last two years and the current year upto \n15.07.2016 is given below:- \nYear Responsibility Total \n2014-15 \nOn Engineering Account 27 \nEngineering dept. jointly with other Dept. 9 \nGrand Total 36 \n2015-16 \nOn Engineering Account 26 \nEngineering dept. jointly with other Dept. 12 \nGrand Total 38 \n2016-17 \n(Up to 15th \nJuly, 2016) \nOn Engineering Account 8 \nEngineering dept. jointly with other Dept. 1 \nGrand Total 9 \n \n       Measures are being undertaken on continuing basis for upkeep of \ntracks to prevent accidents which includes replacement of over -aged \nassets, adoption to suitable technologies for up -gradation and \nmaintenance of track. Safety drives and inspections at  regular \nintervals are carried out to monitor and educate staff for observance \nof safe practices. \n**** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |622", "t": "Rail Connectivity with Neighbouring Countries", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION  NO. 622 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \n \nRAIL CONNECTIVITY WITH NEIGHBOURING COUNTRIES \n \n \n622. SHRI S. SELVAKUMARA CHINNAYAN: \n SHRI P. NAGARAJAN: \n   \n \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)   whether the Railways has any proposal to connect India by rail with \nChina through Tibet and Nepal in the near future; \n \n(b)   if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c)   the time by which the said proposal is likely to be implemented? \n \n \nANSWER \n \n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n \n \n \n \n    (SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n \n \n(a):  No, Madam.   \n \n(b) & (c):  Do not arise. \n \n \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |623", "t": "Railway Projects", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.623 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nRAILWAY PROJECTS \n \n623.  DR. KULAMANI SAMAL: \nSHRI KIRTI AZAD: \nSHRI M. RAJA MOHAN REDDY: \nSHRI RAJU SHETTY: \nSHRIMATI NEELAM SONKER: \nSHRI P.K. BIJU: \nSHRI ALOK SANJAR: \nSHRI RAVINDRA KUMAR PANDEY: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n (a)  the details of the railway projects sanctioned during the last two years and \nthe current year, Zone/State-wise, project-wise and year-wise; \n  \n(b)  the present status of various new/ongoing/pending railway projects and \nsurveys in the country during the above period, Zone/State-wise and project-\nwise; \n  \n(c)  the funds allocated and expenditure incurred on each of the projects during \nthe said period, Zone/State-wise, project -wise and year-wise;  \n \n(d)  whether the Railways proposes to give more financial assistance to the rail \nprojects in the States particularly in Kerala and if so, the details thereof;   \n(e)  whether the Railways has received complaints reg arding substandard and \nlow grade materials being used in some rail projects in the country including \nOdisha and if so, the details thereof and the action taken thereon;  \n(f)  whether the Railways has constituted any committee to monitor the \nimplementation of these projects and if so, the details thereof; and  \n(g)  the steps taken/being taken by the Railways for expeditious completion of \nsuch projects?  \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \n OF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \n MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n  \n(a) to (g):   A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n****** \n\n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO ( g) OF UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 623 BY DR. KULAMANI SAMAL, SHRI KIRTI AZAD, SHRI M. \nRAJA MOHAN REDDY, SHRI RAJU SHETTY, SHRIMATI NEELAM SONKER, SHRI \nP.K. BIJU, SHRI ALOK SANJAR AND SHRI RAVINDRA KUMAR PANDEY TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 20.07.2016 REGARDING RAILWAY PROJECTS \n \n(a) to (c):   Details of all those railway projects sanctioned during the last two \nyears and the current year i.e. 2014 -15, 2015 -16 & 2016 -17 including Cost, \nLength, Fund allotment, Expenditure etc. are available in public domain on \nIndian Railways website i.e. www.indianr ailways.gov.in and are also available \nin Pink Book s presented before the House alongwith Budget papers  for all \nthese years.   \n \n(d):   Funds to the various railway projects are allocated project -wise and \nzone-wise on year to year basis and allocation s are presented alongwith \ncumulative expenditure in the form of Pink Book submitted to the House along \nwith the Budget Papers.  Project -wise budget allotment is made as per \navailability of resources  and progress of work .  In particular , allocation of    \n`45 Crore for new line, `181 Crore for Gauge Conversion and `790 Crore for \nDoubling projects falling fully/partly in State of Kerala have been made in Rail \nBudget 2016-17.   \n \n(e):   System is in place to ensure quality control in execution of projects.  \nTherefore, adherence to q uality in railway projects is a continuous process.  \nComplaints regarding use of substandard material in railway projects, \nwhenever received, are investigated / inquired into and corrective action  and \nsystem improvement, if any, are taken as required.   \n \n(f):   No separate committee has been framed to monitor the implementation \nof railway projects.  The monitoring is done  at different levels from field units \nto Railway Board and above at regular intervals.   \n…2/- \n\n \n-2- \n \n(g):   Some other steps taken/being taken by the Government for effective and \nspeedy implementation of rail projects in the country are (i) substantial \nincrease in allocation of funds, (ii) prioritization of projects, (iii) delegation  of \npowers at field level, (iv) regular co-ordination meetings with State \nGovernments for land acquisition, relocation of utilities, etc. \n \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |624", "t": "Clearances to Railway Projects", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.624 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \n \nCLEARANCES TO RAILWAY PROJECTS \n \n \n624.  SHRI BHARTRUHARI MAHTAB: \nSHRI SANJAY DHOTRE: \nSHRI RAHUL SHEWALE: \n \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n \n(a)  the number of railway projects stalled due to lack of clearances \nfrom the department of environment/forest along with the amount \nstuck therein across the country, as on date, Zone/State/Union \nterritory-wise; \n  \n(b)  whether the Railways have suffered losses on  account of being \ndormant in earning revenue from such projects and their cost \nescalation over a period of time; \n  \n(c)  if so, the details thereof, project-wise and the reasons therefor along \nwith the reaction of the Railways thereto; \n  \n(d)  whether the Ra ilways did not obtain prior clearances from the \ndepartment of environment/forest for these projects; and \n  \n(e)  if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?  \n  \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \n OF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \n MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) to (e):   A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n****** \n\n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF UNSTARRED QUESTION \nNO. 624 BY SHRI BHARTRUHARI MAHTAB, SHRI SANJAY DHOTRE AND SHRI RAHUL \nSHEWALE TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 20.07.2016 REGARDING \nCLEARANCES TO RAILWAY PROJECTS \n \n(a) to (c): Clearances from different land owning agencies, acquisition of land, shifting \nof services/utilities are part of project execution and these activities are bound to \ntake some time.  However, following projects have suffered due to non availability of \nforest clearances.   \nS. \nNo. \nState Railway Name of the Project \n1 Bihar  Eastern Doubling between Ratanpur-Jamalpur \n(Part of Munger Bridge approach track) \n2 Jharkhand East Central Tori- Shivpur-Kathautia New Line \n3 Bihar  East Central Sakri -Biraul-Kusheshwarsthan-\nHasanpur Road New Line \n4 Odisha  East Coast Angul-Sukhinda Road New Line \n5 Odisha  East Coast Byepass line bet. Sukhinda Road and \nJajpur Keonjhar Road \n6 Sikkim, West \nBengal \nNortheast Frontier Sivok-Rangpo New Line \n7 Assam Northeast Frontier New Moynaguri-Jogighopa New Line \n8 Kerala Southern Angamali - Sabarimala New Line \n9 Maharashtra South Central Ratlam-Khandwa-Akola Gauge \nConversion \n10 Chhattisgarh South East Central Gondia-Jabalpur Gauge Conversion \n11 Chhatisgarh South East Central Dallirajahara-Rowghat New Line \n12 Chhatisgarh South East Central Salka Road- Annupur Doubling \n13 Karnataka  South Western Hubli-Ankola New Line \n14 Karnataka  South Western Bangalore- Satyamangalam  New Line \n15 Madhya Pradesh \n& Uttar Pradesh \nWest Central Lalitpur-Singrauli New Line \n \nWorking out cost escalation o r revenue loss on account of delay in forest \nclearance alone is not feasible to be worked out.  \n \n(d) & (e):   Railway being one of the most environment friendly means of transport \ndoes not require environment clearance for undertaking projects .  Proposal fo r \ndiversion of forest land and tree cutting, wherever needed , can only be prepared \nonly after detailed survey, pegging of alignment and preparation of land schedule.   \n \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |625", "t": "Indian Sailors Killed in Oman", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.625 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nINDIAN SAILORS KILLED IN OMAN \n \n625.   SHRI P. NAGARAJAN: \n \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether 2 Indian sailors were killed  and 3 people including pilot \nwere injured during the recent oil tanker fire at the port of Oman; \n \n(b)   if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c)   whether the Indian Embassy in Oman has provided necessary \nassistance to those Indians killed and injured in the accident;  \n \n(d)   if so, the details thereof; \n \n(e)  whether the Government has taken up this issue with the Oman \nauthority and the shipping company to provide due compensation to \nthose Indians who died in the fire; and  \n \n(f)    if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n[GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD)] \n \n(a) & (b) Yes. Two Indian crew members died and three other crew \nmembers suffered burn injuries when an oil tanker caught fire in the \nengine room while at a dock on the border between Oman and Yemen. \n  \n(c) & (d) The Embassy of India in Oman facilitated the transportation \nand airlifting of mortal remains of the two crew members  to India and the \ntreatment of the injured crew members was carried out in Royal Hospital, \nSalalah by the managing company M/s Etihad Engin eering & Marine \nServices, UAE. \n  \n(e) & (f) M/s Etihad Engineering & Marine Services, UAE  has informed \nthe Embassy of India  in Oman that the compensation for the crew \nmembers, who died in the accident in the Engine room of the oil tanker , \nhas been paid by them to their families. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |626", "t": "Director Level Officers", "head": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF PERSONNEL, PUBLIC GRIEVANCES AND PENSIONS \n(DEPARTMENT OF PERSONNEL & TRAINING) \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 626 \n(TO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016) \n \nDIRECTOR LEVEL OFFICERS \n \n†626. SHRI VISHNU DAYAL RAM: \n \nWill the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the actual number of officers serving as Directors in Indian Administrative Service \nwho belong to Scheduled Castes (SC)/Scheduled Tribes (ST); \n \n(b)  whether the officers belonging to SC/ST have not been included in the Joint Secretary \npanel with their colleagues from the same batch; \n \n(c)  if so, the number of such officers along with the reasons therefor; and \n \n(d)  the number of officers belonging to SC/ST wh o have been included in the panel for \nthe post of Joint Secretary during the last three years? \n \nANSWER \n \nMinister of State in the Ministry of Personnel, Public Grievances and Pensions and Minister \nof State in the Prime Minister’s Office. (DR. JITENDRA SINGH) \n(a):   Presently, there are 38 IAS officers working at Director level in Government of India \nunder the Central Staffing Scheme; of which 6 officers belong to SC category and 1 officer \nbelongs to ST Category. \n \n(b) to (d):   The Panels for appointment at J oint Secretary level are prepared on the basis of \nexperience, suitability for appropriate consideration of Civil Services Board out of the \nofficers empanelled to hold Joint Secretary level posts including SC & ST officers. Further, \nin the last three years,  total 29 IAS officers from SC category and 15 IAS officers from ST \ncategory have been empanelled for holding Joint Secretary level posts at the Centre. Further, \nat present, 20 SC and 7 ST IAS officers are working at Joint Secretary level in various \nMinistries/Departments of Government of India under the Central Staffing Scheme. \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |627", "t": "Under Water Robot", "head": " \n                                             \n                                           GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EARTH SCIENCES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 627 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON WEDNESDAY, JULY 20, 2016 \n \nUNDER WATER ROBOT \n \n627. DR. MANOJ RAJORIA: \n \n        Will the Minister of EARTH SCIENCES be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has formulated a scheme/project to deploy under \nwater robots in the Bay of Bengal; \n(b)  if so, the details thereof and its likely benefits to the general public and farmers; \n(c)   whether foreign assistance is being sought for the said project; and \n(d)    if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR MINISTRY OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY AND  \nMINISTRY OF EARTH SCIENCES \n(SHRI Y. S. CHOWDARY) \n \n(a) No Madam. However, an Ocean Glider has been deployed. \n(b) In order to improve the oceanographic observation data in the Bay of Bengal  as \napart of ongoing Ocean Observing System Program , a Glider has been acquired \nby the Indian National Center for Ocean Information services (INCOIS), \nHyderabad. Ocean Glider, an au tonomous, unmanned underwater vehicle  is, \nused to measure various oceanographic parameters such as temperature, \nsalinity, chlorophyll and photosynthetically active radiation along a desired \ntrack in the upper 1000 m of water column. At the end of each dive -and-climb \nphase Glider transmit collected data to the base -station at land via satellite \ntelemetry. Repeated hydrographic survey in the international waters of the \nnorthern Bay of Bengal (18°N, 89.5°E) were conducted during the period of 3 rd \nSeptember, 2015 to 10 th January, 2016 using this Glider and the vehicle has \nbeen successfully recovered after the mission.  Gliders are also used recently \nduring the joint research campaign between India and United Kingdom (U.K.) \nover the Bay of Bengal to understand monsoon ocean process. \n \nOverall improvement to the monsoon forecast will help the economic growth \nparticularly though improved incomes to the larger community depending on \nagricultural activities.  \n(c-d) As the Glider technology  is new , three s cientists from INCOIS have been \ndeputed for two week Glider training at Kongsberg Underwater Technology inc., \nLynnwood, Seattle, USA and Applied Physics Laboratory (APL), University of \nWashington, Seattle, USA. Moreover, during the initial phase of Glider mission, \nINCOIS scientist operated the vehicle under the supervision of APL scientists \nand the team is successfully completed the glider mission outside Indian \nexclusive economic zone (EEZ).  \n \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |628", "t": "Electrification of Railway Line", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS  \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 628 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nELECTRIFICATION OF RAILWAY LINE  \n \n628.  SHRIMATI P.K. SREEMATHI TEACHER:        \n            \n        Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)   whether there is inordinate delay in completion of electrification  \nof Kozhikode-Mangalore railway line; \n \n(b)    if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor; and \n \n(c)   the  steps taken by the Railways for the speedy completion of  \nabove work and the time by which the said project is likely to be \ncompleted? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n (SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a): No, Madam. \n \n(b): Does not arise. \n \n(c):Shoranur-Kozhikode-Charvattur section has already been \ncommissioned on electric traction and electrification of Charvattur -\nMangalore section is planned for commissioning by Decemb er 2016. \nFurther t o expedite electrification  of Kozhikode -Mangalore railway \nline, improved project monitoring mechanism has been introduced and \nadequate funding through Extra Budgetary Resources (Institutional \nFinance) has been provided.   \n******* \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |629", "t": "Science and Technology Demonstration Centres", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY \nDEPARTMENT OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.629 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20/07/2016 \n \nSCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY DEMONSTRATION CENTRES \n \n629. SHRI C. MAHENDRAN: \n \nWill the Minister of SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY òãðìððÐð ¡ðøÜ ÑßðøÌðð÷ò±ð¨îó Ùðüëðó \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to develop Science and Technology demonstration \ncentres in all districts to impart scientific temper among students and people;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the locations identified for the purpose; \n \n(c) the benefits likely to accrue therefrom; \n \n(d) whether any special Science and Technology projects/schemes are proposed in various \nStates including the State of Tamil Nadu; and  \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EARTH SCIENCES \n(SHRI Y.S. CHOWDARY) \nòãðìððÐð ¡ðøÜ ÑßðøÌðð÷ò±ð¨îó ÙðüëððâðÚð Ùð÷ü Üð¸Úð Ùðüëðó +ÉÉè® ÑðöÆãðó òãðìððÐð ÙðüëððâðÚð Ùð÷ü Üð¸Úð Ùðüëðó \n (gÉÉÒ ´ÉÉ<Ç. AºÉ. SÉÉèvÉ®ÉÒ) \n \n \n(a) No, Madam. \n \n(b) & (c):   Do not arise. \n  \n(d) No, Madam.  \n \n(e) Does not arise. \n \n****** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |630", "t": "Attack on African Nationals in India", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.630 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nATTACK ON AFRICAN NATIONALS IN INDIA \n \n630.     SHRI HUKUM SINGH: \n \n Will the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether African diplomats have boycotted some events scheduled by the \nIndian Council for Cultural Relations (ICCR) recently in Delhi and if so, the \ndetails thereof; \n \n(b)    whether the Government did an outreach event with African students \nalong with concerned embassies to reassure them of safety and would \nmeet the African Heads of Mission every three months and if so, the \ndetails thereof;  \n \n(c) whether the African Group of Heads of Mission also decided to \nrecommend to their Government not to send new students to India due to \nstereotyping and racial prejudice due to the recent murder of the \nCongolese students in India and if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(d) the present status of the safety and security of African nationals in India? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n(SHRI M.J. AKBAR) \n \n(a)  No. African diplomats did not boycott some events scheduled by the \nIndian Council for Cultural Relations (ICCR) recently in Delhi. African diplomats \nparticipated in the “Africa Day” celebrations organized by ICCR on 26 May \n2016.  \n \n(b)    Yes, Hon’ble  External Affairs Minister, Minister of State for External \nAffairs and senior officials met African diplomatic and student community to \nassure them of their safety and security . Minister of State of External Affairs \nwould be having a quarterly meeting with the African Heads of Mission.  \n \n(c) No. I t has not come to our notice. African Heads of Mission have \nexpressed their appreciation for the prompt action taken by G overnment of \nIndia related to recent spontaneous and isolated incidents against members of \nthe African community. \n \n(d) The State governments, having large numbers of African nationals, have \nbeen requested to take steps to ensure their safety and security and to \nincrease police patrolling in areas where sizeable African community resides. \nIt has al so been decided to hold regular meetings with the African community \nin all major metropolitan cities.  \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |631", "t": "IT Companies", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ELECTRONICS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 631 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON: 20.07.2016 \n \n \nIT COMPANIES \n \n631.  DR. K. KAMARAJ: \n \nWill the Minister of Electronics & Information technology be pleased to state: - \n \n(a) the number of registered Information Technology (IT) companies functioning in  the \ncountry as on date, State-wise; \n(b) whether more than 50% of the companies working in the field of IT sector are not \nregistered; \n(c) if so, the reaction of the Government thereto; \n(d) whether revenue loss as a result thereof to the exchequer has been assessed; and \n(e) if so, the details thereof? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER  OF STATE FOR MINISTRY OF ELECTRONICS AND \nINFORMATION TECHNOLOGY (SHRI P.P. CHAUDHARY) \n  \n \n(a): As per the Ministry of Corporate Affairs (MCA),  Government of India, the number of \nregistered IT Companies functioning in the country as on 30.06.2016 is 95,084.  The State/UT \nwise list of Registered IT Companies is given in Annexure.     \n \n(b): As per the  MCA, information of companies working in the field of IT sector not registered \nwith Registrar of Companies is not maintained.  \n \n(c) to (e): Do not arise. \n******* \n \n  \n\n  \nAnnexure \n \nState/UT-wise number of Active IT Companies in India as on 30.06.2016 \nSl. No. State Number \n1 A&N Islands 4 \n2 Andhra Pradesh 4,250 \n3 Arunachal Pradesh 3 \n4 Assam 189 \n5 Bihar 764 \n6 Chandigarh 846 \n7 Chhattisgarh 278 \n8 Daman and Diu 4 \n9 Delhi 16,427 \n10 Dadar Nagar Haveli 5 \n11 Goa 170 \n12 Gujarat 3,616 \n13 Himachal Pradesh 173 \n14 Haryana 2,249 \n15 Jharkhand 392 \n16 Jammu and Kashmir 245 \n17 Karnataka 13,117 \n18 Kerala 3,439 \n19 Lakshadweep - \n20 Maharashtra 14,949 \n21 Meghalaya 16 \n22 Manipur 22 \n23 Madhya Pradesh 1,681 \n24 Mizoram 2 \n25 Nagaland 8 \n26 Orissa 1,007 \n27 Punjab 828 \n28 Pondicherry 143 \n29 Rajasthan 2,264 \n30 Sikkim - \n31 Telangana 10,285 \n32 Tamil Nadu 9,416 \n33 Tripura 25 \n34 Uttar Pradesh 3,806 \n35 Uttarakhand 292 \n36 West Bengal 4,169 \nTotal 95,084 \nNote:  IT Companies are those having First three digits of Activity Code (NIC-2004) amongst \n\n(721,722,723,724,725 and 729) \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |632", "t": "Conversion of Railway Stations", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.632 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nCONVERSION OF RAILWAY STATIONS \n \n632.  ADV. NARENDRA KESHAV SAWAIKAR: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n      \n(a) whether the Railways has identified a few railway stations for \nconversion into world class stations; \n(b) if so, the details thereof along with the criteria for selection \nof these stations; and \n \n(c) whether the Railways intends to rope in corporations with \nNon-Governmental Organizations (NGOs) and Non -Resident \nIndians (NRIs) in the programme in view of financial crunch and \nif so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n \n(a) to (c): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n**** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFE RRED IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.  632 BY ADV. NARENDRA KESHAV \nSAWAIKAR TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 20.07.2016 \nREGARDING CONVERSION OF RAILWAY STATIONS. \n(a)&(b): Indian Railway has advertised its plan to redevelop ‘A-1’ and \n‘A’ category stations (about 400 in number)  which are generally \nlocated in metros, major cities, pilgrimage centres and important \ntourist destinations on ‘as is where is’ basis, by inviting proposals \nfrom interested parties with their designs and business ideas. The \nentire cost of station redevelopment is to be met by leveraging \ncommercial development  of land and air space in and around the \nstations.   \n(c)  Railways have issued guidelines for provision, augmentation and \nimprovement of passenger amenities at railway stations through \nindividuals, NGOs, Trusts, Charitable Institutions, Corporations etc.  \nThese guidelines have also been sent to High Commission/Embassy \nof United States of America, United Kingdom, Canada and Australia \nwith a view to elicit cooperation from Non -Resident Indians (NRIs) \nin this regard. \n \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |633", "t": "Capacity Building in IT", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ELECTRONICS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 633 \n                                         TO BE ANSWERED ON: 20.07.2016 \n \nCAPACITY BUILDING IN  IT \n  \n633.  SHRI RAMESH BIDHURI: \n \nWill the Minister of Electronics and Information Technology be pleased to state: - \n(a)     whether the Government has made a road -map for capacity building in the field of rural \nIT infrastructure;   \n(b)      if so, the details thereof; and \n(c) the steps taken to strengthen the digital education in rural areas particularly among the \nrural youths? \nANSWER \n  \nMINISTER  OF STATE FOR MINISTRY OF ELECTRONICS AND \nINFORMATION TECHNOLOGY (SHRI P.P. CHAUDHARY) \n \n(a) to (c) :  Yes, Sir. The Government of India has undertaken following initiatives for capacity \nbuilding in field of rural IT infrastructure: \n \ni)  National Optical Fibre Network (NOFN):  The Government  has approved, ' National \nOptical Fibre Network (NOFN)/BharatNet' , to establish network infrastructure to connect all the \nGram Panchayats (2.5 lakh) in the country by laying incremental fibre to bridge the connectivity \ngap between Gram Panchayats and Blocks or through radio/satellite for providing broadband  \nconnectivity. It is being implemented through a Special Purpose Vehicle (SPV), Bharat \nBroadband Network Limited (BBNL).  Till June,2016 more than 50,465 Gram Panchayats (GPs) \nhave been connected with OFC.  \n \nii)  Under Digital India programme, the Government ha s launched CSC 2.0 Scheme to set up \nat least one Common Service Centre (CSC) to cover all the 2.5 lakh Gram Panchayats of the \nCountry for delivery of various electronic services to citizens across rural India. This would \ninclude strengthening and integrating the existing 100,000 CSCs under the original CSC scheme \nand making operational an additional 1.5 lakh CSCs in Gram Panchayats. The Project is to be \nimplemented over a period of 4 years. Till June,2016   a total number of  1,22,793 CSCs have \nbeen rolled out at Gram Panchayat level.  \n \niii)  The Government is implementing following schemes  for providing digital education and \nliteracy to the masses (including rural India): \n \n\n(a) Department of  Electronics & Information Technology ( DeitY) is implementing a \nproject viz; “Course on Computer Education in Rural India” for Training and Certification \nof one lakh Common Service Centre (CSC) Operators/ Village Level Entrepreneurs (VLE) \nin every state of the country with financial support of Rs. 750.00 lakh  through National \nInstitute of Electronics and Information Technology (NIELIT), an autonomous society \nunder DeitY . Under this project, a total of 1,00,000 VLEs are targeted for Course on \nComputer Concepts (CCC) by March, 2017.   \n \n \n \n(b) DeitY is implementing a project viz; “ Empowering Women in Rural India through \nDigital Literacy (WDLP) with an outlay of  Rs. 287.50 lakh through NIELIT, with an aim \nat training and empowering 25,000 rural  women. The training and examination of 25,000 \nwomen has been completed.   \n \n(c)  National Digital Literacy Mission (NDLM)  scheme was approved in March 2014 with \nan aim to train 10 lakh person with a total budget outlay of Rs. 97.02 crore. \n  \n(d)  Digital Empowerment of citizens by providing Universal Digital Literacy is an \nintegral component of the vision of 'Digital India' initiative. Keeping this in view, a scheme \nentitled 'Digital Saksharta Abhiyan' (DISHA) to make 42.5 lakh persons digitally literate in \nselected households throughout the country was approved in December 2014.  \n \nBoth the above schemes on digital literacy  are being implemented concurrently  and so far \naround 72.92 lakh candidates have been trained and approximately 33.15 lakh candidates \nhave been certified. A total of 1952 training partners are involved under these schemes. Out \nof these Training Partners/ Training Centres, around 57% exist in rural areas (including \nnearly 30,000 CSCs).  \n \n(e) A scheme to make 6 crore rural households digitally literate has also been drawn up in the \ncurrent financial year. \n \niv) A scheme for setting up/upgrading of  NIELIT centres is also under implementation to \ncover rural and remote parts of the country in J&K and North East (NE). The Scheme entails \nsetting up of 10 new extension centres and upgradation of 8 existing centres in NE. One \nextension centre in Leh district of J&K has also been setup. \n \n******** \n  \n\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |634", "t": "Increase in Frequency", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 634 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nINCREASE IN FREQUENCY \n \n†634. SHRI RAJESH VERMA: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to operate train no. 14611 -\n14612 up -down daily and attach sleeper and air conditioned \ncoaches keeping public welfare in mind;  \n \n(b) if so, the time by which train no. 14611 -14612 up-down will run \nwith sleeper and air conditioned coaches; and  \n \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n (a) to (c)  14611/14612 Amritsar -Gorakhpur Express (weekly) is \npresently running in integrated rake link with fully unreserved \n14603/14604 Amritsar -Saharsa Jan Sadharan Express (weekly) \nmeant for General Class passengers.   Hence, increase in frequency \nof 14611/14612 Amritsar -Gorakhpur Express (weekly) from weekly \nto daily is not feasible due to operational and resource constraints.  \nFurther, 14611/14612 Amritsar-Gorakhpur Express (weekly) is a fully \nun-reserved train service.  As such, attachment of AC and Sleeper \nclass coaches in this train is operationally not feasible, as it will \nchange the very character of such train. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |635", "t": "NSSO Data on Creation of Jobs", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF STATISTICS AND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 635 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON WEDNESDAY, THE 20TH JULY, 2016 \n \nNSSO DATA ON CREATION OF JOBS \n \n635. SHRI JANARDAN SINGH SIGRIWAL: \n \nWill the Minister of STATISTI CS AND PROGRAMME \nIMPLEMENTATION be pleased to state  the number of jobs  created \nduring each of the last three years  and the current year as per the \nlatest data of the National Sample Survey Organisation (NSSO), sector-\nwise? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER FOR STATISTICS AND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION \n[SHRI D.V. SADANANDA GOWDA] \n \nLast survey of National Sample Survey Office (NSSO) on Employment -\nUnemployment was conducted during July, 2011 – June, 2012 (68 th \nround of NSS). However, t o assess the effect of economic slowdown \non employment in India , Labour Bureau, Ministry of Labour & \nEmployment, has been conducting Quarterly Quick Employment \nsurveys in selected labour -intensive and export -oriented sectors , \nnamely, textiles including apparels, leather, metals, automobiles, \ngems & jewellery, transport, IT/BPO and handloom/powerloom. Based \non the latest available results from these surveys , the estimated net \naddition of jobs during each of the last three years  is given at \nAnnexure.  \n\nAnnexure \nStatement referred to in reply to Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No. \n635 for 20.7.2016 \n***** \n \n***** \n \nSector wise estimated net addition in employment \n(in Lakhs) \nSl. \nNo Industry/ Group \nJanuary \n2013 – \nDecember \n2013 \nJanuary \n2014 – \nDecember \n2014 \nJanuary \n2015 – \nDecember \n2015 \n1 Textiles 2.86 1.41 0.72 \n2 Leather 0.44 -0.07 -0.08 \n3 Metal -0.35 0.74 0.37 \n4 Automobile 0.16 0.25 -0.08 \n5 Gems & Jewellery 0.09 0.11 -0.19 \n6 Transport -0.09 -0.11 -0.04 \n7 IT/BPO 1.09 1.93 0.76 \n8 Handloom/ Powerloom -0.02 -0.05 -0.11 \n Total 4.19 4.21 1.35 \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |636", "t": "Demand and Supply of Uranium", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nDEPARTMENT OF ATOMIC ENERGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 636 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nDEMAND AND SUPPLY OF URANIUM \n \n636.  SHRI S.P.MUDDAHANUME GOWDA: \n \nWill the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether there is a gap between demand and supp ly of uranium for the \n nuclear power plants of the country; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof and the reasons the refor; \n \n(c)  the measures taken to meet the demand of urani um for smooth functioning \n of nuclear projects; and \n \n(d)  the extent to which these steps have been succ essful? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR, PERSONNEL, PUBLIC GRIEVA NCES AND \nPENSIONS AND PRIME MINISTER'S OFFICE (DR. JITENDRA SINGH): \n \n(a) & (b) No, Sir.   There are currently twenty one  (21) reactors with an installed \ncapacity of 5780 MW.   Of these, thirteen (13) reac tors with a capacity of \n3380 MW are under IAEA Safeguards and use imported uranium which \nis available in adequate quantity.  Eight (8) react ors with aggregate \ncapacity of 2400 MW are fuelled by indigenous urani um.  These reactors \nare now being operated close to their rated capacit y. In addition, one unit \n(Kudankulam Unit-2) has also attained first critica lity (start of controlled \nself-sustaining nuclear fission chain reaction in t he Reactor for the first \ntime) on July 10, 2016.  This unit also uses imported fuel.  \n  \n(c)  The Government has taken measures to augment d omestic uranium \nsupply by opening of new mines and processing facil ities and importing \nfuel for reactors under IAEA Safeguards. \n \n(d)    The steps have resulted in operation of nuclear po wer reactors at or \nclose to their rated capacity. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |637", "t": "Strength of Bureaucrats", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF PERSONNEL, PUBLIC GRIEVANCES AND PENSIONS \n(DEPARTMENT OF PERSONNEL & TRAINING) \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 637 \n(TO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016) \n \nSTRENGTH OF BUREAUCRATS \n \n637. SHRIMATI V. SATHYA BAMA: \n        SHRI PR. SENTHIL NATHAN: \n \nWill the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has taken  any decision on the cadre sanctioned  \nstrength of IAS and IPS officers in the country, State-wise; \n(b)  if so, the details thereof and the  recruitments made during the last three  years, \nyear-wise and cadre-wise; \n(c)  the steps taken by the Government  to direct State Governments to fill up  \nadequate IAS and IPS officers in their  respective States from their  State \nGovernment Services in the coming years; and  \n(d)  the total expenditure incurred by  the central exchequer for the overall  \nexpenditure of IAS and IPS officers in the country, State-wise? \n \nANSWER \n \nMinister of State in the Ministry of Personnel, Public Grievances and Pensions \nand Minister of State in the Prime Minister’s Office. (DR. JITENDRA SINGH) \n(a) &  (b): The Sanctioned strength of the India Administrative Service (IAS) and \nIndian Police Service  (IPS) officers of any given cadre is reviewed ordinarily at the \ninterval of every five years. Cadre-wise details of officers allocated to IAS and IPS on \nthe basis of Civil Services Examination - 2012 to 2014 are at Annexure -I and \nAnnexure-II respectively.  \n \n(c): The appointment by promotion to IAS/IPS from State Civil Service/ State \nPolice Service is governed by the statutory provisions, which envisage separate role to \nCentral Government, State Governments and Union Public Service Commission \n(UPSC). The vac ancies to be filled up are determined year wise and selection \ncommittee meetings are conducted by the UPSC for preparation of select list on \nreceipt of the proposals from the State Governments/UTs. Periodic meetings are \nconducted by the UPSC and Central Go vernment with the State Governments to \nexpedite the proposals for the Selection Committee Meetings so that the vacancies are \nfilled up expeditiously. \n \n(d): The information regarding total expenditure incurred by the central exchequer \nfor the overall  expenditure of IAS and IPS officers in the country, State -wise is not \nmaintained. \n******** \n\nANNEXURE-I \n \nAnnexure-I mentioned in reply to part (a)& (b) of Lok Sabha Unstarred \nQuestion No. 637asked by SHRIMATI V. SATHYA BAMA and SHRI PR. \nSENTHIL NATHAN to be replied on 20.07.201 6  regarding “Strength of \nBureaucrats” \n \nAllocation of IAS (Direct Recruit) officer to various cadres during last 3 years  \n \nSr. No. Name of Cadre CSE- 2012 CSE- 2013 CSE-2014 \n1. A G M U T 12 11 11 \n2. Andhra Pradesh 10* 10* 5 \n3. Assam Meghalaya 7 7 8 \n4. Bihar 10 9 10 \n5. Chhattisgarh 7 7 5 \n6. Gujarat 7 10 9 \n7. Haryana 4 5 4 \n8. Himachal Pradesh 5 4 4 \n9. Jammu & Kashmir 4 4 4 \n10. Jharkhand 7 7 7 \n11. Karnataka 8 8 9 \n12. Kerala 6 6 6 \n13. Madhya Pradesh 13 13 13 \n14. Maharashtra 8 9 8 \n15. Manipur 6* 6* 3 \n16. Nagaland 4 4 4 \n17. Orissa 6 6 7 \n18. Punjab 6 6 5 \n19. Rajasthan 8 8 8 \n20. Sikkim 1 1 1 \n21. Tamil Nadu 9 9 10 \n22. Telangana  *  * 4 \n23. Tripura *   * 3 \n24. Uttar Pradesh 17 17 19 \n25. Uttarakhand 3 3 3 \n26. West Bengal 12 10 10 \nTotal   180 180 180 \n* For CSE -2012 and CSE -2013 cadre allocation was made to erstwhile cadre of \nAndhra Pradesh and Joint Cadre of Manipur-Tripura. \n  \n\nANNEXURE-II \n \nAnnexure-II mentioned in reply to part (a)& (b) of Lok Sabha Unstarred \nQuestion No. 637asked by SHRIMATI V. SATHYA BAMA and SHRI PR. \nSENTHIL NATHAN to be replied on 20.07.201 6  regarding “Strength of \nBureaucrats” \n \nAllocation of IPS (Direct Recruit) officer to various cadres during last 3 years  \n \nSl. No. Name of Cadre CSE- 2012 CSE- 2013 CSE- 2014 \n01. Andhra Pradesh 07* 04 05 \n02. AGMUT 11 10 08 \n03. Assam-Meghalaya 07 07 06 \n04. Bihar 07 07 05 \n05. Chhattisgarh 04 04 01 \n06. Gujarat 07 06 05 \n07. Haryana 04 05 04 \n08. Himachal Pradesh 03 03 03 \n09. Jammu & Kashmir 04 04 03 \n10. Jharkhand 05 04 05 \n11. Karnataka 06 06 07 \n12. Kerala 04 05 06 \n13. Madhya Pradesh 10 09 09 \n14. Maharashtra 09 09 11 \n15. Manipur 06* 04 07 \n16. Nagaland 04 03 04 \n17. Odisha 05 06 04 \n18. Punjab 05 05 05 \n19. Rajasthan 05 05 04 \n20. Sikkim 0 01 01 \n21. Tamil Nadu 08 07 06 \n22. Telangana  * 03 02 \n23. Tripura * 02 02 \n24. Uttar Pradesh 17 19 21 \n25. Uttarakhand  02 02 01 \n26. West Bengal 10 10 15 \n Total 150 150 150 \n     * For CSE-2012 cadre allocation was made to erstwhile cadre of Andhra Pradesh    \nand Joint Cadre of Manipur-Tripura. \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |638", "t": "Welfare of Minorities", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.638 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nWelfare of Minorities \n \n \n    638.  KUMARI SHOBHA KARANDLAJE: \n \n Will the Minister of MINORITY AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the amount spent on the welfare of minorities in various States including in the State of \nKarnataka during each of the last three years and the current year under the Multi -\nSectoral Developmen t Programme, Educational Schemes, Seekho  Aur Kamao (Learn \nand Earn), Nai  Roshni, ( Leadership Development of Minority Women), National \nMinorities Development and Finance Corporation (NMDFC); and \n(b)  the  amount likely to be spent under Pre -Matric Scholarship Scheme, Merit-cum-Means \nBased Scholarship Scheme and Free Coaching and Allied Schem e in variousStates \nincluding the State of Karnataka during the above period?  \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF MINISTRY OF MINORITY \nAFFAIRS \n(SHRI MUKHTAR ABBAS NAQVI) \n \n(a) and (b) Funds released to the Project Implementing Agencies/NGOs/S tate \nChannelising Agencies (SCAs) for implementation of (i) Seekho aur Kamao (Learn and \nEarn) (ii) Nai Roshni – Leadership Development of Minority Women (iii) National \nMinorities Development and Finance Corporation (NMDFC) in various states including \nKarnataka during last three years and current year may please be seen  at Annexure -I, \nAnnexure-II and Annexure-III respectively. \nThe State/UT wise statement of funds released under the Scheme of Multi Sectoral \nDevelopment Programme is at Annexure-IV.  \nThe State /UT -wise details of funds released under the Pre-matric Scholarship \nScheme,  Post-matric Scholarship Scheme  may please be seen at Annexure V. The \nState/UT -wise details of funds released under the Merit-cum-Means based Scholarship \nScheme may please be seen at Annexure –VI.  \n \n \n \n\n \nUnder the scheme of Maulana Azad National Fellowship, there is neither any state -\nwise fund allocation nor is there any state-wise fund release. \nThe State/UT -wise details of funds released under the Free Coaching and Allied \nScheme may please be seen at Annexure VII. The State/UT -wise details of funds \nreleased under the schemes of Support to minority candidates clearing Prelims \nconducted by UPSC/SSC, State Public Service Commission (PSC) etc. Padho \nPardesh- Interest Subsidy on Educati onal Loans for overseas studies  Jiyo Parsi \nmay please be seen at Annexure VIII respectively. \nNai Manzil - The Nai Manzil scheme has been approved with the cost of Rs. 650.00 \ncrore for five years. 50% funding has to come from the World Bank. The World Bank \nhas approved the funding of US$ 50 million. Rs. 155.00 crore has been earmarked for \n2016-17 for implementation of programme.  \n***** \n  \n\n ANNEXURE-I   \nLok Sabha Unstarred Question No.638  raised by Kumari Sobha Karandlaje regarding \nWelfare of Minorities to be answered on 20.07.2016  \n \n  \nFunds released to the Project Implementing Agencies (PIAs) for Implementation of “Seekho Aur Kamao \n(Learn and Earn)” schemes in the States during last three years. \nS. No. State 2013-14  2014-15 2015-16 \nAmount \nreleased       (Rs. \nin crore) \nAmount \nreleased       \n(Rs. in crore) \nAmount \nreleased       \n(Rs. in crore) \n1 ANDHRA PRADESH 0.57 1.97 5.16 \n2 ARUNACHAL PRADESH 0.29 0.28   0.74 \n3 ASSAM 0.73 2.47 4.37 \n4 BIHAR 1.20 3.25 4.37 \n5 CHHATTISGARH 0.10 0.42 1.27 \n6 DELHI 0.58 1.85 1.99 \n7 GUJARAT 0.58 1.69 3.42 \n8 HARYANA 0.67 1.51 4.37 \n9 HIMACHAL PRADESH 0.19 0.56 2.54 \n10 JAMMU & KASHMIR 0.67 4.72 9.00 \n11 JHARKHAND 0.60 1.38 4.09 \n12 KARNATAKA 0.77 1.63 2.54 \n13 KERALA 0.53 1.48 0.78 \n14 MADHYA PRADESH 0.58 2.04 7.25 \n15 MAHARASHTRA 0.19 0.28 2.33 \n16 MANIPUR 0.29 0.14 1.72 \n17 MEGHALAYA 0.29 0.85 1.13 \n18 MIZORAM 0.10 0.28 1.32 \n19 NAGALAND 0.10 0.28 0.73 \n20 ODISHA 0.38 0.96 3.09 \n21 PUDUCHERRY 0.10 0.28 0.00 \n22 PUNJAB 0.58 2.28 4.41 \n23 RAJASTHAN 0.77 2.19 4.78 \n24 SIKKIM 0.10 0.56 1.16 \n25 TAMILNADU 0.24 1.06 3.42 \n26 TELENGANA - 0.71 5.64 \n27 TRIPURA 0.29 0.85 1.23 \n28 UTTAR PRADESH 3.53 5.77 14.34 \n29 UTTARAKHAND 0.64 1.18 2.45 \n30 WEST BENGAL 1.16 3.10 9.78 \n31 Maulana Azad National Academy for \nSkills (All over the Country focus on \nMadarsas \n- - 82.56 \n  Sub - Total 16.79 46.02 191.96 \n  Professional Services 0.21 0.19 0 \n  Grand Total 17.00 46.21 191.96 \n\n \nAnnexure – II \nLok Sabha Unstarred Question No.638  raised by Kumari Sobha Karandlaje regarding \nWelfare of Minorities to be answered on 20.07.2016  \nState wise funds released to the Non -Governmental Organisations for Implementation of the Scheme of \nLeadership Development of Minority Women (NaiRoshni) during   last three years (2013 -14,2014-15, \n2015-16) and current year (2016-17). \n  \nS. No.  \n  \nStates \n2013-14 2014-15 2015-16 \n2016-17(up to \n30.06.2016) \nFund Released (in \nRs.Crores) \nFund Release (in \nRs.Crores) \nFund Release (in \nRs.Crores) \nFund Release (in \nRs.Crores) \n1 Andhra \nPradesh 0.47 0.18 0.13 0.03 \n2 Arunachal \nPradesh 0.05 - 0.00 0.00 \n3"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |639", "t": "Cleanest and Dirtiest Stations", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 639 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \n \nCLEANEST AND DIRTIEST STATIONS \n \n639.  SHRIMATI VANAROJA R.: \n         SHRI K. ASHOK KUMAR:  \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state:  \n(a) whether the Railways has released a list of cleanest railway \nstations in the A1 category;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) whether Varanasi railway station has been found to be the \nmost dirtiest railway station among all other railway stations \nin the country; and  \n \n(d) if so, the steps taken by the Railways to clean the railway \nstations as per the ranking shown in the said list? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)                            \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND                \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) Yes, Madam. Indian Railways have conducted survey on \nassessment of cleanliness standards of major railway stations (A1 \nand A category) based on the feedback from the passengers.  \n\n(b)  These stations have been ranked from Cleanliness Level 1 \n(highest) up to Level 5 based on passenger feedback. Out of 75 \nstations falling in A1 category, 03 stations ranked in Level 1, 23 \nstations in Level 2, 30 stations in Level 3, 18 stations in Level 4 and \n01 station in Level 5.  \n(c) No, Madam.  \n(d) Zonal Railways have been directed to take appropriate \nmeasures to improve cleanliness standards at the stations based on \nthe passenger feedback on various cleanliness parameters. \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |640", "t": "Enhancement of Platform Capacity", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 640 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nENHANCEMENT OF PLATFORM CAPACITY \n \n640. SHRI PRATHAP SIMHA : \n \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a)  whether the Railways has announced to enhance the platform \n capacity of Mysore, Chamaraja Nagar, K R Nagara, Nanjangud \n and Srirangapatna railway stations; \n(b)  if so, the number of platforms to be upgraded; \n(c)  whether any time frame has been fixed for in crease of platforms; \n and \n(d)   if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTRY OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n(a) No, Madam. \n(b)  to (d) Do not arise. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |641", "t": "Complaints through Social Media", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.641 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nCOMPLAINTS THROUGH SOCIAL MEDIA \n \n \n641.  SHRI CHANDU LAL SAHU : \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the number of Twitter complaints received by the Twitter \nhandles @Ministry of Railways and @SureshPrabhu in the last six \nmonths; \n \n(b) the number of complaints that have been addressed via Twitter; \nand \n \n(c)the details of resources spent by the Ministry on the handling of \nTwitter accounts? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATION AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MININSTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n (a) to (c):  The twitter handle @RailMinIndia of Mi nistry of Railways \nand @sureshP rabhu has been receiving large number of tweets \nevery day including complaints. Such tweets are forwarded to the \nconcerned authorities on their twitter handles for speedy resolution. \nAt present, twitter account of the Ministry is handled largel y by the \nexisting manpower by utilising the available infrastructure and \nresources. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |642", "t": "Survey on Railway Line", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 642 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nSURVEY ON RAILWAY LINE \n \n†642. SHRI  A. T. NANA PATIL: \n \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether Railways has decided not to take any action regarding \nrailway project from Sholapur to Jalgaon (454 KM) via Tuljapur, \nOsmanabad, Kunthalgiri, Beed, Paithan, Aurangabad, Verul, Selod \nand Ajanta caves after completion of survey of the same; \n \n(b) if so, the reasons therefor; and \n \n(c) if not, the steps taken by the Railways to start construction on this \nproject? \n \nANSWER \n MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n \n(a) to (c):   Survey for a new line from Solapur to Jalgaon (454 km) via \nTuljapur, Osmanabad, Beed, Paithan, Aurangabad, Verul, Sillod and Ajanta \nCaves has been completed.  The cost of this line has  been assessed as \n`3238 crore with a negative Rate of Return of ( -) 5.69%.  Due to its \nunremunerative nature, huge throwforward of ongoing projects, limited \navailability of funds for new lines and other competing priorities, this \nproject could not be taken forward. \n \nHowever, to reassess viability of the Solapur -Tuljapur-Osmanabad (80 \nkm) leg, an updating survey has been sanctioned. \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |643", "t": "Flood Warning Centres", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EARTH SCIENCES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 643 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON WEDNESDAY, JULY 20, 2016 \n \nFLOOD WARNING CENTRES \n \n 643. KUNWAR SARVESH KUMAR:  \n \n         Will the Minister of EARTH SCIENCES be pleased to state: \n \n(a)    whether early flood warning centres  have been established and if so, \nthe details thereof and the names of the rivers included;  \n(b)   whether remote sensing technology and Geological Information System \n(GIS) is being used for the purpose of flood management including early \nflood warning system and if so, the details thereof and the names of the \nrivers where such technology/system is being used; \n(c)   whether the real time data is received from the satellite regarding flood-\nprone areas and if so, the details thereof; and  \n(d)    whether the G overnment propose to get the help of United States of \nAmerican Flood Monitoring Organisations for availability of real  time \ndata of floods through satellite and if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR MINISTRY OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY AND  \nMINISTRY OF EARTH SCIENCES \n(SHRI Y. S. CHOWDARY) \n \n(a) Yes Madam. The  list of flood warning centers and the rivers are \nincluded in Annexure-I. \n \n(b) Yes Madam. In a pilot mode mathematical models for rainfall runoff \nestimation (like MIKE-11 FF) are used for some of the sites in Damodar \nBasin, Godavari Basin, Mahanadi Basin & Chambal Basin. \n  \n(c) Satellite only provides  real time Quantitative Precipitation Estimation \n(QPE) and no advanced information on flood inundation is possible to \nderive. However, after the flooding is reported, it is possible to \ndemarcate areas of inundation using satellite remote sensing data.  \n \nIn order to meet specific requirements of flood forecas ting, which is \nprovided by central water commission, India Meteorological Department \n(IMD) operates Flood Meteorological Offices (FMOs) at thirteen \nlocations viz., Agra, Ahmedabad, Asansol, Bhubaneshwar, Guwahati, \nHyderabad, Jalpaiguri, Lucknow, New Delhi, Patna, Srinagar , Bangaluru \nand   Chennai.   Apart   from  this,  IMD  also  supports  Damodar  Valley  \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \nCorporation (DVC) by providing QPF for Damodar river basin areas for \ntheir flood forecasting activities. During the flood season, FMOs provide \nvaluable meteorological support to the Central Water Commission \n(CWC) for issuing flood warnings in respect of the 43 rivers of India  \ncovering 146 river basins. CWC is working in close association with IMD \nand State Governments for timely flood forecast whe never the river \nwater level rises above warning level.  \n \nTo meet the requirement of State Governments, IMD Officers invariably \nattend all the meetings called by the State Governments for reviewing \nthe preparedness on floods by various agencies. \n \n(d) No Madam. \n \n  \n\n \nAnnexure-I \nList of Flood Forecasting Stations of CWC \nSl. No. Name of the rivers  Name of Flood Forecast site  Name of state  \n1 2 3 4 \nGanga Basin  \n1.  Alaknanda  Srinagar  Uttaranchal \n2.  Ganga Rishikesh  Uttaranchal \n3.  Ganga  Haridwar  Uttaranchal \n4.  Ganga  Narora Barrage Uttar Pradesh  \n5.  Ganga  Kannaouj Uttar Pradesh \n6.  Ganga Ankinghat Uttar Pradesh  \n7.  Ganga  Kanpur Uttar Pradesh \n8.  Ganga  Dalmau Uttar Pradesh  \n9.  Ganga  Phaphamau Uttar Pradesh \n10.  Ganga Allahabad Chhatnag Uttar Pradesh  \n11.  Ganga  Mirzapur Uttar Pradesh \n12.  Ganga  Varanasi Uttar Pradesh  \n13.  Ganga  Ghazipur Uttar Pradesh \n14.  Ganga Buxar Bihar \n15.  Ganga  Ballia  Uttar Pradesh \n16.  Ganga  Patna Dighaghat Bihar \n17.  Ganga  Patna Gandhighat  Bihar \n18.  Ganga Hathidah Bihar \n19.  Ganga  Munger Bihar \n20.  Ganga  Bhagalpur Bihar \n21.  Ganga  Kahalgaon Bihar \n22.  Ganga Sahibgunj Jharkhand \n23.  Ganga  Farakka West Bengal \n24.  Ramganga  Moradabad Uttar Pradesh \n25.  Ramganga Bareilly  Uttar Pradesh \n26.  Yamuna  Tajewala Weir Haryana  \n27.  Yamuna Mawi Uttar Pradesh \n28.  Yamuna Delhi Rly Bridge NCT Delhi \n29.  Yamuna Mathura Uttar Pradesh \n30.  Yamuna Agra  Uttar Pradesh \n31.  Yamuna Etawa Uttar Pradesh \n32.  Yamuna Auraya Uttar Pradesh \n33.  Yamuna Kalpi Uttar Pradesh \n34.  Yamuna Hamirpur Uttar Pradesh \n35.  Yamuna Chilaghat Uttar Pradesh \n36.  Yamuna Naini  Uttar Pradesh \n37.  Sahibi Dhansa NCT Delhi \n38.  Chambal Gandhisagar Dam Madhya Pradesh \n39.  Betwa Mohara Uttar Pradesh \n40.  Betwa Sahjina  Uttar Pradesh \n41.  Ken Banda Uttar Pradesh \n42.  Gomati  Lucknow Hanuman Setu Uttar Pradesh \n43.  Gomati Jaunpur  Uttar Pradesh \n  \n\n \n \n44.  SAI Raibareli  Uttar Pradesh \n45.  Ghaghra  Elgin Bridge  Uttar Pradesh \n46.  Ghaghra Ayodhya  Uttar Pradesh \n47.  Ghaghra Turtipar Uttar Pradesh \n48.  Ghaghra Darauli Bihar \n49.  Ghaghra Gangpur Siswan Bihar \n50.  Ghaghra Chhapra  Bihar \n51.  Rapti Balrampur Uttar Pradesh \n52.  Rapti Bansi  Uttar Pradesh \n53.  Rapti Gorakpur Bridghat Uttar Pradesh \n54.  Sone Inderpuri Bihar \n55.  Sone Koelwar Bihar \n56.  Sone Maner Bihar \n57.  PunPun Sripalpur Bihar \n58.  Gandak Khadda Utt"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |644", "t": "Representation from Associations/ Public Representatives for Extension of New Trains", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.644 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nREPRESENTATION FROM ASSOCIATIONS/ PUBLIC  \nREPRESENTATIVES FOR EXTENSION OF NEW TRAINS \n \n644.  SHRI BADRUDDIN AJMAL: \n               \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Railways has received representation from associations/public \nrepresentatives for extension/diversion/ frequency enhancement/introduction of \nnew trains including an inter -city Chair car tr ain between Dhubri and Guwahati for \nimproving rail services in Dhubri;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the action taken thereon; and  \n \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n(a) to (c): A large number of representations are received at various levels of \nrailway administration which , inter alia , include Railway Stations, Div ision, Zonal \nHeadquarters and at Railway Board level.  However, Indian Railways do not \nmaintain compendiums of such representation. \nAt present, 2 pairs of trains 1) 15817/15818 Dhubri –Siliguri Rajya Rani Express (Tri-\nweekly) and 2) 55611/55612 Dhubri – Kamakhya Fast passenger are available \nbetween Dhubri and Guwahati which are considered adequate for the present level \nof traffic and availability of platform. However, introduction of new tra ins between \nDhubri and Guwahati  and increase in frequency of existi ng train services is not \nfeasible at present due to operational and resource constraints including lack of \nmaintenance facility at Dhubri and line capacity constraints between Golakganj and \nDhubri. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |645", "t": "Increase in Frequency", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.645 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nINCREASE IN FREQUENCY \n †645. SHRI PANKAJ CHAUDHARY: \n     Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Railways has received representation for increasing the frequency, \nexpansion and attaching additional coaches in train number 75007 / 75008 / 75003 / \n75004 /  55077 / 55031 / 55032 / 75005 / 55048 / 55049 running on Gorakhpur \nAnandnagar-Badhni Gonda rail route; \n(b) if so, the details of action taken in this regard; and \n (c) the time by which the decision is likely to be taken in this regard? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) Representations for increase in frequency, extension and attachment of \ncoaches in existing train services including 75007/75008 Goarkhpur-Gonda \nDEMU and other trains running on Gorakhpur -Anandnagar- Barhni section  \nare received at various levels of Railways administration viz. Railway \nstations, Divisions, Zonal headquarters and Railway Board’s level.  \nHowever, Indian Railways do not maintain compendium of these \nrepresentations. \n(b) & (c) These deman ds are examined and action as found feasible and \njustified, is taken from time to time. Besides, increase in frequency, \nextension and attachment of coaches is an on -going process on Indian \nRailway subject to traffic demand, operational feasibility and avai lability of \nresources. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |646", "t": "Passenger Facilities", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 646  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nPASSENGER FACILITIES \n \n646.  SHRI C. R. PATIL: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS  be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of AC Superfast trains  being run by the Railway along \nwith status of pantry cars provided therewith; \n \n(b) whether passengers are facing a lot  of difficulties on account of \nabsence of facilities in view of the fact that the next stop of the train \nwould be after about six hours of journey particularly in the case of next \nstoppage of Haridwar Mumbai AC Superfast Express after Bhopal; and \n \n(c) if so, the corrective measures that are being taken to ameliorate the \ngenuine difficulties of passengers? \n \n \nANSWER  \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \n OF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n (SHRI MANOJ SINHA)  \n \n(a) At present, 23 pairs of AC Superfast trains are being run by the \nIndian Railways out of which 13 Pairs of trains are provided with pantry \ncars.  \n(b) and (c) The Haridwar Mumbai AC Superfast Express is running \nwithout pantry car.  No complaints regarding catering services have \nbeen reported so far. Station based e -Catering service has been \nprovided at stations en route to take care of the catering  needs of \npassengers on this train. \n**** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |647", "t": "Skill Development of Unemployed Persons", "head": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 647 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.7.2016 \n \n \n \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT  OF UNEMPLOYED PERSONS \n \n \n 647. SHRI  NABA KUMAR SARANIA :  \n \n \n Will the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPR ENEURSHIP \nbe pleased to state: \n \n \n(a) The curriculum-wise and programme wise detail o f skill development \nprogrammes for uneducated persons to various State including Assam and Uttar \nPradesh; and  \n \n(b) The number of beneficiary under the said progra mmes during each of the last \nthree years and the current year programme-wise and State-wise . \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) IN THE MINISTRY OF \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n(SHRI RAJIV PRATAP RUDY) \n \n \n(a) Under Skill Development Initiative Scheme (SDI) , 8 courses have been \ndeveloped for uneducated persons to acquire skill t raining in order to improve their \nemployment potential. List of courses is given below:-  \n \n(1) Kiln Formed Glass \n(2) Design with Glass \n(3) Kiln Formed glass-II \n(4) Kiln Formed glass-III \n(5) Design (Development)with Glass (Advance Craftsman ) \n(6) Design Applications With Glass Bangles. \n(7) Flamework Technique of glass \n(8) Comprehensive Cold Work Technique  \n \n Further, there are number of courses being develope d under Sector Skill Council \n(SSCs) which are for uneducated persons like high altitude porter etc.  \n \n \n(b)      No person has been trained in above referr ed SDI courses during last three \nyears & current year, as no enrolment by any individual.   \n \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |648", "t": "Operation of Trains with Bio-Diesel", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n          LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION N0. 648 \n   TO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \n    OPERATION OF TRAINS WITH BIO-DIESEL \n \n648. SHRI NAGAR RODMAL: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n (a)  whether the Railways proposes to operate trains with bio -diesel in the \ncountry; \n \n(b)   if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c) the quantity of fuel likely to be saved by the Railways as a result of \noperation of trains with bio-diesel? \n \n  ANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n                                          (SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n (a)  Yes, Madam.  \n(b)  Railway started 5% blending of Bio-diesel in High Speed Diesel (HSD) for \ntraction purpose from 05.06.2015, the World Environment Day. \nProgressively orders are being placed and coverage of bio -diesel is \nbeing increased. \nIndian Railways used 4986.8 kilolitres (KLs) of Bio -diesel during the \nfinancial year 2015-16. \n \n(c) The Bio-diesel is approximately 1:1 replacement of HSD when blended \nup to a limit of 10%. Thus, each litre of Bio -diesel blended in HSD brings \nabout the saving of equal quantity of HSD. \n  ****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |649", "t": "Indians Stranded in Libya", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.649 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nINDIANS STRANDED IN LIBYA \n \n649.  DR. K. GOPAL: \n \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to State: \n \n(a) whether at least 1,800 Indians are still in the Libya and may \nneed to be rescued through an emergency evacuation soon; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(c) whether recently many Indians were killed in Libya; and  \n \n(d)  if so, the details thereof?  \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n(SHRI M.J. AKBAR) \n \n(a) & (b) There are around 1750 Indian nationals in Libya. The \nevacuation of Indian nationals in Libya began in July, 2014 and we \nevacuated 3750 Indian nationals since then. Our Mission in Tripoli \ncontinues to render  assistance to those Indian nationals willing to \nreturn to India. Indian nationals currently in Libya are due to their \nown volition.  \n \n(c) & (d) An Indian nurse, Ms. Sonu Sathyan from Kerala and her \ninfant son, Pravan Vipin Kumar died on 25 March, 2015 dur ing the \nclashes between two rival groups in Zawiya (about 45 KM from \nTripoli). The Mission rendered all assistance for transportation of \nmortal remains of the deceased and travel arrangements for her \nhusband, who was in Libya along with the deceased.      \n \n***** \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |650", "t": "Grievance Officer", "head": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF PERSONNEL, PUBLIC GRIEVANCES AND PENSIONS \n(DEPARTMENT OF ADMINISTRATIVE REFORMS AND PUBLIC GRIEVANCES) \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 650 \n(TO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016) \n \nGRIEVANCE OFFICER \n \n650. SHRI PRAHLAD SINGH PATEL:  \n \nWill the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government considers  to make a post of grievance officer in all the  \nCentral Government offices in order to give  an option to the dejected common man to  \navail a second chance of justice; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; \n \n(c)  whether the Government considers  to give stipulated timeframe for each  application \nto be processed at Government offices; and \n \n(d)  if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nMinister of State in the Ministry of Personnel, Public Grievances and Pensions and Minister \nof State in the Prime Minister’s Office. (DR. JITENDRA SINGH) \n(a) & (b):   As per guidelines issued by Department of Administrative Reforms & Public \nGrievances, each Ministry/Department/Public Sector Undertaking/Autonomous Organization \nis required to designate a full time Grievance Officer, known as Director of Public \nGrievances.  The Director of Public Grievances shall be actively inv olved in the process of \ndealing with grievances. Every Wednesday of the week has been earmarked for the Director \nof Public Grievances for hearing the grievances of the citizens.   The names of the Directors \nof Public Grievances for various Ministries/Depart ments are available \non http://www.pgportal.gov.in.  \n  \n(c) & (d):  As per guidelines issued by the Department of Administrative Reforms and Public \nGrievances, a grievance is required to be redressed with in a period of two months.  In case, it \nis not possible an interim reply with reasons for delay is required to be provided. \n \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |651", "t": "'B' Grade Railway Station", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.651 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \n ‘B’ GRADE RAILWAY STATION \n \n†651. SHRIMATI KAMLA DEVI PAATLE: \n           \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Railways proposes to upgrade the Janjgir-Naila railway \nstation of South Eastern Central Railway to ‘B’ grade station;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) to (c):  Janjgir-Naila is a ‘D’ category station in Jharsuguda –Bilaspur \nsection of  South East Central Railway. Stations have been categorised \nin Seven Cat egories i.e. ‘A1’, ‘A’, ‘B’, ‘C’, ‘D’, ‘E’ and ‘F based on the \nannual passenger earnings which are reviewed every five years. The \nannual passenger earnings are required to be between ` 4 crores to ` 8 \ncrores for including any station under ‘B’ category. The annual passenger \nearnings of Janjgir-Naila railway station during the last review \nconducted during year 2011 -12 was ` 1 crore 90 lakhs approximately.   \nAs such, the station has been retained under ‘D’ category. \n*** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |652", "t": "Disbursal of Fellowship", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.652 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nDISBURSAL OF FELLOWSHIP \n \n652. : SHRI B.V. NAIK \n        \nWill the Minister of MINORITY AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether there is deliberate delay in the disbursal of fellowship to minority \ncommunity students by Government’s funding agency like UGC;  \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor; \n(c) the minimum time period UGC undertakes for the verificati on of documents under \nMaulana Azad National Fellowship for Minority (MANFM); \n(d) whether fellowship disbursal complaint redressal mechanism is dysfunctional in \nUGC; \n(e) if so, the details thereof along with total number of complaints received from \nminority students under MANFM during the last three years and the current year; \nand \n(f) the details of MANFM awarded during the above period and the steps taken by the \nGovernment to ensure timely disposal of fellowship to minority community students? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \n(SHRI MUKHTAR ABBAS NAQVI) \n \n(a): No, Madam.  \n \n(b): Does not arise. \n \n(c): University Grants Commission (UGC), which implements the fellowship \nscheme has already initiated steps for disbursing fellowship to minority \ncommunity candidates directly since 2011 for pursing M.Phil./Ph.D. \nresearch on full time/regular basis in Universities/Institutions/Colleges \nin India through e -payment by Canara Bank based on agreement made \nbetween UGC and Canara Bank unde r the scheme of Maulana Azad \nNational Fellowship for Minority Students.  Besides this , the UGC has \nalso implemented the Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) scheme through \nCPMS/PFMS towards disbursement of fellowship to  selected candidates \nsince 2013 so that the fellowship is credited to the beneficiaries account \nexpeditiously.  \n (d) and (e):  No Madam.  As per information provided by UGC while t here are no \nspecific complaints pertaining to delay in the disbursal of fello wship to \nminority community students during the last three years and the current \n \n \n\n \n \n year, there may be delays in payments due to the following reasons:- \n1. Delay in submission of claim by the university. \n2. Late joining by candidates. \n3. Delay in submission of documents to the bank branches. \n4. Delay in upload of documents. \n5. Technical problem in Public Financial Management System (PFMS). \n (f): The details of MANFM  awarded during the last three years and current year  \nis as under:- \nFinancial / \nSelection \nYear \nTotal No. of selected candidates during financial/selection year \nBuddhist \nChristian \nJain \nMuslim \nParsi \nSikh \nTotal \n2013-14 41 105 0 526 2 82 756 \n2014-15 34 109 20 517 1 75 756 \n2015-16* 36 105 20 522 0 73 756 \n2016-17* 32 93 20 543 0 68 756 \n* Selection made for 2015-16 and 2016-17 simultaneously \nSelection for the year 2017-18 yet to be made during 2016-17. \nSelection for the year 2017-18 yet to be made during 2016-17.  \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |653", "t": "Under Construction Atomic Power Plants", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nDEPARTMENT OF ATOMIC ENERGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 653 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nUNDER CONSTRUCTION ATOMIC POWER PLANTS \n \n653.  SHRI GODSE HEMANT TUKARAM: \n \nWill the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the work of under construction Atomic Power plants is running behind \n schedule; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof and the reasons the refor; \n \n(c)  the steps taken to ensure the completion of th e work in time; \n \n(d)  whether the Government is facing opposition fr om the local people at these places; \n and \n \n(e)  if so, the details thereof and the action take n/being taken by the Government in this \n regard?  \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR, PERSONNEL, PUBLIC GRIEVA NCES AND PENSIONS \nAND PRIME MINISTER'S OFFICE (DR. JITENDRA SINGH): \n \n(a)&(b)Two projects Kakrapar Atomic Power Project ( KAPP 3&4) (2X700 MW) at Kakrapar, \nGujarat and Rajasthan Atomic Power Project (RAPP 7& 8) (2X700 MW) at \nRawatbhata, Rajasthan are at various stages of cons truction. There have been \ndelays in respect of these projects mainly on accou nt of delays in receipt of critical \nequipment like Steam Generators, Endshields etc.  \n \nThe 500 MW Prototype Fast Breeder Reactor (PFBR) co nstructed by BHAVINI at \nKalpakkam, Tamil Nadu is at an advanced stage of co mmissioning.  PFBR is a first \nof its kind reactor in the country and development/ manufacture of large sized \nequipment/components took time.  In view of its tec hnological complexity, abundant \ncaution is being taken during erection/installation  and commissioning of various \nsystems.  Further, due to its first of a kind desig n, there have been certain additional \nstipulations by the regulatory body which are being complied with. \n \n \n(c) Several measures were taken to expedite the del iveries of the equipment and as a \nresult, most of the equipment have now been receive d. As of June 2016, KAPP 3&4 \nand RAPP 7&8 had achieved an overall physical progr ess of 75.5% and 61.5% \nrespectively. \n \n \n(d) No, Sir. \n \n \n(e) Does not arise in view of (d) above. \n  \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |654", "t": "E-Catering Facility", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.654 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nE-CATERING FACILITY \n \n654. SHRI V. ELUMALAI: \n \n        Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n                    \n(a) whether it is true that the Railways has extended  e -catering facility in \na large number of stations; and \n(b) if so, the details thereof along with the total number of stations and \ntrains where e-catering facility has been extended? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a)  & (b):  Yes, Madam.  Initially e-catering service had been introduced on \napproximately 1500 trains running without pantry cars through Indian \nRailway Catering and Tourism Corporation (IRCTC).   Further, for widening \nthe range of options available to passengers for ordering food of their \nchoice, as a pilot project, e -catering service was started at 45 major \nstations.  In Rail Budget 2016 -17, extension of station based e -catering \nservices to all 408 A1 and A category stations through IRCTC has been \nannounced. \n \n**** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |655", "t": "Setting up of Railway Station", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 655 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nSETTING UP OF RAILWAY STATION \n \n655. SHRI ANTO ANTONY : \n \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a)  whether there is a proposal pending before the Railways for \n setting up of railway station at Nedumbassery near Kochi \n international airport; and \n(b)  if so, the details and the present status thereof along with the \n estimated cost of implementation? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTRY OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n(a) & (b) A new train halt at Nedumbassery near Cochin International \nAirport between Angamali and Chovvara station in Ernakulam Jn - \nTrichur section has been sanct ioned in 2010-11 at a cost of ` 93 Lakh. \nThe work is held up due to public opposition against closure of level \ncrossing no. 64 at the proposed location. \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |656", "t": "Literacy Rate Among Minorities", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 656 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nLITERACY RATE AMONG MINORITIES \n \n656. SHRI  SIRAJUDDIN  AJMAL: \n \nWill the Minister of MINORITY AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the present lite racy rate among the minorities along with the breakup of \nmale and female literacy rates and its comparison with the overall literacy \nrate in the country, State/UT-wise and community-wise; \n(b) the schemes being implemented and the other measures taken to bridge  \nthe gap in literacy level between the general female population and minority \ngirls in the country; and \n(c) the funds sanctioned, released and utilised under such schemes during \neach of the last three years and the current year, State/UT -wise and \ncommunity-wise? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \n(SHRI MUKHTAR ABBAS NAQVI) \n \n(a): As per Census 2011, the literacy rate among the minorities along with the \nbreak-up of male and female literacy rates and their comparison with the overa ll \nliteracy rate in the country are detailed below: \n \nName of Religion Literacy rate \nPerson Male Female \nTotal 73.0 80.9 64.6 \nHindu 73.3 81.7 64.3 \nMuslim 68.5 74.7 62.0 \nChristian 84.5 87.7 81.5 \nSikh 75.4 80.0 70.3 \nBuddhist 81.3 88.3 74.0 \nJain 94.9 96.8 92.9 \nOther religions and \npersuasions 59.9 70.9 49.1 \nReligion not stated 74.7 81.9 67.3 \n \nState/UT-wise and community-wise details of ‘literacy rates’ are available on the \nwebsite of the Office of Registrar General and Census Commissioner of India. \n\n(b) & (c): The details of schemes being implemented for enhancing opportunities \nfor education  of minorities, in general, and to bridge the gap in literacy level \nbetween the general female populatio n and minority  girls in the country  are as \nunder: \ni. Pre-Matric Scholarship \nii. Post-Matric Scholarship \niii. Merit-cum-Means  Scholarship \niv. Maulana Azad National Fellowship \nv. Integrated Child Development Services (ICDS) scheme for \nproviding services through Anganwadi Centres \nvi. Sarva Shiksha Abhiyan (SSA) and opening of Kasturba Gandh i \nBalika Vidyalayas \nvii. ‘Padho Pardesh' - Interest subsidy on educational loans for \noverseas studies \nviii. ‘Nai Udaan'- Support for students clearing Prelims conducted by \nUPSC, SSC, State Public Service Commissions, etc. \nix. Scheme for Providing Quality Education in Madarsas (SPQEM) \nx. Scheme for Infrastructure Development of Minority Institutions \n(IDMI) \nxi. Greater Resources for Teaching Urdu \nxii. Free Coaching and Allied Scheme \nxiii. Schemes of Maulana Azad Education Foundation (MAEF) for \npromotion of education. \nxiv. Mid Day Meal Scheme \nxv. Rashtriya Madhyamik Shiksha Abhiyan (RMSA) \nxvi. Sakshar Bharat/ Maulana Azad Taleem-e-Balighan \nxvii. Jan Shikshan Sansthan (JSS)  \nxviii. Block Institutes of Teachers Education \nxix. Women’s Hostel. \n \nThe details of funds sanctioned / released/  utilised under such schemes (in the \nmanner collated in the Ministry) during each of the last three years and the current \nyear, State/UT-wise and community -wise are available on the website of Ministry \nof Minority Affairs- www.minorityaffairs.gov.in.  \n \n* * * * * "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |657", "t": "Speed of Trains", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 657 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nSPEED OF TRAINS \n      \n+657.     SHRIMATI RANJANBEN BHATT: \n   \n    Will the Minister of RAILWAYS  be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether  the Railways is contemplating to increase the speed of      \ntrains as well as technical development of Indian railway stations;  \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether the Railways has taken any steps in this regard; and  \n(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) & (b): With a view to increasing speed of trains in Indian Railways, \n‘Mission Raftaar’ has been announced in the Railway Budget 2016-17.   \n          \n\n \n The mission envisages a target of doubling of average speed of \nfreight trains and increasing the average s peed of all non -suburban \npassenger trains by 25 kmph  in next 5 years.  In order to implement it, \na cross-functional directorate has been created in Railway Board.  \n       Technical development of railway stations in this regard includes \nadvanced signallin g technology based systems such as electronic \ninterlocking, train protection and warning systems, etc. to ensure safe \nand efficient running of trains at higher speeds. \n(c) & (d): Action Plan for improving mobility and increasing average \nspeed includes remo val of speed restrictions, construction of road \nover bridges (ROBs) and road under bridges (RUBs), right powering of \ntrains, introduction of twin -pipe in wagons and replacement of \nconventional trains by Main Line Electric Multiple Unit (MEMU) trains \nand Diesel Electric Multiple Unit (DEMU) trains.  \n*** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |658", "t": "Survey Work of Railway Projects", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 658 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nSURVEY WORK OF RAILWAY PROJECTS \n \n†658. PROF. RAVINDRA VISHWANATH GAIKWAD: \n \n \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n[ \n \n(a) the details of projects on which the work of survey has been \nconducted during the last three years under the South Central \nRailway zone; \n \n (b) the details of proposals received by the Railways for sanction \nrelating to construction after survey     for the overall development of \nRailways under the above zone; and \n \n \n(c) the details of proposals approved by South Central Railway? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n \n    (a) to (c):   A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n                                        ****** \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 658 BY PROF. RAVINDRA VISHWANATH \nGAIKWAD TO B E ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 20.07 .2016 \nREGARDING SURVEY WORK OF RAILWAY PROJECTS. \n(a):   The details of projects for which surveys have been \nconducted under South Central Railway during the last three years \ni.e. 2013-14, 2014-15, 2015-16 & current financial year is as given \nbelow:- \nS.No. Name of the Project Plan  \nhead \nLength \n(in Km) \nCost  \n(in  `. \nCr.) \n1 Gadchandur-Adilabad New line 70 448 \n2 Karimnagar-Hassanparthi New line 62 464 \n3 Gooty-Dharmavaram with electrification Doubling 90 469 \n4 Giddalur-Bakrapet via \nPoramamilla,Siddavatam \nNew line 118 1038 \n5 Macherla-Nadikude Doubling 35 146 \n6 Nandyala-Atmakur via Mahanandi New line 58 656 \n7 Jaggayyapeta-Miryalguda New line 37 222 \n8 Pagidipalli-Shankarpalli New line 105 1189 \n9 Manikgarh-Gadchandur Doubling 28 203 \n10 Hyderabad-Srisailam New line 104 1253 \n11 Baptala-Nizampatnam-Reppalli New line 46 481 \n \n(b):  Proposals/repr esentations from organizations, rail users, \nelected representatives, Ministries, Departments, etc. both formal \nas well as informal are received by Railways at various levels \nincluding Ra ilway Board, Zonal Railways, Divisional Headquarters \netc. As receipt of such demands and suggestions is a continuous \nand dynamic process, centralized compendium of such requests is \nnot maintained. \n \n(c):   Out of the above completed surveys, Gadchandur -Adilabad (70 \nKm) New Line project has been included in Capi tal investment \nProgramme of 2016 -17 (as Annexur e to Pink Book) at a cost of `. \n1500 Crore in anticipation of State Government coming forward to \ntake up this project through Joint Venture.                                           \n                                                       ***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |659", "t": "Assessment of Performance of Corporations", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 659 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON JULY 20, 2016 \nASSESSMENT OF PERFORMANCE OF CORPORATIONS \n \n \nNo. 659      SHRI B. SENGUTTUVAN:  \n \nWill the Minister of URBAN DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has assessed the performance of the \nvarious corporations of Tamil Nadu and taken into consideration their \nwoeful performance in solid wast e management, drinking water \nprovision, nightmarish infras tructural inadequacies and lack of \ntransparency etc.; and  \n \n( b) If so, whether the Government proposes to constitute a core \ngroup consisting of experts, elected representatives etc. to see that \nthe funds provided by the Govern ment are properly applied to the \nprojects and an inclusive development is targeted?  \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF URBAN \nDEVELOPMENT \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n \n \n(a):    As the Urban Local Bodies (ULBs) are governed by State-specific \nlaws and regulations, it is for the States to assess them on various \nparameters as determined by the respective States. However, as the \nGovernment of India supplements the State & ULB efforts in urban \ndevelopment through Central Assistance, certain reforms and \nassessments are made for accessing the funds under programmes \nsuch as Swachh Bharat Mission (SBM), Atal Mission for Rejuvenation \nand Urban Transformation (AMRUT) and Smart Cities Programme \ntowards achieving the targets se t under the programmes/missions. \nThe Sanitation Rating is one such exercise under SBM. \n(b):    There is no such proposal.  \n \n**** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |660", "t": "Change in ID Proof Rule of Tatkal", "head": "       GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \n   MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 660 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nCHANGE IN ID PROOF RULE OF TATKAL \n \n 660. SHRI J.J.T. NATTERJEE: \n \n           Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has recently modified the identity \nproof rule of Tatkal tickets; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) whether this will provide an easy ticket sale out of the way \nand if so, the details thereof; \n \n(d) whether the Government has any spec ial scheme to prevent \nthe misuse of Tatkal scheme; and \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n  (a) to (e): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n******* \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) To ( e) OF \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.  660 BY SHRI J.J.T. NATTERJEE  TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 20.07.2016 REGARDING CHANGE IN ID \nPROOF RULE OF TATKAL.  \n \n(a) & (b): No such change has been made in recent past. Prior to July \n2015, it was stipulated that any person booking ticket under Tatkal \nscheme from computerized Passenger Reservation System (PRS) \ncounter had to submit photocopy of proof of identity at the time  of \nbooking of reserved ticket, whose details were captured in the \nsystem. The passengers booking the ticket through internet had to \nindicate the details of proof of identity at the time of booking the \nticket. The passenger was supposed to carry the same o riginal proof \nof identity during journey failing which all the passengers booked on \nthe ticket were treated as travelling without ticket and charged \naccordingly. In view of complaints regarding inconvenience caused to \ngenuine passengers on this account, th is provision was modified in \nJuly 2015 and it was indicated that just like general reservation, in \ncase of Tatkal ticket also, one of the passengers booked on the ticket \nshould carry one of the prescribed proof of identity (in original) during \njourney fail ing which all the passengers will be treated as travelling \nwithout ticket. \n \n(c) to (e):  No, Madam. This provision has been modified with a view to \navoid inconvenience to genuine passengers who were being treated as \ntravelling without ticket if they forgot  to carry the same proof of \nidentity as indicated in the ticket but were having other original \nprescribed proof(s) of identity to prove their genuineness. Moreover,  \n              ...2/- \n\n-2- \n adequate safeguards have been built in the scheme and various ste ps \nhave been taken to avoid misuse of the modified provision, which are \nas under: \ni. No refund is granted on cancellation of confirmed Tatkal ticket.  \n \nii. The facility of change of name is not permitted on the booking \nmade under Tatkal Scheme. \n \niii. The timings of op ening of booking under Tatkal scheme on the \nopening day of reservation have been staggered to 1000 hours & \n1100 hours on the previous day of journey from train originating \nstation for AC and non-AC classes respectively. \n \niv. Authorised ticketing agents have been restricted from booking \nTatkal tickets during the first thirty minutes of opening of Tatkal \nbooking i.e. from 1000 hours to 1030 hours and from 1100 hours \nto 1130 hours.  \n \nv. Web service agents have been permitted to book only one Tatkal \nticket per train per day. \n \nvi. Maximum four passengers per PNR for Tatkal Tickets. Individuals \nare allowed only 2 Tatkal tickets per IP Address from 1000 hours \nto 1200 hours permissible and maximum number of tickets \nallowed to an individual user is 6 per month. \n \nvii. CCTVs are installed at important PRS locations to monitor the \nactivity of touts. Regular inspections/drives are conducted to \nunearth activity of malpractice. \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |661", "t": "Satellite Application for Weather Forecast", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EARTH SCIENCES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 661 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON WEDNESDAY, JULY 20, 2016 \n \nSATELLITE APPLICATION FOR WEATHER FORECAST \n \n661. SHRI M. CHANDRAKASI:  \n \n         Will the Minister of EARTH SCIENCES be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Union Government has any  proposal for satellite based \napplication for advanced and accurate weather forecasting for the \nbenefit of fishermen of the country and if so, the details thereof; and \n(b)   the details regarding new initiatives under the consideration of the \nMinistry to encourage and support fishermen of the country to make their \nlife easy and earn more profits? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR MINISTRY OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY AND  \nMINISTRY OF EARTH SCIENCES \n(SHRI Y. S. CHOWDARY) \n \n(a-b) No Madam, there is no new proposal. Already for the benefit of fisherman \ncommunity, a satellite based application for the fishermen community of \nthe country, called \"Potential Fishing Zone (PFZ) Advisory service \" is \noperational involving Geographic Information System (GIS) tools since \n1999 with locational guidance of fish grounds/aggregation. In addition, \nthe Ocean State Forecast (OSF) (wave height and direction, wind speed \nand direction, ocean currents, sea surfa ce temperature, depth of mixed \nlayer and thermo cline, sea level at major and minor ports, etc.) is also \nbeing provided to fisherman on local marine weather conditions.  \n \nThe use of PFZ information help s fishermen community in re duction of \nsearch time for fish resulting savings in the fuel cost.  \n \nAs per National Centre for Economic Applied research ( NCEAR) report \nroughly one million marine fishermen are active fishers and they are \nbenefited by Potential Fishing Zones (PFZ), Ocean State Forecast (OSF) \nAdvisory Services of Indian National Centre f or Ocean Information \nServices (INCOIS). Out of one million appr oximately 0.66 million people \nare involved in allied fishing activities such as marketing fish, processing \nfish etc. Across the one million coastal fishermen community, the annual \nvalue addition during post Potential Fishing Zone Advisory Services since \n2004-05 is  assessed  at  Rs.  4700  crores.  GDP  contribution of PFZ and  \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \nOcean State Forecasting services for the fishery sector is assessed at \n3.9 % in 2012 -13 from 1.9% in 1995 - 96 and can potentially increase to \n7.8%. Accordingly, additional annual income to fishermen is aggregated \nat Rs. 3,034 crores. Environmental benefits accrue furt her as the saving \ndue to reduction in overall diesel consumption computed as carbon \ncredits, on account on per unit catch due to targeted potential fishing \nzone identification, aggregates annually to Rs. 36,200/- Crores. \n \nA wide range of advanced communica tion technology are employed for \ndissemination of the information, including Electronic Display Boards \ninstalled at 100 fishing harbours/fish landing centers / fishing \nhamlets/fishermen cooperative societies, through telephones, Fax, Local \nCable TV Network s, Doordarshan, All India Radio (Thiruvananthapuram \nand Karwar), Community Radio’s, FM Radio Stations (like Radio Benziger \nin Kollam, Radio Monsoon in Thiruvananthapuram, Kalpakkam \nCommunity Radio, Radio Ala in Kakinada), Local News Papers, SMS, \nINCOIS web  site, email, Interactive Voice Response System (IVRS), \nmobile applications viz. Fisher Friend Mobile Application (FFMA), \nmKRISHI, In -house developed android application, Village information \nCentres, etc. The feedback received from the fishermen suggests t hat \nthey depend on Ocean State Forecast for planning their daily fishing \nactivities, where as PFZ helps saving the fuel and reduce search time.  \n \n \n***** \n  "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |662", "t": "Sagar Purvi", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EARTH SCIENCES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 662 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON WEDNESDAY, JULY 20, 2016 \n \nSAGAR PURVI \n \n662.  DR. C. GOPALKRISHNAN: \n \n          Will the Minister of EARTH SCIENCES be pleased to state: \n \n(a)     Whether the Government has recently dispatched a survey vessel “Sagar \nPurvi” a  float ship to study about ocean temperature, currents, sea erosion on \nthe Arabian Sea, the Gulf of Mannar in the Bay of Bengal. \n(b)    If so, the details thereof: \n(c) Whether any useful information has been received through this float ship; and  \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR MINISTRY OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY AND \n MINISTRY OF EARTH SCIENCES \n(SHRI Y. S. CHOWDARY) \n \n(a) Yes Madam, the Government of India has deployed the Coastal Research \nVessel [CRV] Sagar Purvi  to study about ocean parameters along the coastal \nwaters of India. \n(b) CRV Sagar Purvi was deployed for implementing various programmes of MoES \nsuch as Monitoring of marine pollution levels and conservation and \nmanagement of coastal resources including coral reef under Coastal Ocean \nMonitoring and Prediction System (COMAPS) Programme, Integrated Coastal \nand Marine Area Management (ICMAM), Swathe bathymetry survey of the \nExclusive Economic Zone of India (EEZ) and etc., along the coastal waters of \nIndia.  \n(c) Yes Madam, the data an \n(d) .d samples collected using CRV Sagar Purvi was useful in understanding the \nmarine pollution levels, biological wealth and conservation of coastal \nresources in the coastal waters of India and for the better understanding of \nthe seabed morphological features and its geo-morphological implications.   \n(e) Under COMAPS programme the water quality parameters are periodically \nmonitored in sensitive coastal marine areas of India especially for oil spills \nand thus helping in development of possible predic tion of sea water quality in \nthese selected locations to assess the state of marine environment. \nBathymetry charts generated by swathe bathymetry surveys likely serve as a \nbase map for Oceanographic Researchers, Communication purpose, Defence, \nNavigation s ectors and etc. Systematic sediment sampling and its analysis \nhelps to understand the sedimentation history and palaeo -climatic regime of \nthe Indian peninsula. \n***** \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |663", "t": "Water Logging due to Rain", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.663 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nWATER LOGGING DUE TO RAIN \n \n663. DR. KIRIT SOMAIYA : \n             \n      Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Railways has received complaints about the delay in Mumbai \nlocal train services during June, 2016 and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(b) whether it is a fact that trains are delayed due to water logging; and  \n \n(c) if so, the steps taken by the Railways to tackle the problem?  \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) Yes, Madam.  On Central Railway system, there have been 3 major cases \nof disruption in rail services on 11.06.2016 in the month of June 2016 due to \nOverhead Equipment (Electric) tripping on all the 4 lines on the Main Line and \nUP & DOWN Harbour line.  On Western Railway system, 3 complaints were \nreceived regarding delay in local train services due to reasons which inter-alia \nincludes derailment in suburban section at Lower Parel station and incident of \ntrespassings in suburban sections. \n \n(b) & (c) Yes, Madam.  The following steps have been taken by the Railways to \ntackle water logging problem during monsoon in Mumbai sub urban area: \n(i) Railway culverts have been cleaned and desilted in coordination with \nMumbai Corporation of Greater Mumbai. \n(ii) Side dr ain within railway area have been cleaned and repaired before \nmonsoon. \n(iii) Water pumps have been installed at locations prone to flooding to clear \nthe flood water during heavy rains. \n \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |664", "t": "Training Camps for Football", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 664 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nTraining Camps for Football \n \n+664.  SHRI DEVJI M. PATEL: \n   \nWill the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to state: \n  \n(a)   the World ranking of India in football and the measures proposed by \nthe Government to enhance interest in football at school and college \nlevel; \n(b)  whether the Government organizes the training camps for football at \nvillage level in the country and if so, the details thereof; and \n(c)  the total number of training camp s organised in all districts of \nRajasthan State, district-wise during the last three years? \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) FOR \nYOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(SHRI VIJAY GOEL) \n \n(a) The current World Ranking of India in football is 1 52.  The \nGovernment of India has taken a series of steps to popularize \nFootball in the country.  Several rounds of discussions have been held \nwith International Football Federation (FIFA), All India  Football \nFederation (AIFF), Kendriya Vidyalaya Sangathan (KVS), Central \nBoard of Secondary Education (CBSE), Subroto Mukherjee Sports \nEducation Society and other stake holders.  As a result, a Mission 11 \nmillion programme has been finalized  in coordination with FIFA, with \nthe prime objective to engage more than 11 million children in \nactivities relating to football.   \n \n(b)& (c): Sports is a state subject and hence development of sports in \nthe states is the responsibility of the concerned State Gov ernment.  \nThe Government of India does not organize coaching cam ps at \nvillage level. \n************** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |665", "t": "Financial Sports to NSFs", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 665 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nFinancial Grants to NSFs \n \n665.  SHRI RAVNEET SINGH: \n   \nWill the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to \nstate: \n  \n(a)  the details of the financial grants provided by the Central \nGovernment to the National Sports Federations (NSFs) in \nIndia during the last two years; \n(b)  whether the Government will bring the Sports Development \nBill, 2011 for consideration of the House; and \n(c)  if so, the time by which it is anticipated and the details \nalong with the salient features thereof? \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) FOR  \nYOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(SHRI VIJAY GOEL) \n \n(a)  Details of financial grant provided during the last two \nyears to various National Sports Federations (NSFs) and some \nother organisations are given in the annexure.  \n \n(b) & (c) The Ministry of Youth Affairs & Sports has formulated \na draft National Sports De velopment Bill (NSDB).  The salient \nfeatures of the NSDB are: \n \n Central Government support for deve lopment and \npromotion of sports. \n\n Promotion of ethical practices in sports. \n  Rights and obligations of the Indian Olympic Association \nand National Sports Federations.  \n Participation of athletes in the management/decision \nmaking of the NSFs and the Indian Olympic Association. \n Mechanism for sports dispute settlement.  \n Bringing National Sports Federations under Right to \nInformation Act, 2005 with certain exclusion clauses for \nprotecting personal/confidential information relating to \nathletes. \n Age and tenure restrictions for office-bearers of NSFs. \n \nSince further consultations are required, it would be difficult to \nindicate a definite time frame for bringing it for consideration \nof the House.  \n \n***** \n\n \nAnnexure \n \nAnnexure referred to in reply to part ( a) of Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No. \n665 to be answered on 20-7-2016 asked by SH RI RAVNEET SINGH regarding \nFinancial Grants to NSFs  \n \n Grants released to NSFs and some other organisations during last two years \n(Provisional) \n(Rupees in lacs) \nS. \nNo \nName of the Federation 2014-15 2015-16 \n(Provisional) \n1 Athletics Federation of India, New Delhi 83.55 1831.44 \n2 Archery  448.59 1105.00 \n3 All India Chess Federation, Chennai 107.95   195.00 \n4 National Rifle Association of India, New \nDelhi \n1039.63 2212.00 \n5 All India Tennis Association, New Delhi 48.52     47.00 \n6 Judo Federation of India 114.66   275.00 \n7 Rowing Federation of India, Secunderabad 40.69 308.98 \n8 Table Tennis Federation of India, New Delhi 122.02 296.00 \n9 Swimming Federation of India, Ahmadabad 7.22 177.25 \n10 Squash Racket Federation of India, Chennai 101.56 170.00 \n11 Boxing  99.36 1215.00 \n12  Hockey India  520.33 2038.26 \n13 Indian Weightlifting Federation, New Delhi 83.47 765.00 \n14 Badminton Association of India 511.59 1380.00 \n15 Equestrian Federation of India, New Delhi 12.43 16.00 \n16 All India Football Federation 131.63 154.30 \n17 Indian Golf Union, New Delhi 37.29 37.00 \n18 Wrestling Federation of India, I.G. Stadium \nDelhi \n532.31 1510.00 \n19 Yachting Association of India, New Delhi 116.91 161.98 \n20 Indian Amateur Kabaddi Federation, Jaipur  18.00 113.00 \n21 Volleyball Federation of India, Chennai 125.92 309.83 \n22 Gymnastics Federation of India, Jodhpur 66.10 210.00 \n23 Amateur Handball Federation, J & K 24.95 14.61 \n24 Basketball Federation of India, N Delhi 52.63 9.83 \n25 Indian Kayaking & Canoeing Association, \nNew Delhi  \n59.94 132.67 \n26 All India Sports Council of the Deaf,  New \nDelhi \n3.02 65.64 \n27 Paralympic Committee of India, Bangalore 197.72 720.08 \n28 Special Olympic Bharat, New Delhi 19.17 600.34 \n29 All India Carrom Federation, New Delhi 5.83 0.00 \n\n30 Amateur Baseball Federation of India, Delhi 2.25 0.00 \n31 Atya Patya Federation of India, Nagpur. 1.25 0.50 \n32 Cycle Polo Federation of India, New Delhi 2.85 0.75 \n33 Indian Power lifting Federation 5.25 0.00 \n34 Kho-kho Federation of India, Kolkata 7.75 0.00 \n35 Sepak Takraw Federation of India, Nagpur 10.53 104.00 \n36               Shooting Ball Federation of India, New Delhi 0.00 0.00 \n37 Softball Federation of India, Indore 0.00 0.00 \n38 Taekwondo Federation of India, Bangalore 39.80 85.00 \n39 Tenni-Koit Federation of India, Bangalore 3.00 0.50 \n40 Tennis Ball Cricket Federation of India, \nGorakhpur. \n0.00 0.00 \n41 Tug of War Federation of India, New Delhi 3.00 0.00 \n42 Wushu Association of India, New Delhi 68.55 241.00 \n43 Billiards & Snooker Federation of India, \nKolkatta \n76.25 75.00 \n44 Cycling Federation of India 69.29 351.00 \n45 Amateur Soft Tennis Federation of India 0.50 0.00 \n46 Bridge Federation of India 0.00 16.00 \n47 Ice Hockey (NSPO) 2.00 0.00 \n48 School Games Federation of India, Bhopal 17.20 55.00 \n49 Indian Olympic Association, New Delhi 1830.87 32.20 \n50 Association of Indian Universities (NSPO) 148.18 0.00 \n51 Bowling Federation of India 10.44 0."}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |666", "t": "New Science and Technology Projects", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY \nDEPARTMENT OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No.666 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20/07/2016 \n \nNEW SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY PROJECTS \n \n666. SHRI  PR. SENTHIL NATHAN :  \n    \nWill the Minister of SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY òãðìððÐð ¡ðøÜ ÑßðøÌðð÷ò±ð¨îó Ùðüëðó \nbe pleased to state : \n \n(a) the details of Autonomous Institutions and Statutory Boards under Department \nof Science and Technology; \n(b) the new Science and Technology projects undertaken by Departme nt of Science \nand Technology including the above Institution s/Boards during each of the last three \nyears and the current year; and \n(c) the funds provided for the above projects/institutions during the above period, \nState/Institution/Board-wise? \n  \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY \nAND MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EARTH SCIENCES \n(SHRI Y.S. CHOWDARY) \nòãðìððÐð ¡ðøÜ ÑßðøÌðð÷ò±ð¨îó ÙðüëððâðÚð Ùð÷ü Üð¸Úð Ùðüëðó +ÉÉè® ÑðöÆãðó òãðìððÐð ÙðüëððâðÚð Ùð÷ü Üð¸Úð Ùðüëðó \n (gÉÉÒ ´ÉÉ<Ç. AºÉ. SÉÉèvÉ®ÉÒ) \n \n \n(a) to (c):  The information is being collected and will be laid on the Table of the \nHouse. \n \n \n \n******** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |667", "t": "Strength of SC/ST Officials", "head": " \n  \n \n \n  GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS \nDEPARTMENT OF TELECOMMUNICATIONS  \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.667  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20 TH  JULY, 2016 \n \nSTRENGTH OF SC/ST OFFICIALS \n \n667. SHRI RATTAN LAL KATARIA: \n \nWill the Minister of COMMUNICATIONS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the total strength of executive and non-executive employees in the department \nand the number of SC and ST officials in various categories; \n \n(b)  whether guidelines issued by the DoPT regarding the implementation of \nreservation quota is followed by the department; \n \n(c)  if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor along with the action \ntaken to fill the reserved vacancies; \n \n(d)  whether some people have got jobs on fake SC and ST certificate; and \n \n(e)  if so, the remedial action taken in this regard? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (IC) OF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS & \n MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) The total  strength of employees  as categorized in the Department is as \nfollows: \n \nDepartment of Telecommunications  \n \nS. No.    Category           Total         SC              ST  \n \n1    Group A   2071            353    116 \n2              Group B  1100            125                40 \n3    Group C       805            162      44 \n \nDepartment of Posts  \n \nS. No.    Category           Total         SC                 ST  \n1    Group A         609   62                  33 \n2              Group B               8426             1225      503 \n3     Group C           190260           31681            13499 \n \n(b) Yes, Madam.  DOP&T’s guidelines for providing the reservation to the extent of \n15% for  SCs and 7.5% for STs is followed in the  Department.  \n \n(c) Filling up of vacancies in various cadres, including the reserved vacancies for \nSC/ST, is an ongoing and long term process. Deficiencies are monitored and the \nvacancies are filled as per relevant recruitment rules. \n \n(d) & (e) Yes, Madam. One  complaint/case of bogus certificate of caste has been \nnoticed  in the  Department of Telecommunications  for securing employment.  Action \nhas been taken against the official as per the extant rules.  \n \n************ "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |668", "t": "Attack on Hindus in Bangladesh", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.668 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nATTACK ON HINDUS IN BANGLADESH \n \n668.  SHRI CH. MALLA REDDY: \nSHRI MUTHAMSETTI SRINIVASA RAO (AVANTHI): \nPROF. SAUGATA ROY: \nSHRI KUNWAR PUSHPENDRA SINGH CHANDEL: \n \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)   whether the incidents of threats and attacks on Hindus and \ntheir institutions in South Asian countries have increased \nparticularly in Bangladesh and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(b)   whether these attacks are being made by organised \ninternational groups; \n \n(c)   if so, the details thereof and the diplomatic efforts being made \nby the Government to stop these attacks/threats; and \n \n(d)   whether the Government is taking initiative to tackle this \nissue in consultation with the respective Governments and if \nso, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n[GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD)] \n \n(a) & (b) There have been a number of targeted attacks on \nbloggers, writers and professors, publishers and minorities in \nBangladesh over the last year and a half. During this period, several \nincidents of violent attacks on members of the Hindu community, \nincluding on their places of worship and their properties, have been \nreported.   Although Islamic State (IS) and Al Qaeda in the Indian \nSubcontinent (AQIS) are reported to have claimed responsibility for \na number of such killings, the Government of Bangladesh has \nrepeatedly denied the presence of these international terrorist \n\ngroups and has emphasized that local extremist groups were \nresponsible for these incidents. \n \n(c) & (d) The Government of India has conveyed our concerns in \nthis regard to the Government of Bangladesh at various levels, \nincluding in a regular manner through our High Commission in \nDhaka. The Government of Bangladesh has assured us that it \naccords top priority to containing the proliferation of terrorist \nactivities inside Bangladesh and their expansion beyond the borders \nof Bangladesh. It has also underlined its commitment to a policy of \nzero tolerance towards terrorism and has reiterated its \ndetermination to investigate these incidents and apprehend the \nperpetrators of these atrocities. \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |669", "t": "Cleanliness in Railways", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 669 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nCLEANLINESS IN RAILWAYS \n \n†669. SHRIMATI RITI PATHAK: \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state:  \n(a) whether the Railways has taken any steps  to ensure clean \ntoilets, platforms and railway tracks at  the railway stations in \nthe mega cities of the country under Swachh Bharat Abhiyan; \nand \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the total funds spent by the \nRailways  for the said purpose during the year 2015-16? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) & (b)  Yes, Madam. Under the Swachh Bharat Abhiyan , Special \nCleanliness Campaign was launched on Indian Railways on 2nd Oct, \n2014. Regular events on cleanliness are planned and organised to \nimprove and maintain cleanliness at Railway premises including \n\ntoilets, platforms and tracks at railway stations in the mega cities. \nWeekly special intensive cleaning drives at major Railway stations \nin rotation have also been undertaken by Zonal Railways.  \n  On completion of one year of Swachh Bharat Mission, \ntheme based cleanliness drives have been launched by Indian \nRailways from 25th Sept, 2015.  Campaigns for increasing the \nawareness and participation from all sections viz. Railway staff, \nRailway users/public as well as Charitable Institutions/Social \nOrganisations, were organised at many major stations. Enforcement \nof Indian Railways (Penalties for activities affecting cleanliness at \nrailway premises) Rules, 2012 has also been intensified. \n   An amount of  ` 315 crores approx. have been spent by \nthe Ministry on cleanliness and sanitation at all stations of Zonal  \nRailways during the year 2015 -16. This includes cleanliness of \ntoilets, platforms and tracks within station limit, circulating area, \nwaiting rooms under Swachh Bharat Abhiyan. \n \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |670", "t": "Safety Norms for NPPs", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nDEPARTMENT OF ATOMIC ENERGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 670 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nSAFETY NORMS FOR NPPs \n \n670.  SHRIMATI BHAVANA PUNDALIKRAO GAWALI PATIL: \n \nWill the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether all Nuclear Power Plants (NPPs) in the  country are set up as per the \n safety  norms fixed by International Atomic Energy  Agency (IAEA) and if so, \n the details thereof; \n \n(b)  whether indigenous uranium is being used in al l these plants as fuel and if so, \n the details thereof; and \n \n(c) the names of the countries from where uranium i s being imported for these \n Nuclear Plants? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR, PERSONNEL, PUBLIC GRIEVA NCES AND \nPENSIONS AND PRIME MINISTER'S OFFICE (DR. JITENDRA SINGH): \n \n(a) All nuclear power plants in India are set up in  line with the safety norms laid \ndown by the Atomic Energy Regulatory Board (AERB). AERB safety norms \nare generally in line with those of the Internation al Atomic Energy Agency \n(IAEA).  \n \n(b) No, Sir.  There are currently twenty one (21) r eactors with an installed \ncapacity of 5780 MW. Of these, eight (8) reactors w ith aggregate capacity of \n2400 MW are fuelled by indigenous uranium. The rema ining thirteen (13) \nreactors with a capacity of 3380 MW are under IAEA Safeguards and use \nimported uranium. In addition, one unit (Kudankulam  Unit-2) has also attained \nfirst criticality (start of controlled self-sustain ing nuclear fission chain reaction \nin the Reactor for the first time) on July 10, 2016 . This unit also uses imported \nfuel. \n \n(c) Presently, the Uranium is being imported from t he Russian Federation, \nCanada and the Republic of Kazakhstan.  The details  of the quantity of \nuranium imported so far and the anticipated supplie s during the calendar year \n2016 are furnished in the enclosed annexure. \n \n***** \n\nAnnexure  \n \nSr. \nNo. \nFirm/Country  Date of \nentering \ninto \nContract \nTotal Quantity to be procured as per \nContract \n \nTotal \nQuantity \nreceived till \ndate \nAnticipated \ndelivery in \nthe year 2016  \nRemarks  \n1.  M/s. AREVA, \nFrance \n17.12.2008  300 MT of Natural Uranium Ore \nConcentrate . \n299.88 MT  Nil  The Contract concluded with one -time \nsupply of the material during the year \n2009. \n2.  \nM/s. JSC TVEL \nCorporation, \nRussia \n11.02.2009  2000 MT of Natural  Uranium Oxide \nPellets.   \n1813 MT  187 MT  \n \nThe material is being procured through \nthe Annual Supplements to the Contract.  \nThe Contract concludes with the import \nof 187 MT of Pellets. \n11.02.2009  58 MT of Enriched  Uranium Oxide \nPellets. \n58.30 MT  Nil  The Contract concluded with one -time \nsupply of the material during the year \n2009. \n03.03.2015  42 MT of Enriched  Uranium Oxide \nPellets. \n42.15 MT  Nil  The Contract concluded with one -time \nsupply of the material during the year \n2015. \n3.  M/s. Cameco, \nCanada \n15.04.2015  The Contract permits procurement of \na minimum of 2750 MT and maximum \n5500 MT of Natural Uranium Ore \nConcentrate .   \n250.74 MT  12 50 MT  The material is to be procured during \n2015–2020. \n4.  \nM/s. JSC NAC \nKazatomProm, \nKazakhstan \n12.11.2009  2100 MT of Natural Uranium Ore \nConcentrate .  \n2095.9 MT  Nil  The Contract concluded during the year \n2014.   \n08.07.2015  The Contract permits procurement of \na minimum of 3750 MT and maximum \n7000 MT of Natural Uranium Ore \nConcentrate .   \n999.807 MT  15 00 MT  The material is to be procured during \n2015–2019. \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |671", "t": "Draft Real Estate Rules", "head": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \n  \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN POVERTY ALLEVIATION \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 671 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON JULY 20, 2016 \n \nDRAFT REAL ESTATE RULES \n \nNo. 671 SHRI DHANAN JAY MAHADIK :  \nDR. HEENA VIJAYKUMAR GAVIT: \n \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AN D URBAN POVERTY ALLEVIATION \nbe pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  whether the attention of the Government has been drawn \nto homebuyers reeling under the impact of delayed projects \nand mounting loan liabilities and if so, the details thereof, \nState-wise;  \n \n(b) whether the Government has framed real estate rules \nempowering homebuyers to ask for compensation if \ndevelopers do not fulfill the pr omises they had made at the \ntime of launching the project and booking dwelling unit;  \n \n(c)  if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(d)  whether the rules also ke ep check on builder s' arbitrary \nand fraudulent activities and if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n \n \n…..2/- \n \n\n-2- \n \n \n(e)  whether the rules will adv ersely affect developers hit by \ndelay in ongoing projects and if so, the details thereof? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOUSING & URBAN \nPOVERTY ALLEVIATION \n \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n \n \n \n(a) to (e):  In order to establish the Real Estate Regulatory Authority \nfor regulation and promotion of the real estate sector in \nan efficient and transparent  manner; to protect the \ninterest of consumers; and to establish an adjudicating \nmechanism for speedy disput e redressal, Ministry of \nHousing & Urban Poverty Alle viation pilot ed the Real \nEstate (Regulation and De velopment) Act, 2016. \nSpecified Sections of the Act have come into effect from \n01\nst May, 2016. \n  \nAs per Section 84 of the Real Estate (Regulation and \nDevelopment) Act, 2016, six m onths time is provided for \nframing and notification of the Rules by the appropriate  \n \n \n……3/- \n \n\n \n-3- \n \nGovernment.  As per Section 2(g) of the Real Estate \nAct, 2016 “appropriate Government” is defined as \nfollows: \n   \n“appropriate Government” means in respect of matters \nrelating to,- \n \n (i) the Union Territory wit hout Legislature, the Central \nGovernment; \n (ii) the Union Territory of Puducherry, the Union \nTerritory Government; \n (iii) the Union Territory of Delhi, the Central Ministry of \nUrban Development; \n (iv) the State, the State Government. \n \nThe Ministry of Housing & Urban Poverty Alleviation \nbeing the ‘appropriate gove rnment’ for UTs without \nlegislature, has prepared the draft rules, which have been \nuploaded on the Minis try’s website on 24 th June, 2016 \ninviting comments/suggestions thereupon.  \n \n****** \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |672", "t": "Metro Rail Projects", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.672 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON JULY 20, 2016 \nMETRO RAIL PROJECTS \nNo. 672  DR. P. VENUGOPAL: \n   PROF. K.V. THOMAS: \n   DR. KAMBHAMPATI HARIBABU: \n   MOHAMMED FAIZAL: \n   SHRI B. SENGUTTUVAN: \n   DR. KIRIT SOMAIYA: \n  \n Will the MINISTER OF URBAN DEVE LOPMENT be pleased to state: \n(a) the details of metro rail proposals received by the Government \nduring the last three years and the current year, stretch and State/ UT-\nwise along with the estimated cost of each stretch; \n(b) the details of proposals cleared and lying pending stretch and \nState-wise, the reasons for pendency along with the time by which \npending proposals are likely to be cleared; \n(c) the funds sanctioned, released and utilized during the above \nperiod for various projects, stretch and State/UT-wise; \n(d) the present status of various under construction and \nsanctioned metro rail stretches, stretch and city-wise and the time by \nwhich these are likely to be completed and operationalized; and \n(e) Whether various metro rail projects are going behind schedule \nand if so, the details thereof, stretch and city-wise and the details of \ncost escalated as a result thereof along with the steps taken/being \ntaken to complete these projects within a reasonable period of time? \n \nCont…. \n\n-2- \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n \n(a) & (b) : The details of metro rail proposals received/ \ncleared/pending during the last three years and the current year along \nwith the names  of stretch and the estimated cost stretch wise, \nState/UT-wise are given in Annexure-I & IA. \n  \n(c): The details of funds sanctioned and released by the Government \nof India and utilization of funds by Metro Companies during the last \nthree years and current year are given in Annexure-II. \n                                                                                                                             \n          \n(d): The details of progress of under construction and sanctioned \nmetro rail stretches and the time by which these are likely to be \ncompleted are given in Annexure-III.   \n \n(e) : Bangalore and Chennai Metro Rail Projects are running behind \nschedule. The details of these two metro rail projects along with \nreasons of delay are given in Annexure-IV.  The approved project cost \nof Bangalore Metro Project Phase-1 was revised in July, 2015 from \nRs.11,608.92 crore to Rs.13,845.01 crore due to increase in land cost, \nsystem work including depot and fluctuations in foreign currency. \nThere is no escalation of project cost of Chennai Metro Rail Project. \nx-x-x-x-x \n\n    Annexure-I \nANNEXURE-I REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) & (b) OF THE LOK SA BHA UNSTARRED QUESTION NO.672 \nFIXED FOR ANSWER ON 20.07.2016 REGARDING METRO RAIL PROJECTS AS KED BY DR. P. VENUGOPAL,         \nPROF. K.V. THOMAS, DR. KAMBHAMPATI HARIBABU, MOHAMMED FAIZAL, S HRI B. SENGUTTUVAN AND DR. \nKIRIT SOMAIYA. \n  \nDETAILS OF THE PROPOSALS RECEIVED/SANCTIONED/PENDING AND REASON S FOR PENDENCY DURING \nTHE LAST THREE YEARS AND CURRENT YEAR WITH ESTIMATED COST OF PROJECTS \n \nState/UT \nfrom which \nProposal \nreceived \nProject Stretch of \nthe \nProject \nEstimated/ \nApproved \nCost \n(Rs in \ncrore) \nSanctione\nd/ not-\nsanctioned \nReason for Pendency \n& time by which the \nproposals are likely to \nbe cleared \nMaharashtra Mumbai Metro Line 3 The \ninformation \nis attached \nat \nannexure \nIA. \n23,136.00 Sanctioned  \n \n \n \n \n-- \nKarnataka Bangalore Metro Rail Project Phase-2 26,405.14 Sancti oned \n Rajasthan Jaipur Metro Rail Project Phase-1 3,149.00 Sanctione d \n Gujarat Ahmadabad Metro Rail Project \nPhase-1 \n10,773.00 Sanctioned \n Maharashtra Nagpur Metro Rail Project 8,680.00 Sanctioned \n Uttar \nPradesh \nLucknow Metro Phase 1A 6,928.00 Sanctioned \n Tamil Nadu Extension of Chennai Metro  3,770.00* Sanctioned \nAndhra \nPradesh \nVijayawada Metro Project  6,823.00* Not yet \nSanctioned# \nSanction of Metro Rail \nprojects is an ongoing \nprocess which requires \nextensive consultations \nwith all stakeholders. No \ntime limit can be \nspecified for sanction of \nMetro Rail projects. \nTherefore, there is no \npendency.  \nAndhra \nPradesh \nVishakhapatnam Metro Project 12,773.00* Not yet \nSanctioned \nUttar Pradesh Metro Extension from Noida City \nCentre to Sector 62 Noida \n1,807.00* Not yet \nSanctioned \nUttar Pradesh Kalindi Kunj to Botanical Garden, \nNoida \n845.00* Not yet \nSanctioned \nUttar Pradesh Metro Connection between Noida and \nGreater Noida \n5,533.00* Not yet \nSanctioned \nNCT of Delhi Extension of Najafgargh-Dhansa 569.00* Not yet \nSanctioned \nMaharashtra Pune Metro Rail Project Phase-I 11,802.00* Not yet \nSanctioned# \nKerala Kochi Metro Project Phase-IB 1682.00* Not yet \nSanctioned \nChandigarh, \nHaryana, \nPunjab.  \nMetro Rail Project in Greater \nChandigarh Region  \n13,909.00* Not yet \nSanctioned \nKerala Light Metro Rail Project – \nThiruvananthapuram  \n4354.00* Not yet \nSanctioned \nKerala Light"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |673", "t": "Hassle-Free Entry in U.S.", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.673 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n                                     \nHASSLE-FREE ENTRY IN U.S. \n \n†673.  SHRI KAPIL MORESHWAR PATIL:  \n \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether India and U.S. have signed a pact for hassle-free entry \nof Indians at selected airports of the U.S.; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(c) the details of the airports which will facilitate such hassle-free \nentry?  \n  \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n[GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD)] \n \n(a) & (b) A M emorandum of Understanding between Consular, \nPassport and Visa Division, Ministry of External Affairs of India, and \nUS Customs and Border Protection, Department of Homeland \nSecurity of the United States , for the development of an \nInternational Expedited Traveller Initiative (Global Entry \nProgramme) was signed in Washington D.C. on 3 June 2016. \nOperationalization of the MOU will facilitate expedited entry of pre-\napproved, Indian travellers upon arrival in the United States. \n \n(c) According to the  US Customs and Border Protection website, \nGlobal Entry kiosks are located at 59 airports across th e US and in \nother parts of the world. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |674", "t": "ISIS Activity in Neighbouring Countries", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.674 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nISIS ACTIVITY IN NEIGHBOURING COUNTRIES \n \n674.  SHRI K. C. VENUGOPAL: \nSHRI MULLAPPALLY RAMACHANDRAN:  \n \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has taken note of the growing incidents of \nterrorist activities supported by organisations like ISIS in the \nneighbouring countries; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof and the precautionary steps taken/being \ntaken by the Government to ensure the safety and security of Indians \nliving in these areas; \n \n(c)  the details of action taken by the Government to ensure safety of \ndiplomats and institutions in terrorism affected countries; \n \n(d)  whether the Government has raised  the matter with the concerned \nGovernments; and \n \n(e)  if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n(SHRI M.J. AKBAR) \n \n(a) The Government of India is closely and regularly monitoring the \nactivities of terrorist organisations, including ISIS, in the neighbouring \ncountries. \n \n(b) The Government of India is taking all precautionary measures to \nensure the safety and security of Ind ian officials and Indian communities in \nthe neighbouring countries. Whenever necessary, information affecting \nIndia's security interests abroad is duly shared with concerned local \ngovernment authorities. As per standard diplomatic norms and practices, \nalso followed in other countries, the primary responsibility for ensuring the \nsafety and security of Indian officials and institutions in these countries \nvests with the local government. Accordingly, regular channels of \ncommunication are being maintained with the governments of neighbouring \ncountries. \n \n(c) to (e) The Government is also regularly upgrading security \narrangements at our Embassies and Consulates in close consultation and \nliaison with the concerned local government.     \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |675", "t": "Disclosing Call Details of Individuals", "head": " \n  \n \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS \nDEPARTMENT OF TELECOMMUNICATIONS  \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.675  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20 TH  JULY, 2016 \n \nDISCLOSING CALL DETAILS OF INDIVIDUALS \n \n675. SHRI P.C. MOHAN: \n \nWill the Minister of COMMUNICATIONS  be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether complaints have been received regarding the breach of security of \nindividual's cell phone details by private security agencies; \n \n(b)  if so, the details of the cases, State and service provider-wise; \n \n(c)  the action being taken against the service provider for breach of trust; \n \n(d)  whether any agency or agencies have been appointed by the Government for \nmobile phone investigation; and \n \n(e)  if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (IC) OF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS & \n MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n \n(a) to (c)   Madam, Department of Telecommunications has not received any \nformal complaint regarding the breach of Security of individual’s cell phone details by \nprivate security agencies. However , there were media reports  in The Tribune( e-\nnews paper , Delhi edition) over internet with the headlines   ‘ Police bust gang selling \nCDR’ on 11 th  July 2016 which indicated that  a gang of four persons  has been \narrested by Crime Branch of  Delhi Police that used to leak call details records (CDR)  \nto a private detective agency .  \n \n(d) & (e)   As per Media Reports, Crime Branch of Delhi Police has arrested  four \npersons,  along with  a Constable of Uttar Pradesh Police,  in relation with the leakage \nof CDRs and  is investigating the case.  Department of Telecommunications has \nissued the Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) on 2 nd  January, 2014  to Telecom \nService Providers (TSPs) to handle Lawful Interception & Monitoring. In these SOPs it \nhas been inter-alia mandated to facilitate the information  only against the requests \nmade by Nodal officers of Law Enforcement Agencies(LEA) and other investigation \nauthorities of  LEAs/Security Agencies under Section 92 of Criminal Procedure Code \n(Cr. PC) and /or under any other Act having specific provisions. \n \n***************** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |676", "t": "Indo-UK Relation after Brexit", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.676 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nINDO-UK RELATION AFTER BREXIT \n \n676.  SHRI C.N. JAYADEVAN: \n \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether Britain has voted to leave the European Union (EU); \nand \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and its likely impact on Indo -UK \nrelations and our prospects between the European Union \ncountries and UK? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n[GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD)] \n \n(a) & (b) In the referendum held on 23 June 2016, the people of \nthe United Kingdom voted to leave the European Union (51.9% vs. \n48.1%). For the United Kingdom to leave the European Union, it has \nto invoke Article 50 of the Lisbon Treaty . It is up to the Government \nof United Kingdom to decide when to invoke this Article. Such an \ninvocation w ill then set in motion , the process for the United \nKingdom to withdraw from the European Union. The relationship \nbetween the United Kingdom and the European Union is therefore \nyet to evolve and until such time, it is hard to assess the impact of \nBrexit on India-United Kingdom relations. India values its strong and \nmulti-faceted relationship with the United Kingdom and the \nEuropean Union  and is committed to further strengthening these \nties. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |678", "t": "FDI in Railways", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 678 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nFDI IN RAILWAYS \n \n678.     SHRI M.B. RAJESH: \n \n     Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has decided to allow 100 per cent \nForeign Direct Investment (FDI) in Railways;  \n \n(b)  if so, the reasons therefor along with its aims and objectives; \n \n(c) whether the Government has conducted any study of experiences \nof FDI in Railways in other countries and if so, the details and \nfindings thereof;  \n \n(d) whether the Government has taken adequate safeguards to \nensure that interest of employees will be protected in the wake of \nFDI in Railways and if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(e) whether the Government has prepared any roadmap in this regard \nand if so, the details thereof? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) & (b): Yes, Madam. Government in August, 2014 had permitted \n100% Foreign Direct Investment (FDI) in construction, operation and \nmaintenance in certain identified areas in the Rail sectors. \n \n--2/- \n\n-2- \n \nThe objectives of FDI policy are : modernisation and strengthening of \nrail network and development of rail -related industries through \ninfusion of foreign equity and technology leading to growth in \nmanufacturing and enhancing competitiveness. \n \n(c): No, Madam. \n \n(d): Yes, Madam. Areas identified for FDI are not in conflict with \nmanagement and operations of the existing network of Indian \nRailways which continues to be with Government of India. \n \n(e): Ministry of Railways issued Sectoral guidelines in November, \n2014 for Domestic/Foreign Direct Investment (FDI) in rail sector in \ncertain identified areas. \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |679", "t": "Lodha Committee Report", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 679 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nLodha Committee Report \n \n679.   SHRI KALIKESH N. SINGH DEO: \n SHRI RABINDRA KUMAR JENA: \n           \nWill the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government has taken cognizance of Lodha Committee \nreport on the BCCI and if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons \ntherefor; \n  \n(b) whether the Government has taken/plans to undertake steps to ensure \nthe enforcement of the Lodha Committee report and if so, the details \nthereof and if not, the reasons therefor; \n \n(c) whether the Government plans to constitute a similar panel for other \nsporting bodies to bring about accountability and transparency in their \nfunctioning and if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons \ntherefor; \n \n(d) whether the Government has taken any initiative to bring BCCI under \nits control; and \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n   THE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) FOR YOUTH AFFAIRS \nAND SPORTS \n(SHRI VIJAY GOEL) \n \n(a)&(b)  Madam, Board of Control for Cricket of India (BCCI) has informed \nthat the Justice Lodha Committee appointed by the Hon’ble  Supreme Court \nsubmitted its report to the Hon’ble Supreme Court on 4th January, 2016.  The  \n \n\nreport is before the Hon’ble Supreme Court and BCCI is awaiting the final \norder on implementation of the recommendations of the Justice Lodha \nCommittee.   \n \n(c)       In order to ensure that National Sports Federations (NSFs) \nfunction in a democratic manner, Government has framed the National \nSports Development Code of India, 2011 (NSDCI) which is effect ive from \n31/1/2011 to bring in transparency and accountability in the func tioning of \nvarious National Sports Federations (NSFs) for healthy development of sports \nin the country.  NSDCI, inter-alia, contains instructions to adhere to age and \nduration of tenure limits of office bearers , adopt impartial and transparent \nselection procedures, take measures against age fraud in sports, hol d \nregular national championships, include sportspersons in the management of \nNSFs, hold the elections as per Model election guidelines devised by the \nGovernment, etc.  \n \n(d) & (e)     Madam, BCCI is an autonomous body registered under the \nSocieties Registration Act.  Recognition to BCCI has not been g ranted by \nGovernment.  However, since International Cricket Council (ICC) recognizes \nBCCI as the apex National Federation responsible for promotion of cricket in  \nIndia, a team selected by BCCI is considered as the Indian Team.  The \nMinistry only grants permission to BCCI from sports angle for participatio n of \nIndian teams in international events abroad and for holding International \nCricket Matches in India at no Cost to the Govt., subject to clearance of the \nMinistry of External Affairs from political angle and the Ministry of Ho me \nAffairs from security angle.  \n \n*****\n\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |680", "t": "PYKKA Scheme", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 680 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nPYKKA Scheme \n \n680.  SHRI DUSHYANT CHAUTALA: \n SHRI N.K. PREMACHANDRAN: \n  \n Will the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to \nstate:  \n(a) the details about the financial allocation and number of panchayats \nbenefited under Panchayat Yuva Krida Aur Khel Abhiyan (PYKKA) for \ndevelopment of sports in rural areas; \n \n(b) whether  many State Governments have not been granted any \nassistance under this scheme for the development of sports in rural \nareas; and  \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof and the action taken by the Government for \nproper implementation of this scheme in all States? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \nFOR YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS  \n(SHRI VIJAY GOEL) \n \n(a) to (c) The Panchayat Yuva  Krida aur Khel Abhiyan (PYKKA) was \nbeing implemented by the Ministry of Youth Affairs &  Sports from 2008-09 \nto 2013-14 for creation and maintenance of basic sports infrastructure at \nvillage and block panchayat level and holding of annual sports \ncompetitions to encourage mass participation in sports. All State \nGovernments have been granted fi nancial assistance under the PYKKA \nScheme for development of sports in rural areas.  State-wise details of \nfunds released to States under the PYKKA Scheme is given in Annexure – \nI. Year-wise details of financial allocation under the PYKKA Scheme and \ndetails of playfields approved and developed during its currency is given \nin Annexure II.  \n***** \n\nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) to (c) OF THE LOK SABHA UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 680 FOR \n20.07.2016 ASKED BY SHRI DUSHYANT CHAUTALA AND SHRI N.K. PREMACHANDRAN, MPs  REGARDING PYKKA \nSCHEME \nAnnexure – I \nState-wise details 