rship of SCO will provide opportunities for \ncooperation on economic and security matters including counter -\nterrorism. SCO also has potential to enhance connectivity options \nand energy security for India. \n \n(b)  India has diplomatic relations with all the SCO member \ncountries. SCO has regular discussions on wide range of issues. It \nalso organizes joint anti-terrorist exercises and facilitates sharing of \ninformation and best practices on combating terrorism. \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |682", "t": "Executive Lounge", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.682 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nEXECUTIVE LOUNGE \n \n†682. SHRI RAMDAS C. TADAS: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Railways is considering to construct executive \nlounge at major railway stations; and  \n(b)  if so, the time by which such lounges are likely to be constructed \nat Delhi, Nizamuddin and Sewagram and Wardha railway stations \nof Maharashtra? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n (a) & (b): Indian Railway Catering and Tourism Corporation (IRCTC) \nhas been entrusted with the task of setting  up Executive Lounges at \n49 stations. Executive Lounge at New Delhi, Agra Cantt. & Jaipur \nstations have started operation. Executive Lounge at Delhi railway \nstation is targeted for completion by December, 2016. The site for \nExecutive Lounge at Nizamuddin r ailway station is to be finalized. \nExecutive Lounge has not been planned at Sewagram and Wardha \nrailway stations in Maharashtra. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|9|UNSTARRED |683", "t": "Construction of Stadiums", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. †683 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2016 \n \nConstruction of Stadiums \n \n†683. SHRI LAKHAN LAL SAHU: \n SHRIMATI KAMLA DEVI PAATLE: \n  \n Will the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to \nstate:  \n(a) whether the Government has received proposals from various States \nincluding Chhattisgarh for the development and encouragement of sports \nand construction of stadia in their States; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c) the present status of the proposals pending during the last two years? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \nFOR YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS  \n(SHRI VIJAY GOEL) \n \n(a)  Sports is a State subject and, therefore , development and \nencouragement of sports and construction of stadia  is primarily the \nresponsibility of the State Government. The Central Government has been \ncomplementing/supplementing the efforts of the State Governments  for \ncreation of sports infrastructure and conduct of competitions  through \nschemes, namely, Rajiv Gandhi Khel Abhiyan (RGKA) and Urban Sports \nInfrastructure Scheme (USIS) during the last two years.  \n(b) State-wise d etails of funds released under RGKA and USIS during \nthe last two years are given in Annexures I and II.  \n(c) Release of grants under RGKA and USIS were demand-driven and \nmade against  proposals received from States /UTs and other eligible \nentities, and which are complete in all respects as per provisions of the \n\nrespective Scheme and subject furnishing of Utilisation Certificate  in \nrespect of grants released by this Ministry. A new Central Sector Scheme \ncalled “Khelo India – National Programme for Development of Sports ” has \nbeen launched in place of erstwhile RGKA  and USIS, for implementation \nduring 2016-17. All the States and other eligible entities have been asked \nto furnish project proposals in accordance with the guidelines of the new \nScheme.  \n****** \n  \n\nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO P ART (b) OF THE LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. †683 FOR 