nancial assistance has been given to \nStates/UTs by the Government;  \n (b) the funds allocated and spent for each scheme, State/UT-wise;  \n (c) the criteria adopted to sanction financial assistance to each State/UT in this regard; \n(d) the proposal of State Government of Maharashtra pending for the last three years; and \n(e) the time by which clearances are likely to be given to the proposed schemes?        \n \n ANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) FOR MINISTRY OF PLANNING AND \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR MINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT & \n MINISTRY OF HOUSING &URBAN POVERTY ALLEVIATION \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n \n(a) & (b): The Social Sector Schemes are implemented by various Ministries viz. Food & Public \nDistribution, Health & Family Welfare, Human Resource Development, Labour & Employment, \nMinority Affairs, Rural Development, Social Justice &  Empowerment, Housing and Urban \nPoverty Alleviation, Tribal Affairs, Urban Development , Drinking Water & Sanitation  and \nWomen & Child Development. Among these schemes, there are 12 major schemes having larger \noutlays. The scheme-wise details of the major S ocial Sector Schemes, along with funds released \nto the States/UTs during 2013-14 to 2015-16 are given in the Annexure. \n(c): The Social Sector Schemes are implemented by the States/Administrative \nMinistries/Departments concerned as per the guidelines of the  individual schemes, prepared in \nconsultation with the States/UTs, which also includes  the criteria adopted to sanction financial \nassistance to States/UTs.  \n(d) & (e): No proposal/project  during last three years from the State of Maharashtra is pending \nwith NITI Aayog.  \n****** \n\n                                                                                                       ANNEXURE \nAnnexure to the Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No. 974.  to be answered on 22.07.2017 on Social Sector \nSchemes raised by \n SHRI GODSE HEMANT TUKARAM \nState- wise Releases during 2013-14,